\par }{\fs20\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof {\shp{\*\shpinst\shpleft1440\shptop2070\shpright10800\shpbottom2070\shpfhdr1\shpbxpage\shpbxignore\shpbypage\shpbyignore\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt0\shpz2\shplockanchor\shplid2049{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn fFlipH}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fFlipV}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn shapePath}{\sv 4}}{\sp{\sn fFillOK}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fFilled}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fArrowheadsOK}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn posrelh}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn posrelv}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn fLayoutInCell}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn fLayoutInCell}{\sv 1}}}{\shprslt{\*\do\dobxpage\dobypage\dodhgt8194\dpline\dpptx0\dppty0\dpptx9920\dppty0\dpx1190\dpy2070\dpxsize9920\dpysize0\dplinew15\dplinecor0\dplinecog0\dplinecob0}}}}{\f0\fs16  \par }}{\footerf \pard\plain \s22\ql \b\f354\fs18  Page {\field{\*\fldinst PAGE}{\fldrslt 1}}{     }\'a9 2026 \uc2 Factiva, Inc.  All rights reserved.\par }{\footer \pard\plain \s22\ql \b\f354\fs18  Page {\field{\*\fldinst PAGE}{\fldrslt 1}} of {\field{\*\fldinst NUMPAGES}{\fldrslt 1}}{     }\'a9 2026 \uc2 Factiva, Inc.  All rights reserved.\par }\pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\fs20 {\par\fs20\b \uc2 AMERICA STRONG NEVER STOP MOVING\b0\par\par\uc2 383 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Saturday\par \uc2 WNSA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MULROY, LEAK, BLINKEN, TEIXEIRA, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, HOUSE, BIDEN, PROTESTS, SMITH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NATIONWIDE PROTESTS OVER ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, DOTSON, HEBBE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WRONG HOME FATAL POLICE SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, STORM, TRACK, FORECAST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 26 MILLION ON ALERT\par \par \uc2 GERSHKOVICH, RUSSIA, ESPIONAGE, MILMAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PARENTS OF DETAINED JOURNALIST SPEAK OUT\par \par \uc2 JAPAN, EXPLOSION, KISHIDA, KIMURA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXPLOSIVE ATTACK ON JAPAN PM\par \par \uc2 SUDAN, MILITARY COUP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY CLASHES IN SUDAN\par \par \uc2 RESCUE, CHILDREN, O'BRIEN, GROSS, MEXICO\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MISSING CHILDREN RESCUED\par \par \uc2 BOSTON MARATHON, ANNIVERSARY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE INDEX\par \par \uc2 MINOR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: #AMERICASTRONG\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Finally, tonight, "America Strong," one man's secret to living a good life, never stop moving.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Lee Minor has been running around this track in Liberty, Missouri since 1969. You'll see him here year-round, at least three times a week.\par \par \uc2 LEE MINOR (RUNNER)\par \par \uc2 I like to run in all kinds of weather, and I love to come here after a snow and you just watch your footprints as you go along.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Lee also competes in races. And recently, on his 85th birthday, he celebrated his 600th race.\par \par \uc2 LEE MINOR (RUNNER)\par \par \uc2 My legacy will probably be how slow I am. The last race, I came in second out of five in the 80 and over, but I can't compete with those young whippersnappers anymore.\par \par \uc2 SUPPORTER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Come on, Lee.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) For Lee, running is also family time. Here he is after finishing a 5K with loved ones, including some of his great grandkids. With his son Mike at the Super Heroes Race on Father's Day. His youngest granddaughters at a Color Run, crossing the finish line at a Santa Run and blowing a kiss to his wife Judy during the Kansas City Zoo Run. His motivation?\par \par \uc2 LEE MINOR (RUNNER)\par \par \uc2 I do it a lot for health.\par \par \uc2 LEE MINOR (RUNNER)\par \par \uc2 What a beautiful day.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) An octogenarian grateful for every step.\par \par \uc2 LEE MINOR (RUNNER)\par \par \uc2 I love this life, and I want to live as long as I can, and I mean live.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And inspiring so many along the way. Thanks so much for watching tonight. I'm Whit Johnson in New York. Good night.\par \par \uc2 Document WNSA000020230417ej4f0000b\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 THE INDEX\b0\par\par\uc2 206 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Saturday\par \uc2 WNSA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MULROY, LEAK, BLINKEN, TEIXEIRA, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, HOUSE, BIDEN, PROTESTS, SMITH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NATIONWIDE PROTESTS OVER ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, DOTSON, HEBBE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WRONG HOME FATAL POLICE SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, STORM, TRACK, FORECAST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 26 MILLION ON ALERT\par \par \uc2 GERSHKOVICH, RUSSIA, ESPIONAGE, MILMAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PARENTS OF DETAINED JOURNALIST SPEAK OUT\par \par \uc2 JAPAN, EXPLOSION, KISHIDA, KIMURA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXPLOSIVE ATTACK ON JAPAN PM\par \par \uc2 SUDAN, MILITARY COUP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY CLASHES IN SUDAN\par \par \uc2 RESCUE, CHILDREN, O'BRIEN, GROSS, MEXICO\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MISSING CHILDREN RESCUED\par \par \uc2 BOSTON MARATHON, ANNIVERSARY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE INDEX\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) To "The Index" now. Somber ceremonies today mark the tenth anniversary of the deadly Boston Marathon bombing.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) A bagpiper led a procession to the memorial sites near the marathon's finish line, where two bombs detonated, killing three people and injuring more than 260 others. Security will be tight for this year's race to be held on Monday, though the \uc2 FBI\uc2  says it's not aware of any specific threats.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) When we come back, "America Strong."\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WORLD NEWS TONIGHT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COMING UP\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) He's been running for more than a half a century and has no plans to stop.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document WNSA000020230417ej4f0000a\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 NATIONWIDE PROTESTS OVER ABORTION PILL SUPREME COURT TEMPORARILY PAUSES DRUG RESTRICTIONS\b0\par\par\uc2 623 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Saturday\par \uc2 WNSA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MULROY, LEAK, BLINKEN, TEIXEIRA, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, HOUSE, BIDEN, PROTESTS, SMITH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NATIONWIDE PROTESTS OVER ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to the nationwide protests over the abortion pill.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Abortion rights supporters demonstrating outside of the Supreme Court today. This, just hours after Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  issued a stay of a lower court ruling that would have restricted use of the drug, mifepristone, which is used in the majority of abortions in this country.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The justices specter to weigh in next week. ABC's Elizabeth Schulze is at the Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 ACTIVIST (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Are we going to back down?\par \par \uc2 ACTIVISTS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 No.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT TEMPORARILY PAUSES DRUG RESTRICTIONS\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, protests across the country with the battle over access to the abortion pill now in the hands of the Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 ACTIVIST (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Abortion pills are murder.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  issuing a stay late Friday that keeps mifepristone available until the end of the day Wednesday, as the nation's highest court considers a Texas judge's legal ruling that could ultimately suspend FDA approval of the pill used in more than half of US abortions. Overnight, President Biden blasting the Texas decision.\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT JOE BIDEN (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 I think it's outrageous but the court has done relative (inaudible) concluding that they're going to overrule the FDA in whether the is safe or not. I think it's out of their domain.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Less than a year after the Supreme Court overturned Roe v. Wade, anti-abortion activists say they are hopeful.\par \par \uc2 ACTIVIST (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 We certainly see it as encouraging.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The debate deeply personal for 32-year-old Brittany House, who joined hundreds of abortion-rights activists today at the Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 BRITTANY HOUSE (PROTESTER)\par \par \uc2 I'm just happy overall. I was able to have my abortion in the way that I wanted and in the way that I needed.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) She tells us, she had a medical abortion using mifepristone.\par \par \uc2 BRITTANY HOUSE (PROTESTER)\par \par \uc2 I'm standing before you today, 11 years later, safe, healthy, financially stable.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BANNED OR SEVERELY LIMITED ABORTION\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Fourteen states have mostly banned the abortion pill. It would be banned in every state if the Supreme Court signed with the Texas Supreme Court ruling and suspends FDA approval.\par \par \uc2 ACTIVISTS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Abortion is murder.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Anti-abortion advocates hoping that ruling holds.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What was your reaction to the original decision from the Texas judge?\par \par \uc2 CAROLINE TAYLOR SMITH (PROTESTER)\par \par \uc2 My first reaction was a lot of excitement. We've been waiting for the decision, everybody had been, for all the really long time.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Some states aren't waiting for the Supreme Court. Maryland now joining a growing number of states for Democratic governors stockpiling it.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Elizabeth Schulze with us now at the Supreme Court. So, walk us through the legal process here and how it's expected to play out in the next four days.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Whit, it will be status quo until the Supreme Court weighs in, which is expected to happen sometime before midnight Wednesday night. So, for the next four days, the justices will consider the government's request for a full stay, as well as abortion opponents' arguments that these restrictions should immediately take effect. Whit?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And so much at stake. Elizabeth, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document WNSA000020230417ej4f00003\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 26 MILLION ON ALERT SEVERAL POCKETS OF SEVERE WEATHER IN THE NORTHEAST\b0\par\par\uc2 275 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Saturday\par \uc2 WNSA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MULROY, LEAK, BLINKEN, TEIXEIRA, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, HOUSE, BIDEN, PROTESTS, SMITH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NATIONWIDE PROTESTS OVER ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, DOTSON, HEBBE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WRONG HOME FATAL POLICE SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, STORM, TRACK, FORECAST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 26 MILLION ON ALERT\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Tonight, more than 26 million Americans are on alert for the threat of severe weather from Texas to Illinois. Places like Houston, New Orleans, and St. Louis all in the danger zone. Let's get right to ABC's senior meteorologist Rob Marciano. And, Rob, what can we expect tonight?\par \par \uc2 ROB MARCIANO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Whit, we've got several pockets of severe weather, one pretty close to the northeast here in parts of New Jersey, eastern Pennsylvania. Heavy rain. This is the same system that brought heavy rain to Florida.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SPRING STORMS\par \par \uc2 ROB MARCIANO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But along the Delaware River, we've had some flash flooding from Allentown down to Philadelphia.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DANGEROUS WEATHER\par \par \uc2 ROB MARCIANO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The other pockets across I-10 and through the Florida panhandle, then larger scale from Shreveport to Little Rock. We've got rough weather move through parts of Missouri and St. Louis, even a threat for a tornado watch.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FUTURECAST\par \par \uc2 ROB MARCIANO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This lull will intensify as it moves over Chicago tonight. It will wrap around some snow, one to five inches in spots. It will also get those winds cranking through tomorrow afternoon and evening. This is a pretty potent system for mid-April. Whit?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Rob, thanks.\par \par \uc2 Document WNSA000020230417ej4f00005\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 DOJ LOOKS TO SUPREME COURT IN ABORTION PILL BATTLE WILL ASK FOR "EMERGENCY RELIEF" TO PUT RULING ON HOLD\b0\par\par\uc2 577 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CAPTURED\par \par \uc2 ARREST, DOCUMENTS, TEIXEIRA, GARLAND, \uc2 FBI\uc2 , SWAT, RYDER\par \par \uc2 DOCUMENTS, DOJ, ARREST, MOTIVE, TEIXEIRA\par \par \uc2 DOCUMENTS, LEAK, PENTAGON, SECURITY, BIDEN, IRELAND\par \par \uc2 FLOODING, RAIN, TRAPPED, SUBMERGED, TRANATLIS, RESCUES\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, DOJ, MIFEPRISTONE, \uc2 FDA\uc2 , SUPREME COURT, FLORIDA\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, Victor, thanks very much. Now to the abortion pill battle. The Justice Department is set to ask the Supreme Court to intervene. Rachel Scott is live at the court with the latest. Good morning, Rachel.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOJ LOOKS TO SUPREME COURT IN ABORTION PILL BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WILL ASK FOR "EMERGENCY RELIEF" TO PUT TX JUDGE'S RULING ON HOLD\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) George, good morning. And what happens in the next 24 hours will determine if access to abortion changes for women in this country for the second time in nearly a year. The Justice Department taking the battle over the abortion pill all the way to the Supreme Court, asking the justices intervene great. In a statement, the Attorney General asking the high court "To defend the \uc2 FDA\uc2 's scientific judgment and protect American access to safe and effective reproductive care."\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) At the center of all this, access to the abortion drug, Mifepristone, that was approved by the \uc2 FDA\uc2  more than 20 years ago. It's used in more than half of abortions in the United States. After conflicting federal rulings over whether or not to ban the drug, a federal appeals panel stepped in saying the drug can stay available for now but imposing new restrictions, including limiting the use of the drug, up to seven weeks into a woman's pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION PILL BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: APPEALS COURT REINSTATES APPROVAL OF DRUG, ALLOWS OTHER PARTS OF RULING\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And also no longer allowing the dug to be available by mail even in states where abortion is legal, instead requiring a woman to make three in person visits with her doctor in order to obtain the pill. As for what happens next, in the coming hours we are expecting the Justice Department to file an emergency appeal. But if the Supreme Court does not weigh in, those new restrictions are set to go into effect in less than 24 hours tomorrow morning, George.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) In the meantime, Rachel, Florida has passed one of the strictest abortion bans in the country.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLORIDA PASSES SIX WEEK ABORTION BAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOV DESANTIS SIGNS BILL INTO LAW OVERNIGHT\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes. And Florida Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  wasted no time signing it. This is a bill to ban abortion at six weeks into a woman's pregnancy, that's before most women even know that they are pregnant. Of course this would have significant implications on access to abortions in the south.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) 14 states have stopped nearly all abortion services. I just got back from Florida. Clinics there, they were seeing a surge in out-of-state patients traveling to Florida for abortion care. And, of course, politically speaking here we know that Florida Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  is expected to run for president in 2024. He's leaning into these abortion restrictions that Democrats used to help mobilize their voters in the midterm elections. George.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Rachel Scott, thanks. Michael.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230518ej4e0002y\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 THE INDEX\b0\par\par\uc2 185 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TEIXEIRA, GARLAND, LEAK, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS, SPYING\par \par \uc2 TEIXEIRA, LEAK, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INTELLIGENCE COMMUNITY SHOCK WAVES\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, SCHIFELING, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEMPORARY STAY IN ABORTION PILL BATTLE\par \par \uc2 STORM, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STATE OF EMERGENCY\par \par \uc2 LEE, STABBING, MOMENI\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOCUMENTS: VIDEO CAPTURES MOGUL'S MURDER\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, PENCE, NOEM, NRA CONVENTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP AND PENCE ADDRESS NRA\par \par \uc2 PROTESTS, RETIREMENT AGE, FRANCE, MACRON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SHOWDOWN OVER REFORM\par \par \uc2 BAN, TIKTOK, MONTANA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STATEWIDE BAN\par \par \uc2 BEAR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE INDEX\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) To "The Index" now. A startling face to face encounter in Asheville, North Carolina.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Home security camera showing the moment a man relaxing in his carport is jolted by a black bear sneaking up behind him. Take a look. The bear appearing to be just as scared as he was. Both locking eyes for a moment before the bear turned and ran. The man handled it better than I would, that's for sure.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) When we come back, the curtain about to come down for the last time on Broadway's longest-running show.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020230417ej4e0000a\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 PHANTOM'S FINAL BOW "PHANTOM OF THE OPERA" TAKES A FINAL BOW AFTER 13,981 PERFORMANCES\b0\par\par\uc2 379 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TEIXEIRA, GARLAND, LEAK, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS, SPYING\par \par \uc2 TEIXEIRA, LEAK, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INTELLIGENCE COMMUNITY SHOCK WAVES\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, SCHIFELING, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEMPORARY STAY IN ABORTION PILL BATTLE\par \par \uc2 STORM, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STATE OF EMERGENCY\par \par \uc2 LEE, STABBING, MOMENI\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOCUMENTS: VIDEO CAPTURES MOGUL'S MURDER\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, PENCE, NOEM, NRA CONVENTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP AND PENCE ADDRESS NRA\par \par \uc2 PROTESTS, RETIREMENT AGE, FRANCE, MACRON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SHOWDOWN OVER REFORM\par \par \uc2 BAN, TIKTOK, MONTANA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STATEWIDE BAN\par \par \uc2 BEAR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE INDEX\par \par \uc2 "PHANTOM OF THE OPERA", RUBIN, LAMPEL\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Finally, tonight, after a record-breaking run, the "Phantom's" final bow.\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM BROADWAY SHOW, "THE PHANTOM OF THE OPERA"\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It's the end of an era on Broadway. "Phantom of the Opera" completing its historic 35-year run. The iconic \uc2 Andrew Lloyd Webber\uc2  production tells the story of a mysterious masked man lurking in the catacombs of the Paris opera house. Since its Broadway debut in 1988, the musical at the majestic theater has been seen by nearly 20 million people, grossing more than a billion dollars. But "Phantom" wasn't able to rebound after taking a major hit during the pandemic. The last performance of the longest production on Broadway ever will be on Sunday. Today, fans eager to catch its final bow.\par \par \uc2 THEATERGOER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 I saw this a long time ago when I was a kid.\par \par \uc2 THEATERGOER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 My parents got engaged the night they saw it here. And then I have been obsessed with it since I was 5.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And many of the thousands who work behind the scenes grateful and still moved by the "Music of the Night."\par \par \uc2 TARA RUBIN (CASTING DIRECTOR)\par \par \uc2 The music is so lush and so beautiful and so romantic. People never tire of hearing it.\par \par \uc2 ALAN LAMPEL (HEAD ELECTRICIAN)\par \par \uc2 The generations that have come to see the show, the excitement that I see every night on people's faces.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) My daughters absolutely love that show. It will be missed. Thanks so much for watching tonight. I'm Whit Johnson in New York. Hope to see you right back here tomorrow night. Have a good night.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020230417ej4e0000b\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 SHOWDOWN OVER REFORM TOP FRENCH COURT: RETIREMENT AGE CAN RISE TO 64\b0\par\par\uc2 421 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TEIXEIRA, GARLAND, LEAK, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS, SPYING\par \par \uc2 TEIXEIRA, LEAK, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INTELLIGENCE COMMUNITY SHOCK WAVES\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, SCHIFELING, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEMPORARY STAY IN ABORTION PILL BATTLE\par \par \uc2 STORM, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STATE OF EMERGENCY\par \par \uc2 LEE, STABBING, MOMENI\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOCUMENTS: VIDEO CAPTURES MOGUL'S MURDER\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, PENCE, NOEM, NRA CONVENTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP AND PENCE ADDRESS NRA\par \par \uc2 PROTESTS, RETIREMENT AGE, FRANCE, MACRON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SHOWDOWN OVER REFORM\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Overseas, tonight, a victory for French President \uc2 Emmanuel Macron\uc2 . His plan to raise the retirement age to 64 getting the final nod despite months of nationwide mass protest. And tonight, after the ruling, protesters are back on the streets, more than 100 people arrested. ABC's Tom Soufi Burridge is in Paris. Tom, good evening.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TOP FRENCH COURT: RETIREMENT AGE CAN RISE TO 64\par \par \uc2 TOM SOUFI BURRIDGE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, Whit, as you can see, there's that heavy police presence on the streets of Paris tonight. Police officers trying to quell pockets of protests.\par \par \uc2 TOM SOUFI BURRIDGE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Earlier demonstrators clashing with riot police, setting fire to bins and bicycles. The government's unpopular law to raise the minimum retirement age here from 62 to 64 without the democratic vote has been approved by France's constitutional council after months of protests. President \uc2 Emmanuel Macron\uc2  saying, people are living longer, so this reform is needed to balance the books. But the union's rejecting a meeting with Macron next week and promising more strikes.\par \par \uc2 TOM SOUFI BURRIDGE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Tonight, protesters telling us they'll hit the streets again tomorrow. Whit?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Tom, thank you.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOJ INDICTMENTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MEXICO DRUG CARTEL LEADERS CHARGED\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Next here, the Justice Department announcing a sweeping crackdown on Mexico's Sinaloa cartel and its global network, accusing them of fueling America's fentanyl crisis.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Attorney General \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  charging 28 people, including three sons of notorious drug lord El Chapo, who is serving a life sentence here in the US. Chemical suppliers in China also being charged. Eight of the accused are in custody. The US offering rewards for several others.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) When we come back, the state becoming the first in the nation to pass a bill banning TikTok on all personal devices. And after 35 years, the final curtain call for one of Broadway's most iconic shows.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020230417ej4e00008\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 STATEWIDE BAN MONTANA BANS TIKTOK ON ALL PERSONAL DEVICES\b0\par\par\uc2 191 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TEIXEIRA, GARLAND, LEAK, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS, SPYING\par \par \uc2 TEIXEIRA, LEAK, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INTELLIGENCE COMMUNITY SHOCK WAVES\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, SCHIFELING, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEMPORARY STAY IN ABORTION PILL BATTLE\par \par \uc2 STORM, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STATE OF EMERGENCY\par \par \uc2 LEE, STABBING, MOMENI\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOCUMENTS: VIDEO CAPTURES MOGUL'S MURDER\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, PENCE, NOEM, NRA CONVENTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP AND PENCE ADDRESS NRA\par \par \uc2 PROTESTS, RETIREMENT AGE, FRANCE, MACRON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SHOWDOWN OVER REFORM\par \par \uc2 BAN, TIKTOK, MONTANA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STATEWIDE BAN\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Next, tonight, Montana late today becoming the first state in the US to pass a bill banning TikTok on all personal devices.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The bill prohibits the popular social media app from operating within the state. If signed by the governor, it would take effect in January. TikTok has suggested it will take legal action. The Biden administration has threatened a nationwide ban, demanding TikTok's Chinese owners sell the company because of concerns China could access users' personal data.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) When we come back, a frightening moment. A man at home coming face-to-face with a bear.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020230417ej4e00009\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 STATE OF EMERGENCY 1,000+ CALLS FOR HELP, RESIDENTS STRUGGLE AFTER RECORD STORM\b0\par\par\uc2 412 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TEIXEIRA, GARLAND, LEAK, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS, SPYING\par \par \uc2 TEIXEIRA, LEAK, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INTELLIGENCE COMMUNITY SHOCK WAVES\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, SCHIFELING, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEMPORARY STAY IN ABORTION PILL BATTLE\par \par \uc2 STORM, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STATE OF EMERGENCY\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, to the state of emergency in Broward County, Florida. Fort Lauderdale getting more than two feet of rain in less than 24 hours.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) A torrent of water in a parking garage you see there. The mayor saying there's not one area of the city that hasn't been impacted.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The cleanup will take days as the water recedes. ABC's Victor Oquendo is there.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 1,000+ CALLS FOR HELP, RESIDENTS STRUGGLE AFTER RECORD STORM\par \par \uc2 VICTOR OQUENDO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, families in south Florida cleaning up after more than two feet of rain fell in Fort Lauderdale in less than 24 hours. That's more than a third of what the city gets in a typical year.\par \par \uc2 VICTOR OQUENDO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) This is how you have to get to work now.\par \par \uc2 VICTOR OQUENDO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) We met Elmie Maria (PH) making her way through floodwaters on her way to work.\par \par \uc2 VICTOR OQUENDO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What's it like seeing your neighborhood like this?\par \par \uc2 RESIDENT (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 It's bad, like, knowing lots of people lost lots of property.\par \par \uc2 VICTOR OQUENDO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Water ruining much of what was inside Sylvia Coziel's (PH) home of 35 years.\par \par \uc2 RESIDENT (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 We have no beds, no furniture, nothing to put back in the house. Even our appliances are gone.\par \par \uc2 VICTOR OQUENDO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) South of here, in Hallandale Beach, tow truck drivers working nonstop.\par \par \uc2 TOW TRUCK DRIVER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 We've been out here all night just clearing up some of the roads and just kind of moving some of the cars to the side and stuff like that.\par \par \uc2 VICTOR OQUENDO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And flights resuming at Fort Lauderdale Hollywood International Airport, the storm shutting it down for more than a day.\par \par \uc2 VICTOR OQUENDO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And there is a chance for more showers this evening. It's actually sprinkling a little bit now. But drier weather is on the way, giving residents here that much needed break. Whit?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) They're certainly looking forward to that. Victor, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020230417ej4e00005\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 DOCUMENTS: VIDEO CAPTURES MOGUL'S MURDER SUSPECT ALLEGEDLY DROVE VICTIM TO SECLUDED AREA, STABBED HIM\b0\par\par\uc2 455 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TEIXEIRA, GARLAND, LEAK, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS, SPYING\par \par \uc2 TEIXEIRA, LEAK, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INTELLIGENCE COMMUNITY SHOCK WAVES\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, SCHIFELING, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEMPORARY STAY IN ABORTION PILL BATTLE\par \par \uc2 STORM, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STATE OF EMERGENCY\par \par \uc2 LEE, STABBING, MOMENI\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOCUMENTS: VIDEO CAPTURES MOGUL'S MURDER\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Next, tonight, the suspect in the stabbing death of tech CEO Bob Lee in San Francisco appearing before a judge for the first time. Court documents claiming the suspect confronted Lee about his sister. Hours later, stabbing him three times in a planned and deliberate attack. The video and text messages, they say, support their case. ABC's DeMarco Morgan is in San Francisco.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUSPECT ALLEGEDLY DROVE VICTIM TO SECLUDED AREA, STABBED HIM\par \par \uc2 DEMARCO MORGAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, Nima Momeni, the man police say stabbed tech executive Bob Lee to death, making his first court appearance as prosecutors accused him of a planned and deliberate attack. Outside the courtroom, the suspect's sister now at the center of the case. Court documents allege Bob Lee knew Nima Momeni's sister who lived in the Luxury Millennium Tower apartment building. They say Lee, the sister and a friend spent the afternoon drinking hours before Lee's death and that Momeni later confronted Lee asking if his sister had been doing drugs or anything inappropriate. Lee reassuring him nothing inappropriate had happened.\par \par \uc2 DEMARCO MORGAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Police say, later that night, Lee joined Momeni and his sister at the Millennium Tower and that cameras would show the two men driving off in Momeni's \uc2 BMW\uc2  around 2:00 AM to a dark secluded area. Minutes later, Lee is seen walking away and injured. Prosecutors say he was stabbed three times, one penetrating his heart. A four-inch kitchen knife was later recovered with blood on it.\par \par \uc2 DISPATCHER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Location is 365 Main crossing of Folsom & Harrison. There's been a stabbing.\par \par \uc2 DEMARCO MORGAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Police piecing together Lee's the final moments with surveillance images like these obtained by "The Daily Mail" as he collapsed outside an apartment building. Prosecutors say Nima Momeni fled the scene and left the victim to die. Momeni's sister allegedly sent a text message to Lee that night asking if Lee was doing okay, "Just wanted to make sure you are doing okay because I know Nima came way down hard on you. And thank you for being such a classy man, handling it with class."\par \par \uc2 DEMARCO MORGAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Whit, the suspect's arraignment has been postponed until the end of the month. Whit?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) DeMarco Morgan, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020230417ej4e00006\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 TRUMP, PENCE ADDRESS NRA GOP HOPEFULS AT CONVENTION IN WAKE OF MASS SHOOTINGS\b0\par\par\uc2 507 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TEIXEIRA, GARLAND, LEAK, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS, SPYING\par \par \uc2 TEIXEIRA, LEAK, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INTELLIGENCE COMMUNITY SHOCK WAVES\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, SCHIFELING, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEMPORARY STAY IN ABORTION PILL BATTLE\par \par \uc2 STORM, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STATE OF EMERGENCY\par \par \uc2 LEE, STABBING, MOMENI\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOCUMENTS: VIDEO CAPTURES MOGUL'S MURDER\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, PENCE, NOEM, \uc2 NRA\uc2  CONVENTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP AND PENCE ADDRESS \uc2 NRA\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Next tonight, former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his former vice president and potential rival \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  appearing at the same event for the first time since they left office, both addressing the \uc2 NRA\uc2  convention in Indianapolis in the wake of two deadly mass shootings. Here's ABC's chief Washington correspondent \uc2 Jon Karl\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP, PENCE ADDRESS \uc2 NRA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOP HOPEFULS AT CONVENTION IN WAKE OF MASS SHOOTINGS\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Appearing at the Annual Convention of the \uc2 National Rifle Association\uc2  today, some of the nation's top Republicans made it clear they would oppose any tightening of America's gun laws in the wake of recent mass shootings.\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 With me at 1600 Pennsylvania Avenue, no one will lay a finger on your firearms.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Former President Trump did mention the recent shooting at the Covenant School in Nashville, calling it monstrous. He also called the shooter who killed five in Louisville earlier this week evil and disturbed. Shortly before Trump spoke, former Vice President Pence took the stage.\par \par \uc2 FORMER VICE PRESIDENT MIKE PENCE (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 Hello, \uc2 NRA\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) He faced scattered boos from those who apparently didn't like his recent remarks, critical of Trump's behavior on January 6th. Pence also addressed the recent shootings calling them unspeakable acts and he called for measures to deal with mental health and school security. But he too ruled out any new gun laws.\par \par \uc2 FORMER VICE PRESIDENT MIKE PENCE (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 We don't need gun control. We need crime control. We don't need lectures about the liberties of law-abiding citizens.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Republican South Dakota Governor \uc2 Kristi Noem\uc2  told the crowd her granddaughter, who is not yet 2 years old, already has her own guns.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR KRISTI NOEM (REP) (SOUTH DAKOTA)\par \par \uc2 I want to reassure you, she already has a shotgun and she already has a rifle. And she's got a little pony name Sparkles, too, so the girl is set up.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And an indication of just how much sway the \uc2 National Rifle Association\uc2  still has over Republicans, just about every declared or potential 2024 Republican presidential candidate was there either in person or remote via satellite. That includes not just Pence and Trump, but also DeSantis, \uc2 Chris Sununu\uc2 , Nikki Haley, Tim Scott, \uc2 Asa Hutchinson\uc2 , just about everybody thinking about running for president felt they need to be there today in Indianapolis, Whit.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And that race just barely getting started. \uc2 Jon Karl\uc2 , thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020230417ej4e00007\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 TEMPORARY STAY IN ABORTION PILL BATTLE SUPREME COURT EXTENDS ACCESS TO PILL WHILE IT CONSIDERS CASE\b0\par\par\uc2 446 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TEIXEIRA, GARLAND, LEAK, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS, SPYING\par \par \uc2 TEIXEIRA, LEAK, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INTELLIGENCE COMMUNITY SHOCK WAVES\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, SCHIFELING, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEMPORARY STAY IN ABORTION PILL BATTLE\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Next here, fast-moving developments in the battle over the abortion pill. Late today, the Supreme Court keeping federal rules in place temporarily while it considers lower court rulings that have restricted its use or banned it out right. This avoids a dramatic rollback that was set to kick in at midnight tonight. Here's ABC's Rachel Scott.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT EXTENDS ACCESS TO PILL WHILE IT CONSIDERS CASE\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, the Supreme Court allowing the abortion pill mifepristone stay widely available for now, putting on hold the several major restrictions that were set to go into effect in just a matter of hours. Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  issuing a five-day administrative stay, keeping the status quo for the pill used in more than half of abortions in the US while the justices take more time to fully consider the court challenge.\par \par \uc2 DEIRDRE SCHIFELING (NATIONAL POLITICAL DIRECTOR ACLU)\par \par \uc2 We hope that the Supreme Court throws this case out. It is meritless, and it's undermining the FDA's authority.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It comes after a week of chaos and confusion as federal judges issued conflicting rulings over access to the abortion drug. The Biden administration asked the Supreme Court to intervene, to block restrictions that would have gone into effect tomorrow, preventing women from accessing the drug after seven weeks of pregnancy, requiring three in-person doctor visits and making it unavailable by mail. As of now, mifepristone can still be administered up to 10 weeks of pregnancy and remains available via telehealth and by mail for at least five more days.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  only putting it on hold until late Wednesday, which means we could learn as early as next week whether the Supreme Court decides to take up this case, Whit.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Rachel Scott at the Supreme Court. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WILDFIRES BURNING OUTSIDE NEW YORK CITY\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Next, tonight, multiple wildfires burning outside New York City.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) A large fire threatening homes in Rockland County. Volunteer firefighters and residents trying to beat back the flames. More than 100 homes were evacuated, several houses damaged, at least one firefighter injured. Authorities believe a passing freight train may have sparked the flames, then fueled by that record heat, wind and dry conditions.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020230417ej4e00004\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 APPEALS COURT PARTIALLY BLOCKS ABORTION PILL RULING COURT PRESERVES ACCESS TO DRUG, BUT TIGHTENS RESTRICTIONS\b0\par\par\uc2 371 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 LEAK, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS, HARRIS\par \par \uc2 LEAK, BIDEN, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPORT: CLASSIFIED DOCUMENT LEAKER WORKED ON MILITARY BASE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHITE HOUSE RESPONDS AS PRESIDENT BIDEN VISITS IRELAND\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, RULING, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're going to turn now to new breaking news overnight in the abortion pills battle.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: APPEALS COURT PARTIALLY BLOCKS ABORTION PILL RULING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COURT PRESERVES ACCESS TO DRUG, BUT TIGHTENS RESTRICTIONS\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) An appeals court partially blocked a ruling in order to protect access to the drug, but tightened restrictions. Our senior congressional correspondent Rachel Scott is here the latest on that as the case gets closer to the Supreme Court doesn't it, Rachel? Good morning.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning to you, Robin. Yes, that's exactly right. Let's start with the big picture.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TIGHTER RULES ON MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The pill used in more than half of abortions in the United States does remain legal and available for now. But there are several new limitations. A federal appeals court stepping in overnight to impose tighter rules. This would limit the use of the abortion drug mifepristone allowing it to be used up to seven weeks of pregnancy instead of 10 weeks and deciding that mifepristone can no longer be sent in the mail. Now, this appeals court weighing in after conflicting rulings from federal judges about whether the abortion drug should be banned. But Democratic-led states not waiting for that to come down, wasting no time taking matters into their own hands to stockpile the abortion drug.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION PILL BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW IMAGES OF FIRST STATE STOCKPILE OF MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Washington state, for instance, bought enough for a three-year supply in that state. This morning, the Biden administration reacting to this ruling, saying that they will continue to fight this in the courts. We could see this make its way all the way up to the Supreme Court nearly one year after the Supreme Court overturned Roe vs. Wade, George\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Rachel Scott, thanks.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230518ej4d00004\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ABORTION PILL APPEAL TO SUPREME COURT APPEALS COURT: PILL REMAINS AVAILABLE WITH RESTRICTIONS\b0\par\par\uc2 541 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TEIXEIRA, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS, GARLAND, ARREST, LEAK\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, LEAK, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FALLOUT FROM LEAK ARREST\par \par \uc2 FLOODING, STORM, TRANTALIS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HISTORIC STORM EMERGENCY\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM, HEAT\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, GRANT, GRALL, PRABHAKARAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION PILL APPEAL TO SUPREME COURT\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Several developments tonight in the battle over the abortion pill. Overnight, an appeals court saying the medicine can still remain on the market, but with strict limits, making it much more difficult for women to actually use. And now, the Justice Department is pushing back, appealing directly to the Supreme Court. Here's ABC's Rachel Scott.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: APPEALS COURT: PILL REMAINS AVAILABLE WITH RESTRICTIONS\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, the Justice Department taking the battle over the abortion pill to the Supreme Court after a federal appeals panel put new restrictions on the drug. Attorney General \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  calling on the High Court to defend the \uc2 FDA\uc2  scientific judgment and protect Americans access to safe and effective reproductive care. Mifepristone is the primary drug used in more than half of abortions in the US.\par \par \uc2 HEALTH CARE PROVIDER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 And then this is the medicine for tomorrow. So, you'll do the first dose.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) A federal appeals court ruling the drug can remain on the market for now, but with significant restrictions, only allowing to be used up to seven weeks of pregnancy down from ten and no longer making it available by mail, even in states where abortion is legal. Melissa Grant runs four abortion clinics with telehealth services in 17 states across the country. She says more than half of their patients get the abortion drug by mail.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA GRANT (CHIEF OPERATING OFFICER CARAFAM)\par \par \uc2 It should be more available and not less. The people who it need the most oftentimes live in very rural areas and have difficulty traveling.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Starting Saturday, patients will now be required to make three in-person visits with their doctor to get the pills.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BANNED OR SEVERELY LIMITED ABORTION\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Since Roe vs. Wade was overturned 14 states have seized nearly all abortions.\par \par \uc2 LAWMAKER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Show the bill passes.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Today, Florida on track to become the 15th after passing a six-week abortion ban, Governor DeSantis says that he will sign.\par \par \uc2 ERIN GRALL (REP) (STATE SENATOR FLORIDA)\par \par \uc2 Florida does not want to be a destination state for abortion.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) We travel there talking to health care providers who are already seeing a surge of out-of-state patients, now bracing to turn most away.\par \par \uc2 DR SUJATHA PRABHAKARAN (ABORTION CARE PHYSICIAN)\par \par \uc2 Every time I'm in the health center, there is a patient, at least one if not multiple from all over the southeast who traveled hundreds of miles to get their health care.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The Department of Justice is expected to file that emergency appeal in the coming hours. If the Supreme Court does not weigh in, those new restrictions will remain in place. Whit?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Rachel Scott in Washington for us tonight, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020230414ej4d00006\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 NEW CDC REPORT ON MATERNAL MORTALITY RISE IN WOMEN DYING DURING PREGNANCY & FIRST YEAR AFTER BIRTH\b0\par\par\uc2 1,324 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRESIDENT BIDEN ON THE WORLD STAGE\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, UK, DOCUMENTS, LEAK, AUSTIN, WAPO\par \par \uc2 WAR, UKRAINE, RUSSIA, DOCUMENTS, BREACH, MISSILE\par \par \uc2 CARSTENS, GERSHKOVICH, RUSSIA, PRISON, SWAP, WHELAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TOP US HOSTAGE OFFICIAL ON EFFORTS TO FREE WSJ REPORTER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STATE DEPT. \uc2 EVAN GERSHKOVICH\uc2  "WRONGFULLY DETAINED" BY RUSSIA\par \par \uc2 INDIANA, FIRE, SMOKE, TOXINS, EVACUATIONS, JONES, BROWN, RATZMAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MASSIVE FIRE FORCES THOUSANDS TO EVACUATE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RECYCLING PLANT BLAZE SENDING TOXIC SMOKE IN THE AIR\par \par \uc2 KY, SHOOTING, BANK, BODYCAM, STURGEON, GALLOWAY, WILT, HUMPHREY, SMITH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LOUISVILLE SHOOTING VICTIMS\par \par \uc2 SCOTT, 2024, HALEY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: YOUR VOICE YOUR VOTE\par \par \uc2 INFLATION, CPI, GAS, GROCERY, UTILITY, RENT\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP FROM MANCHESTER TOWNSHIP, NEW JERSEY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 2500 ACRES 10% CONTAINED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA RIGHT NOW\par \par \uc2 MUSIC VIDEO CLIP FROM ED SHEERAN'S "EYES CLOSED"\par \par \uc2 MUSK, BBC, INTERVIEW, TWITTER, DOG\par \par \uc2 VALLOW DAYBELL, MURDER, TRIAL, HERMOSILLO\par \par \uc2 HOMEBUYER, SCAM, AIRBNB, ROTHER, WORK, TIPS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SCAM U\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW WARNING FOR FIRST TIME HOMEBUYERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WOMAN ACCUSED OF TRYING TO SELL A RENTED AIRBNB TO COUPLE\par \par \uc2 NYC, SUBWAY, YOUNG, SHEERAN, "EYES CLOSED"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA: GULF STORM MOVES NORTH\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, LEAK, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS\par \par \uc2 TAIWAN, CHINA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GROWING TENSIONS IN TAIWAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S. KICKS OFF DRILLS WITH PHILIPPINES DAYS AFTER CHINA'S\par \par \uc2 JONES, REINSTATEMENT, PEARSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DECISION DAY FOR OUSTED TENNESSEE LAWMAKER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POSSIBLE VOTE TODAY ON REINSTATING JUSTIN PEARSON\par \par \uc2 ARCINIEGA, FINLEY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SECOND FORMERLY-CONJOINED TWIN HEADED HOME\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REMARKABLE RECOVERY FOR SISTERS AFTER SEPARATION SURGERY\par \par \uc2 GRANDE, BODY IMAGE, KAZDIN\par \par \uc2 INFLATION, ECONOMY GAS PRICES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALL EYES ON NEW INFLATION NUMBERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT YOU CAN DO TO LOWER YOURS GAS & GROCERY BILLS\par \par \uc2 MATERNAL DEATH, MURTHY, RODRIGUEZ, WILLIAMS\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, guys, we're going to turn now to startling numbers from a new CDC report showing that, during the pandemic, more women died during pregnancy or within the year after giving birth.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW CDC REPORT ON MATERNAL MORTALITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RISE IN WOMEN DYING DURING PREGNANCY & FIRST YEAR AFTER BIRTH\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's Black Maternal Health Week, and Janai Norman is here with more on that report on why women of color are at greater risk. Good morning, Janai.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You guys, good morning. So, let's start here. The rate of maternal deaths in the US increased 75% in the last two decades. And we saw a huge increase during the pandemic, before returning closer to pre-pandemic levels and preliminary data for 2022. But specialists tell us the biggest problems include access to affordable high-quality care during pregnancy and especially postpartum.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MATERNAL MORTALITY RATES\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, alarmingly high maternal mortality rates. A new report from the CDC showing a 40% spike in 2021 with more women dying during pregnancy or within a year after giving birth.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The US has one of the worst maternal mortality rates among industrialized, wealthy countries. Why do you think that is?\par \par \uc2 DR VIVEK MURTHY (US SURGEON GENERAL)\par \par \uc2 We know that many women don't have access to preventive and emergency care that they need during pregnancy and after pregnancy. And part of that is that many women don't have the extended coverage that they need for postpartum care.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PREGNANCY RELATED DEATHS: 1,018\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And another new report looking at over 1,000 pregnancy-related deaths in 36 states from 2016 to 2019, finding that 84% were preventable. Black women are three to four times more likely to die from a pregnancy-related causes than white women.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RAISING AWARENESS ABOUT DISPARITIES DURING BLACK MATERNAL HEALTH WEEK\par \par \uc2 DR VIVEK MURTHY (US SURGEON GENERAL)\par \par \uc2 We see that there are long-standing structural issues and barriers that have prevented black women and women of color more broadly from getting the kind of care that they need.\par \par \uc2 EMILIE RODRIGUEZ (DOULA & FOUNDER ASHE BIRTHING SERVICES)\par \par \uc2 We're not aiming to just walk out alive as, you know, as the goal here.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right, yeah.\par \par \uc2 EMILIE RODRIGUEZ (DOULA & FOUNDER ASHE BIRTHING SERVICES)\par \par \uc2 That's the baseline.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Emilie Rodriguez is a doula and founder of Ashe Birthing Services in New York.\par \par \uc2 EMILIE RODRIGUEZ (DOULA & FOUNDER ASHE BIRTHING SERVICES)\par \par \uc2 I wish that when people became pregnant, their provider would say, "Where would you like to give birth? You're a low-risk person. So, if you are high-risk, I would say let's birth in the hospital. That's what I would like to see and all the low-risk people birth outside of the hospital or in the hospital with midwives.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Experts say that anyone planning a birth outside of a hospital or birthing center should have certified midwives attending and have access to hospital if a medical emergency arises.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BIRTH OUTSIDE HOSPITAL OR BIRTHING CENTER\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Rodriguez is Dr. Carla Williams' doula. After having a negative birthing experience in the hospital, Williams, a practicing obstetrician, hired a midwife and doula and had home birth with her a second and third children, joining the less than 1% of women who birth at home, which carries its own set of risks.\par \par \uc2 DR CARLA WILLIAMS (OBSTETRICIAN)\par \par \uc2 I was told by the doctor that, you know, the clock was ticking and that it was going to be time to have a C-Section if I didn't continue to dilate and if I didn't continue to dilate and if I didn't deliver soon. I asked for more time. You know, it's funny to say that, you know, ask for permission.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LABOR & DELIVERY OPTIONS 2020\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) 2020 data across the US shows about one in five to one in three women undergoing c-sections to give birth and an epidural rate covering nearly 80%.\par \par \uc2 DR VIVEK MURTHY (US SURGEON GENERAL)\par \par \uc2 There's been concerned about how high the cesarean section rates have been in this country. And, look, we want to apply care where it's appropriate. And I think we have seen circumstances where sometimes woman aren't offered the full set of options or aren't given the full information they need to help make the best decision for themselves.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, after your two home births, how did that impact how you move forward as a provider yourself?\par \par \uc2 DR CARLA WILLIAMS (OBSTETRICIAN)\par \par \uc2 The biggest thing I feel is, just talking to the patients, really explaining things, giving a true informed consent and allowing them to be autonomous and focusing on the postpartum period and what's necessary to keep them healthy in that crucial time after birth.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And recent CDC data showing just how crucial postpartum care is, finding half maternal deaths happened one week to one year after giving birth. And while one in four of those deaths are from hemorrhage or cardiac conditions, nearly the same amount, one in four, were from mental health conditions with more than 80 deaths attributed to suicide by new moms. The surgeon general says postpartum depression is a major factor. Mental health and social stressors like the lack of resources, returning to work too soon are the important drivers of these mortality numbers that are just unfathomable.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) When you hear the doctor in your report saying that she would have, would rather give birth outside of the hospital...\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Wow.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's really something.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes. And that makes you think. She's a practicing OB, but that is her experience.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Wow.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah. All right, thank you for that enlightening and very important report, Janai. Appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230517ej4c0000n\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 EASY WEEKNIGHT MEALS WITH KRISTIN CAVALLARI "TRULY SIMPLE"\b0\par\par\uc2 1,797 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 LUOMA, MOORE, HASTE, STURGEON, BESHEAR, GREENBERG, SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 LEAK, KIRBY, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON, GUN REFORM, JONES, COOPER, SHULMAN, FARMER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXPELLED TENNESSEE LAWMAKER REINSTATED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ONE OF TWO DEMOCRATS OUSTED FROM STATE LEGISLATURE VOTED BACK IN\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION PILL BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DRUGMAKERS CALL FOR REVERSAL OF FEDERAL JUDGE'S RULING\par \par \uc2 CHARGES, TAYLOR, SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 CLIMATE CHANGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GROWING CONCERNS OVER RISING SEA LEVELS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STUDY FINDS MAJOR SURGE SINCE 2010 IN SOUTHERN U.S.\par \par \uc2 BASEBALL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: METS "ROLL" TO VICTORY!\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REMARKABLE PAIR OF FAIR BALLS HELP NEW YORK TOP SAN DIEGO\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 PARDON, ABBOTT, PERRY, GARZA, BROGDON, FOSTER\par \par \uc2 DAYBELL, TRIAL, BLAKE, WOODCOCK, ARCHIBALD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "DOOMSDAY MOM" LORI VALLOW DAYBELL ON TRIAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IDAHO MOTHER ACCUSED OF KILLING HER SON & DAUGHTER\par \par \uc2 "JUICE JACKING", SECURITY, HACKING, PAYTON\par \par \uc2 REYNOLDS, WREXHAM AFC, FOSTER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AHEAD ON GMA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HILARY SWANK WELCOMES TWINS AT 48\par \par \uc2 LOUISVILLE, SHOOTING, BANK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY LOUISVILLE BANK RAMPAGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AT LEAST FIVE KILLED, EIGHT WOUNDED\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, PILL, ROE V WADE, ACCESS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW NUMBERS SHOW IMPACT OF ABORTION BANS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TENS OF THOUSANDS UNABLE TO GET LEGAL ACCESS\par \par \uc2 TUPPERWARE, STOCK, BANKRUPTCY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE END OF TUPPERWARE?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STOCK PLUNGES AFTER COMPANY SAYS IT COULD GO UNDER\par \par \uc2 PREGNANCY, CHILDBIRTH, SWANK, GERIATRIC, TREND\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HILARY SWANK WELCOMES TWINS AT 48\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OSCAR WINNER JOINS GROWING TREND\par \par \uc2 "VOGUE", CHALAMET, SWIFT\par \par \uc2 PANTS, BAGS, HAIRCARE, SCENTS, WHITENING, CANDLES\par \par \uc2 HAHN, "TINY BEAUTIFUL THINGS", ACTOR, TV\par \par \uc2 BOSTON, \uc2 WNBA\uc2 , DRAFT, FEVER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 WNBA\uc2  TOP DRAFT PICK ALIYAH BOSTON LIVE!\par \par \uc2 TRAILER, "THE MARVELS"\par \par \uc2 COOKING, "TRULY SIMPLE", CAVALLARI, RECIPES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EASY WEEKNIGHT MEALS WITH KRISTIN CAVALLARI\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're back now on "GMA." If you're looking for ideas for dinner, maybe tonight, our next guest has you covered. Kristin Cavallari's new cookbook is called "Truly Simple," and she swears it is. It's full of easy and delicious recipes for weeknights in particular. I love this, Kristin, I love that you are back on "GMA." We always have so much fun together.\par \par \uc2 KRISTIN CAVALLARI ("TRULY SIMPLE")\par \par \uc2 It's good to be back.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's so good, and talk to me about, about the "Truly Simple" of it all because on a weeknight as a busy mom, it's pretty important to get something good on the table but also keep it simple for you.\par \par \uc2 KRISTIN CAVALLARI ("TRULY SIMPLE")\par \par \uc2 Yeah, I mean, I'm balancing\u160\'00\'A0three kids 'schedules. You know, we're going from flag football to horseback riding. It's, it's crazy. So, I still want to make a good dinner every night. I promise you these recipes are very simple and very quick.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And behind the scenes, I was like, "Really, really?" And she said, "Really, really."\par \par \uc2 KRISTIN CAVALLARI ("TRULY SIMPLE")\par \par \uc2 I'm going to give you one. I'm going to show you. You can do these.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, and we chose this because it looks, it smells so good, and everybody here will eat very well. This is sweet balsamic chicken thighs. You love the thighs. You say they have more flavor. They're also very reasonable.\par \par \uc2 KRISTIN CAVALLARI ("TRULY SIMPLE")\par \par \uc2 They are, and yes, I only use thighs because they do have more flavor and especially the bone-in thighs. I also love crisping up the skin, which I'm going to show you. I just think that they taste amazing.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, let's get to it.\par \par \uc2 KRISTIN CAVALLARI ("TRULY SIMPLE")\par \par \uc2 Okay, I'm going for you to work.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Please do.\par \par \uc2 KRISTIN CAVALLARI ("TRULY SIMPLE")\par \par \uc2 Okay, so we are going to put some salt, pepper, and garlic powder on our thighs.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Just sort of...?\par \par \uc2 KRISTIN CAVALLARI ("TRULY SIMPLE")\par \par \uc2 Yeah, you just, and I actually love getting underneath the skin, but I won't make you do it, Lara. I won't make you do it right now.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you, I appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 KRISTIN CAVALLARI ("TRULY SIMPLE")\par \par \uc2 So then what we're going to do is we are going to crisp up the skin. And what you're going to do is you're going to put them in your hot pan.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, you don't put oil on the skin before you put it in the pan?\par \par \uc2 KRISTIN CAVALLARI ("TRULY SIMPLE")\par \par \uc2 So, we're going to\u160\'00\'A0put in the pan, actually, and then you're going to just get your thighs in here, and don't even touch them. Let them be for up to six minutes because you want them then to look like this when you flip them over.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's gorgeous.\par \par \uc2 KRISTIN CAVALLARI ("TRULY SIMPLE")\par \par \uc2 You want them to be super crispy.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But there is oil in the pan, right? I know it's not a smart question, but I'm not a smart cook.\par \par \uc2 KRISTIN CAVALLARI ("TRULY SIMPLE")\par \par \uc2 There is oil in the pan, yes. No, no, this is very good questions.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, so that, they're not, they're now crispy.\par \par \uc2 KRISTIN CAVALLARI ("TRULY SIMPLE")\par \par \uc2 They are now crispy.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And you use the same pan, which I love because one less thing to wash. Chicken is done. Let's make the sauce.\par \par \uc2 KRISTIN CAVALLARI ("TRULY SIMPLE")\par \par \uc2 Okay, so you are going to remove your thighs, put them on a plate, and then you're going to add your butter, big fan of butter here, baby. Let's see, this guy, butter, a little white wine and some shallots.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And you like this combo of white wine and shallots, you are telling our producers.\par \par \uc2 KRISTIN CAVALLARI ("TRULY SIMPLE")\par \par \uc2 I do. I do. I love shallots because, you know, similar to onion, almost a little garlicky flavor. I think they just complement any dish.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I do like them better than onion. They are so flavorful.\par \par \uc2 KRISTIN CAVALLARI ("TRULY SIMPLE")\par \par \uc2 I do, too. Okay, so we're going to get that going. I do use lot of butter in the cookbook, which is pretty much the only cow's milk that we use, maybe a little bit of sour cream from time to time.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Kids love it, though.\par \par \uc2 KRISTIN CAVALLARI ("TRULY SIMPLE")\par \par \uc2 Well, everyone loves that, let's be honest.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And by kids, I meant me. You like to also get your kids involved in the process.\par \par \uc2 KRISTIN CAVALLARI ("TRULY SIMPLE")\par \par \uc2 I do. My kids love being in the kitchen, which I absolutely that they, that they do. Okay, so we are going to actually add some thyme. Usually we would let this, you know, reduce a little bit more.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, of course.\par \par \uc2 KRISTIN CAVALLARI ("TRULY SIMPLE")\par \par \uc2 We have some chicken broth, and then we have a little coconut sugar.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's interesting.\par \par \uc2 KRISTIN CAVALLARI ("TRULY SIMPLE")\par \par \uc2 I love coconut sugar. Okay, so where the balsamic vinegar comes into play.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And vinegar might scare some people because it can take, you know, over, but you say not so. It reduces and breaks down.\par \par \uc2 KRISTIN CAVALLARI ("TRULY SIMPLE")\par \par \uc2 Yeah, when you reduce it, it loses that vinegary flavor. We're going to let this cook for a little while. And this is full fat canned coconut milk, which just makes it creamy without all that added dairy.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Like a curry situation going on.\par \par \uc2 KRISTIN CAVALLARI ("TRULY SIMPLE")\par \par \uc2 A little bit, yeah. Do you smell that? It smells so good. And then we're going move down here. And then, okay, how I like to thicken sauces is with arrowroot powder. So, what we do is we have our arrowroot powder, you're going to add a tablespoon of water.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It smells so good.\par \par \uc2 KRISTIN CAVALLARI ("TRULY SIMPLE")\par \par \uc2 You're going to whisk that up. So, and then I like to do this immediately. You don't want to let your arrowroot just kind of sit there because it'll get kind of gooey. You add that in and then let that sit for a while. And you're going to add your thighs back into the sauce and let them cook.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) How long does this sit?\par \par \uc2 KRISTIN CAVALLARI ("TRULY SIMPLE")\par \par \uc2 So you're going to do about eight-ish minutes on each side. So see, you can see how much this is thickening up the sauce.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So they're cooking with the sauce.\par \par \uc2 KRISTIN CAVALLARI ("TRULY SIMPLE")\par \par \uc2 They are, and then you come over here.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I don't know if you guys can see the finished product, but it is so delicious.\par \par \uc2 KRISTIN CAVALLARI ("TRULY SIMPLE")\par \par \uc2 You can put the added sauce on. Here, I'm going to do that for you.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 KRISTIN CAVALLARI ("TRULY SIMPLE")\par \par \uc2 Do you want sauce? Mine already has some on.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Don't mind if I do.\par \par \uc2 KRISTIN CAVALLARI ("TRULY SIMPLE")\par \par \uc2 And then this is my potato salad. This is a sour cream chive potato salad, also, which is very good.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) When you're making potato salad, do you have a have a favorite? Do you use, what's your favorite potato?\par \par \uc2 KRISTIN CAVALLARI ("TRULY SIMPLE")\par \par \uc2 You know, you can honestly use anything. I like a little fingerling. It's good, right?\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh my gosh, it is fantastic. It's better than good. And it really was truly simple.\par \par \uc2 KRISTIN CAVALLARI ("TRULY SIMPLE")\par \par \uc2 It has that nice little sweetness to it, truly simple, see?\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That is fantastic. Come on over here, Robin Roberts. You're going to love this. "Truly Simple" is the name of Kristin's book. Oh my goodness. Scan the QR code on the screen for this recipe. I mean it, do it. On goodmorningamerica.com, as well. The book, "Truly Simple," I'm sorry to be eating, it's just so good, the book, "Truly Simple," is out today.\par \par \uc2 KRISTIN CAVALLARI ("TRULY SIMPLE")\par \par \uc2 Thank you.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We'll be right back, everybody.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 We've got a lot coming up tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Michael Strahan is back. Have a lovely day.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Have a great day, everybody.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230515ej4b0003l\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 DEALS & STEALS SPRING SPARKLE\b0\par\par\uc2 1,331 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting 