ON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You haven't?\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) No, first time. Learned something new.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, you see, go ahead. There you go. You've got yourself a wristlet there, yeah.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 I think I'd probably wear a fanny pack like The Rock.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, so what's great about these, though, if you do choose one, it's got a lot of compartments on the inside to stash all your stuff in style, plus a little phone pocket on the outside.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh wow, I like that.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Your choice, huge assortment, $20 today.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) $20, great deal there. Oh, you know, this a 10, Perfect 10 haircare.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IT'S A 10 HAIRCARE\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's a 10.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) This actually, I use this.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You do? It's so good. So, we've got three different assortments from them. We've got the blow dry assortment, which is great because it's all glossing, so blow-drying is not going to dry out your hair. This is going to help keep it shiny. This is the keratin collection, which is really great to help restore dry, brittle, color-treated or damaged hair. Their classic collection, if you\u160\'00\'A0put any heat on your hair, or color on your hair, these products are terrific. They start today at $11 with our discounts.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You know, when I blow-dry my hair, you know I need all that.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HYDRAAROMATHERAPY SCENTS\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Exactly, exactly. Okay, Hyraaromatherpy. This is something you would use. So, you're going to take one of those little shower bursts, put it right in this sachet, hang it in your shower, and the steam from the shower than allows that essential oils to just fill the bathroom, so you turn an ordinary shower into a spa experience. Pretty fabulous. The scent is great. Plus we have, right here we've got their bath, their bath teas, which gives you an herbal bath without the mess, and then also all of their roll-on, aromatherapy roll-ons in every scent to help whether it's clarity, dream, unwind, energize. We've got so many options. These are all made in America, really a great product to just elevate your day. These at 50 percent off start at $3.25.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) When you said about hanging it in the show, (inaudible) Eddie went, "Ooh!" I'm like, "Eddie, first of all, you got to take a shower, Eddie."\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) There you go. Maybe that would encourage it.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GLO SCIENCE TEETH WHITENING\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Glo Science. This is an easy way for brightening and whitening teeth. What's great about this is that it combines both heat and blue-light technology created by a New York City dentist with the technology that's used really in dentist offices all around the country.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) For the home.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) They promise faster visible results with no sensitivity, which is important.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Really?\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) This set, which gives you very specific instructions about how to make it work for you, 50 percent off, $99.50. Plus two words...\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Free shipping, two of my favorite words.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SNIF CANDLES\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You got it. And then finally...\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Candles.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...this is Snif, and this was started by two best friends. I like this one. This is, like, instant karma. Smell that. They wanted to kind of revolutionize and put a little twist on ordinary scents. So instant karma, it's kind of a spicy warm cardamom and cinnamon. Which ones? This right here, off the grid, that's lily of the valley, moss, tuberose. It's kind of an herby sent. All of the scent notes are listed online. The packaging is beautiful. So, if you need a little elevated relax and sniff, $22.50 and free shipping.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Nice little sniff right here. This is good. Tory, thank you, as always. And we've partnered with these companies, these great companies, on these deals. You can get them by heading directly to our website. We're going to have much more, spring sparkle deals this week, including tomorrow, items for the home. And coming up next here on "GMA," Kathryn Hahn is here live. We'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STORY SYNOPSIS\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230515ej4b0003f\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 KATHRYN HAHN LIVE IN TIMES SQUARE "TINY BEAUTIFUL THINGS"\b0\par\par\uc2 1,669 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 LUOMA, MOORE, HASTE, STURGEON, BESHEAR, GREENBERG, SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 LEAK, KIRBY, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON, GUN REFORM, JONES, COOPER, SHULMAN, FARMER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXPELLED TENNESSEE LAWMAKER REINSTATED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ONE OF TWO DEMOCRATS OUSTED FROM STATE LEGISLATURE VOTED BACK IN\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION PILL BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DRUGMAKERS CALL FOR REVERSAL OF FEDERAL JUDGE'S RULING\par \par \uc2 CHARGES, TAYLOR, SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 CLIMATE CHANGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GROWING CONCERNS OVER RISING SEA LEVELS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STUDY FINDS MAJOR SURGE SINCE 2010 IN SOUTHERN U.S.\par \par \uc2 BASEBALL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: METS "ROLL" TO VICTORY!\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REMARKABLE PAIR OF FAIR BALLS HELP NEW YORK TOP SAN DIEGO\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 PARDON, ABBOTT, PERRY, GARZA, BROGDON, FOSTER\par \par \uc2 DAYBELL, TRIAL, BLAKE, WOODCOCK, ARCHIBALD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "DOOMSDAY MOM" LORI VALLOW DAYBELL ON TRIAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IDAHO MOTHER ACCUSED OF KILLING HER SON & DAUGHTER\par \par \uc2 "JUICE JACKING", SECURITY, HACKING, PAYTON\par \par \uc2 REYNOLDS, WREXHAM AFC, FOSTER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AHEAD ON GMA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HILARY SWANK WELCOMES TWINS AT 48\par \par \uc2 LOUISVILLE, SHOOTING, BANK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY LOUISVILLE BANK RAMPAGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AT LEAST FIVE KILLED, EIGHT WOUNDED\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, PILL, ROE V WADE, ACCESS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW NUMBERS SHOW IMPACT OF ABORTION BANS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TENS OF THOUSANDS UNABLE TO GET LEGAL ACCESS\par \par \uc2 TUPPERWARE, STOCK, BANKRUPTCY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE END OF TUPPERWARE?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STOCK PLUNGES AFTER COMPANY SAYS IT COULD GO UNDER\par \par \uc2 PREGNANCY, CHILDBIRTH, SWANK, GERIATRIC, TREND\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HILARY SWANK WELCOMES TWINS AT 48\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OSCAR WINNER JOINS GROWING TREND\par \par \uc2 "VOGUE", CHALAMET, SWIFT\par \par \uc2 PANTS, BAGS, HAIRCARE, SCENTS, WHITENING, CANDLES\par \par \uc2 HAHN, "TINY BEAUTIFUL THINGS", ACTOR, TV\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And we are so happy to welcome back Kathryn Hahn to "GMA." You know her from movies like "Glass Onion" and "Bad Moms," and now she's starring in "Tiny Beautiful Things" on Hulu. Welcome back.\par \par \uc2 KATHRYN HAHN ("TINY BEAUTIFUL THINGS")\par \par \uc2 Thank you so much for having.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, this is based on the book by Cheryl Strayed. Ali and I watched the first couple episodes on Sunday. It is terrific. But for people who haven't seen the book, what's this story about?\par \par \uc2 KATHRYN HAHN ("TINY BEAUTIFUL THINGS")\par \par \uc2 Well, the book is very, the pilot of the show is very loosely based on the book. The book is a collection of an advice column and responses under the name of Dear Sugar, who is revealed to be Cheryl Strayed, this amazing writer who wrote "Wild" starring, which became a movie starring Reese Witherspoon. So, Dear Sugar is this advice column, and I think why it hits so radically and so, like, deeply is because there's something radically empathic about her responses. It's, she, what she generously does, Cheryl Strayed, is she gives, she gives of herself to the questioner, and in that radical honesty, I think you feel, one feels less alone in the answers that they give back. And I...\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You can feel her feeling it.\par \par \uc2 KATHRYN HAHN ("TINY BEAUTIFUL THINGS")\par \par \uc2 And I think what's so thrilling about this adaptation by Liz Tigelaar, especially in the pilot, which I read first, is that it's not a linear adaptation at all. Like, she's, she's basically taking the Cheryl Strayed what we've met in "Wild," that we've all seen "Wild," in Reese's production of it, and it's as if, as if Cheryle didn't take that trip on the Pacific Coast Trail. And it's like\u160\'00\'A0what would have happened if she had not.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And you hadn't read the book before you took on this project.\par \par \uc2 KATHRYN HAHN ("TINY BEAUTIFUL THINGS")\par \par \uc2 No, I'm one of the very few. Yeah, I was like, I walked in like, "So, I have questions." Everyone was like, "Oh my God, oh my God" because there's really, like, understandably, like, is a beautiful following for Cheryl, and so I was able to walk in with some pretty basic questions, and Cheryl was so open with it, Liz was so open with it, and we really kind of were able to carve out this, this fictional version of her present-day life together.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, let's take a look at a clip to see what you carved out.\par \par \uc2 KATHRYN HAHN ("TINY BEAUTIFUL THINGS")\par \par \uc2 All right, let's see what I carved out.\par \par \uc2 TV CLIP FROM "TINY BEAUTIFUL THINGS"\par \par \uc2 ACTOR ("TINY BEAUTIFUL THINGS")\par \par \uc2 I realize that this woman that I am pretending to be, you know, working class, pulled himself up by her bootstraps, kind of disheveled, she's literally you.\par \par \uc2 KATHRYN HAHN ("TINY BEAUTIFUL THINGS")\par \par \uc2 Okay, okay, take a left now.\par \par \uc2 ACTOR ("TINY BEAUTIFUL THINGS")\par \par \uc2 You should be the one doing this.\par \par \uc2 KATHRYN HAHN ("TINY BEAUTIFUL THINGS")\par \par \uc2 Doing what?\par \par \uc2 ACTOR ("TINY BEAUTIFUL THINGS")\par \par \uc2 Being Sugar.\par \par \uc2 KATHRYN HAHN ("TINY BEAUTIFUL THINGS")\par \par \uc2 What? No.\par \par \uc2 ACTOR ("TINY BEAUTIFUL THINGS")\par \par \uc2 I mean, it doesn't pay, and, you know, there's no credit because it's anonymous, but I would be your point, and all you have to do is answer like one letter a week.\par \par \uc2 KATHRYN HAHN ("TINY BEAUTIFUL THINGS")\par \par \uc2 Sam, stop it. I'm not giving anybody advice.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You did not want to be an advice, your character did not want to be an advice columnist right there, but if, put yourself in her shoes right now and write an advice column to younger self.\par \par \uc2 KATHRYN HAHN ("TINY BEAUTIFUL THINGS")\par \par \uc2 I would say chill out about your nose, your nose is so, it is really perfect, and that's in the script. There is so much agita I put on, like, changing this face, and I'm so glad I didn't. I feel like you all, all of you beautiful high schoolers are perfect the way you are. You don't have to change a damn thing. Sorry if said damn, but you know what I mean, I'll say D-A-M like it's a, you know, a...\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Water thing.\par \par \uc2 KATHRYN HAHN ("TINY BEAUTIFUL THINGS")\par \par \uc2 ...a water thing. And also be gentle on yourselves. Like, I think we, especially as women, are so hard on ourselves, young women, and we're so tough on ourselves and our ambitions and what we're supposed to be doing. And I think there's this ideal of perfection that we put on ourselves, which is, like, really unattainable, and I feel it adds so much stress and anxiety, and it keeps us out of being, out of the present, and it keeps us in this, like, future place, and it goes way too fast.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It does go way too fast. And you talked out being in the present, and we have to congratulate you because you're part of the Marvel cinematic universe, yes.\par \par \uc2 KATHRYN HAHN ("TINY BEAUTIFUL THINGS")\par \par \uc2 Segue, segue, segue.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Is anything you can tell us about it? Because we know they're very tight-lipped about this type of thing.\par \par \uc2 KATHRYN HAHN ("TINY BEAUTIFUL THINGS")\par \par \uc2 I'm a witch, I can say that. I am a witch, and I feel like my whole life was preparing for this particular part, so I'm very excited for that.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's all you're getting, Michael.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Remember the picture, you became an instant meme. And so...\par \par \uc2 KATHRYN HAHN ("TINY BEAUTIFUL THINGS")\par \par \uc2 Oh, there it is, very attractive.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) This is instant, does\u160\'00\'A0that give you, like, credit with your kids?\par \par \uc2 KATHRYN HAHN ("TINY BEAUTIFUL THINGS")\par \par \uc2 No, nothing does. But you know what I mean? When you're a mom, there's really nothing you can do to make yourself cool. You just have to, you just, everything is, like, is just a lot of, like, shrugs and a lot of, like, one-word answers and a lot of like, "I'm available to text" between duh-duh-duh, and then it's\u160\'00\'A0radio silence. And it's like, "Why are you mad at me?" So it's a lot of, like, trying to not take your teen personally.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That goes for dads, too.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Very true.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Segue, segue, segue. Okay, I can't believe it's been 20 years, ""How to Lose a Guy in 10 Days." And you were recently reunited on a project with Kate, Kate Hudson.\par \par \uc2 KATHRYN HAHN ("TINY BEAUTIFUL THINGS")\par \par \uc2 Yes, yes, dear, dear, dear Kate. I know, I can't believe it's been 20 years. We had a lot of laughs thinking about that and how, like, special. That was my first film I ever did, it was my first, a lot of firsts, lots, my first time out of the country. I was able to go to Toronto to do that. It was like, so it was a huge, huge deal. And also, like, to meet, you know, my first big movie star before Kate Hudson, Michael Dolenz of the Monkees, and that was a huge deal at the monster\u160\'00\'A0truck show in Cleveland, Ohio. So to be able to meet, so to be able to meet her was like a dream, a real dream. And just this, like, and still just is, like, she's a miracle person to me, just as real and honest and such a good mom. And so we picked up right where we left off during "Glass Onion." It was heaven.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Beautiful.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you for coming in.\par \par \uc2 KATHRYN HAHN ("TINY BEAUTIFUL THINGS")\par \par \uc2 Oh, are you kidding me? Thanks\u160\'00\'A0for having me. You're all gems.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) "Tiny Beautiful Things" is streaming now on Hulu. And coming up, Aliyah Boston, the first pick in the WNBA draft, she's here live.\par \par \uc2 KATHRYN HAHN ("TINY BEAUTIFUL THINGS")\par \par \uc2 Very exciting.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Big deal.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230515ej4b0003h\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 "POP NEWS"\b0\par\par\uc2 991 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 LUOMA, MOORE, HASTE, STURGEON, BESHEAR, GREENBERG, SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 LEAK, KIRBY, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON, GUN REFORM, JONES, COOPER, SHULMAN, FARMER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXPELLED TENNESSEE LAWMAKER REINSTATED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ONE OF TWO DEMOCRATS OUSTED FROM STATE LEGISLATURE VOTED BACK IN\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION PILL BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DRUGMAKERS CALL FOR REVERSAL OF FEDERAL JUDGE'S RULING\par \par \uc2 CHARGES, TAYLOR, SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 CLIMATE CHANGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GROWING CONCERNS OVER RISING SEA LEVELS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STUDY FINDS MAJOR SURGE SINCE 2010 IN SOUTHERN U.S.\par \par \uc2 BASEBALL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: METS "ROLL" TO VICTORY!\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REMARKABLE PAIR OF FAIR BALLS HELP NEW YORK TOP SAN DIEGO\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 PARDON, ABBOTT, PERRY, GARZA, BROGDON, FOSTER\par \par \uc2 DAYBELL, TRIAL, BLAKE, WOODCOCK, ARCHIBALD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "DOOMSDAY MOM" LORI VALLOW DAYBELL ON TRIAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IDAHO MOTHER ACCUSED OF KILLING HER SON & DAUGHTER\par \par \uc2 "JUICE JACKING", SECURITY, HACKING, PAYTON\par \par \uc2 REYNOLDS, WREXHAM AFC, FOSTER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AHEAD ON GMA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HILARY SWANK WELCOMES TWINS AT 48\par \par \uc2 LOUISVILLE, SHOOTING, BANK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY LOUISVILLE BANK RAMPAGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AT LEAST FIVE KILLED, EIGHT WOUNDED\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, PILL, ROE V WADE, ACCESS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW NUMBERS SHOW IMPACT OF ABORTION BANS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TENS OF THOUSANDS UNABLE TO GET LEGAL ACCESS\par \par \uc2 TUPPERWARE, STOCK, BANKRUPTCY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE END OF TUPPERWARE?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STOCK PLUNGES AFTER COMPANY SAYS IT COULD GO UNDER\par \par \uc2 PREGNANCY, CHILDBIRTH, SWANK, GERIATRIC, TREND\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HILARY SWANK WELCOMES TWINS AT 48\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OSCAR WINNER JOINS GROWING TREND\par \par \uc2 "VOGUE", CHALAMET, SWIFT\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Let's get some "Pop News" now with Lara.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA EXCLUSIVE: VOGUE MAY COVER REVEAL\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you, Robin. We're going to begin "Pop News" this morning with an exclusive. Thank you, "Vogue" magazine for this very first look at their upcoming May issue, celebrating this year's theme for the Met Gala.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This year's Met Gala, fashion's biggest night, set to celebrate the life and work a long time Chanel designer, the late, great Karl Lagerfeld as part of the \uc2 Metropolitan Museum of Art\uc2 's new exhibition, "Karl Lagerfeld, A Line of Beauty."\par \par \uc2 CHIOMA NNADI (VOGUE.COM)\par \par \uc2 The exhibit brings together over 150 objects spanning that six-decade career at Chanel, Chloe, Fendi and his own label.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) "Vogue" magazine, who helps through the annual fete, sharing exclusive new details from their May issue, featuring 10 models Lagerfeld loved and worked with often, from Naomi Campbell to Kendall Jenner, all wearing new creations from designers who interpreted his singular vision. Photographed by Annie Leibovitz at \uc2 Paris' Grand Palais\uc2 , the site under construction during the shoot home to many of Lagerfeld's history making fashion shows. \uc2 Anna Wintour\uc2 , "Vogue's" editor-in-chief, writing, "A tribute to Karl feels like a tribute to life itself, a celebration in its purest form. We all miss him so very much." The dress code for this year's gala, in honor of Karl.\par \par \uc2 CHIOMA NNADI (VOGUE.COM)\par \par \uc2 The Met Gala red carpet is always a place where people really let their creative juices flow, so we should be in for a treat.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, let it flow. And this year's gala celebrating the life and work of Karl Lagerfeld, right, so it is only proper that his beloved cat, Choupette, should attend. Yes, the "New York Post" is reporting this morning that Choupette has been sent an invitation to this year's gala and could, in fact, be the star of the red carpet. It all happens in less than a month, always on the first Monday in May. You can read the full cover story in the May issue of "Vogue," on newsstands April 25. Why are you laughing, George?\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I was just thinking of how Choupette could have afforded to pay for her own ticket, even.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) There is actually, there is more to that. Do you guys not remember that when Karl Lagerfeld he passed away, he left a large inheritance to Choupette.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's what I was...\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, looking forward to seeing what you wear, darling.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TIMOTHEE CHALAMET TO SING IN BOB DYLAN BIOPIC\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Also in "Pop News" this morning, Timothee Chalamet will play '60s music icon Bob Dylan in a new biopic. The 27-year-old will also sing in the upcoming film, called "A Complete Unknown," the phrase coming from Dylan's 1965 song, "Like A \uc2 Rolling Stone\uc2 ." Director James Mangold saying the movie will follow, quote, "the story of a young, 19-year-old Bob Dylan coming to New York with $2 in his pocket and follows his rapid ascent onto the global stage." No word yet on Chalamet's co-stars, but Mangold has confirmed that Dylan's musical mentors, Woody Guthrie, Pete Seeger and Joan Baez, will all be portrayed in the film. "A Complete Unknown" set to begin production this August. Looking forward to that.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It should be good.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I agree.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TAYLOR SWIFT CONCERT GOER "BORN TO BE A GIRL DAD"\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And finally this morning, we love this dad that you're about to see for loving two Taylor Swift almost as much as his daughters. Look at him go. They are singing every word along with Taylor at her show in Arlington, Texas. The song, "You Belong With Me." That dad there, named Brett Martin, certainly belongs there with his three daughters and their friends, living his best life, making memories that will last a lifetime. Taylor is in the midst of her "Eras" tour, which will continue here in the States through August. Got to get to that.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) He was singing every word.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Every single word. Thought that was really cute. That's "Pop News."\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230515ej4b0003d\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 HILARY SWANK WELCOMES TWINS AT 48 OSCAR WINNER JOINS GROWING TREND\b0\par\par\uc2 1,178 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 LUOMA, MOORE, HASTE, STURGEON, BESHEAR, GREENBERG, SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 LEAK, KIRBY, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON, GUN REFORM, JONES, COOPER, SHULMAN, FARMER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXPELLED TENNESSEE LAWMAKER REINSTATED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ONE OF TWO DEMOCRATS OUSTED FROM STATE LEGISLATURE VOTED BACK IN\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION PILL BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DRUGMAKERS CALL FOR REVERSAL OF FEDERAL JUDGE'S RULING\par \par \uc2 CHARGES, TAYLOR, SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 CLIMATE CHANGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GROWING CONCERNS OVER RISING SEA LEVELS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STUDY FINDS MAJOR SURGE SINCE 2010 IN SOUTHERN U.S.\par \par \uc2 BASEBALL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: METS "ROLL" TO VICTORY!\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REMARKABLE PAIR OF FAIR BALLS HELP NEW YORK TOP SAN DIEGO\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 PARDON, ABBOTT, PERRY, GARZA, BROGDON, FOSTER\par \par \uc2 DAYBELL, TRIAL, BLAKE, WOODCOCK, ARCHIBALD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "DOOMSDAY MOM" LORI VALLOW DAYBELL ON TRIAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IDAHO MOTHER ACCUSED OF KILLING HER SON & DAUGHTER\par \par \uc2 "JUICE JACKING", SECURITY, HACKING, PAYTON\par \par \uc2 REYNOLDS, WREXHAM AFC, FOSTER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AHEAD ON GMA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HILARY SWANK WELCOMES TWINS AT 48\par \par \uc2 LOUISVILLE, SHOOTING, BANK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY LOUISVILLE BANK RAMPAGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AT LEAST FIVE KILLED, EIGHT WOUNDED\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, PILL, ROE V WADE, ACCESS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW NUMBERS SHOW IMPACT OF ABORTION BANS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TENS OF THOUSANDS UNABLE TO GET LEGAL ACCESS\par \par \uc2 TUPPERWARE, STOCK, BANKRUPTCY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE END OF TUPPERWARE?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STOCK PLUNGES AFTER COMPANY SAYS IT COULD GO UNDER\par \par \uc2 PREGNANCY, CHILDBIRTH, SWANK, GERIATRIC, TREND\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HILARY SWANK WELCOMES TWINS AT 48\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OSCAR WINNER JOINS GROWING TREND\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, back now our cover story, Hilary Swank welcoming twins. The actress announcing the news on social media, becoming a mother at 48 years old. Rhiannon Ally has the details for us. Good morning there, Rhiannon.\par \par \uc2 RHIANNON ALLY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning to you, Robin. Well, it's certainly exciting, but being a new mom isn't easy at any age. But a growing number of women, like actress Hilary Swank, are making their motherhood dreams come true on their own terms.\par \par \uc2 TV CLIP FROM "ALASKA DAILY"\par \par \uc2 HILARY SWANK (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 This job isn't easy, and we don't do it to be liked. We do it because it matters.\par \par \uc2 RHIANNON ALLY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) She already has a hit ABC show, and now Oscar-winning actress Hilary Swank can celebrate a new breakout role as a mom of twins. The star of "Million Dollar Baby" posted this picture holding her two babies, saying, quote, "It wasn't easy, but boy, and girl, was it worth it." Back in October, Swank first announced her pregnancy on "GMA."\par \par \uc2 HILARY SWANK (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 This something that I've been wanting for a long time, and my next thing is I'm going to be a mom and not just of one but of two.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Really?\par \par \uc2 HILARY SWANK (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 Yeah.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Oh my gosh.\par \par \uc2 HILARY SWANK (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 I can't believe it.\par \par \uc2 RHIANNON ALLY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Fans followed the star's milestones on social media, from sonogram to her red carpet debut with a six-month baby bump at the Golden Globes to prepping her playlist for birth. At 48 years old, Swank joins a growing trend of women having children later in life. And while some women are delaying childbirth, waiting to get pregnant can also come with an increased possibility of infertility and pregnancy complications.\par \par \uc2 DR. JESSICA SHEPHERD (HER VIEWPOINT)\par \par \uc2 There is not just one approach when it comes to having a baby later on in life. What we really want to look at is the safety of becoming pregnant at a later age and what are the complications that may come from that but in the end, making sure that we have healthy mom and healthy baby.\par \par \uc2 RHIANNON ALLY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) There are a lot of reason women's are waiting until later. Many are focusing on careers and also finding partners later. And Robin, like everything, there's no one age fits all for motherhood.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) No, there is not, Rhiannon, thank you.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GIVING BIRTH IN YOUR 40S\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT ARE THE POTENTIAL RISKS FOR MOTHER & CHILD?\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Our chief medical correspondent, Dr. Jennifer Ashton, is with us now. I remember when Hillary was over there, and she was so excited about this.\par \par \uc2 DR. JEN ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Me, too.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) How common at this age?\par \par \uc2 DR. JEN ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Not common at all. But remember, things are different now. Forty is often the new 30, 50 is the new 40, and women are healthier and more vibrant, generally now than they were a generation ago. So, we are hearing about it and seeing it more. But I think what's really important is when you hear a celebrity at 48 or 50 or 52 announcing their pregnancy, they might not, in general, be telling the whole story. So, oftentimes they may have frozen their eggs at an earlier age, they may use a donor egg. Inside the world of OB-GYN there's kind of a lot of controversy about this because people feel that celebrities are giving the general population a false sense of hope without sharing the complete picture. So, it's not common at this age.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, all right, what are the risks for both baby and mama?\par \par \uc2 DR. JEN ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well first of all, let's talk about the mom, right, because when you're talking about older pregnancies, over 40 certainly, or around the age of 50, remember pregnancy is a stress test. So, we see more things like gestational diabetes, preeclampsia or high blood pressure in pregnancy. For the fetus, low birth weight, preterm birth and deliveries, or even, tragically, stillbirths. So, they are considered a high-risk pregnancy and need to be followed a little more closely. But if the mom is in good shape, you know, we can expect to have a healthy pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And I heard in Rhiannon's report the reason why some women are putting off motherhood. If you decide to do that, have a child later in life, what is, you're an OB-GYN. What's\u160\'00\'A0your suggestion?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT WOMEN SHOULD KNOW ABOUT WAITING TO HAVE CHILDREN\par \par \uc2 DR. JEN ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Let's start 20 years before and reframe our paradigm and not one of\u160\'00\'A0thinking of infertility but being proactive about fertility. So, think about egg freezing in your 20s or 30s, which is still incredibly expensive, but more and more health care employers are providing that as a service. And the cost is slowly starting to come down. Not smoking, keeping your weight at a healthy range, and staying current with all of those well-woman visits that screen for things like cancer, high blood pressure and mental health conditions, super important. We need a healthy mom so we can have a healthy baby.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That we do. All right, Jen, as always, thanks so much.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230515ej4b0003c\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 THE END OF TUPPERWARE? STOCK PLUNGES AFTER COMPANY SAYS IT COULD GO UNDER\b0\par\par\uc2 585 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 LUOMA, MOORE, HASTE, STURGEON, BESHEAR, GREENBERG, SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 LEAK, KIRBY, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON, GUN REFORM, JONES, COOPER, SHULMAN, FARMER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXPELLED TENNESSEE LAWMAKER REINSTATED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ONE OF TWO DEMOCRATS OUSTED FROM STATE LEGISLATURE VOTED BACK IN\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION PILL BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DRUGMAKERS CALL FOR REVERSAL OF FEDERAL JUDGE'S RULING\par \par \uc2 CHARGES, TAYLOR, SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 CLIMATE CHANGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GROWING CONCERNS OVER RISING SEA LEVELS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STUDY FINDS MAJOR SURGE SINCE 2010 IN SOUTHERN U.S.\par \par \uc2 BASEBALL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: METS "ROLL" TO VICTORY!\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REMARKABLE PAIR OF FAIR BALLS HELP NEW YORK TOP SAN DIEGO\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 PARDON, ABBOTT, PERRY, GARZA, BROGDON, FOSTER\par \par \uc2 DAYBELL, TRIAL, BLAKE, WOODCOCK, ARCHIBALD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "DOOMSDAY MOM" LORI VALLOW DAYBELL ON TRIAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IDAHO MOTHER ACCUSED OF KILLING HER SON & DAUGHTER\par \par \uc2 "JUICE JACKING", SECURITY, HACKING, PAYTON\par \par \uc2 REYNOLDS, WREXHAM AFC, FOSTER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AHEAD ON GMA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HILARY SWANK WELCOMES TWINS AT 48\par \par \uc2 LOUISVILLE, SHOOTING, BANK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY LOUISVILLE BANK RAMPAGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AT LEAST FIVE KILLED, EIGHT WOUNDED\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, PILL, ROE V WADE, ACCESS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW NUMBERS SHOW IMPACT OF ABORTION BANS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TENS OF THOUSANDS UNABLE TO GET LEGAL ACCESS\par \par \uc2 TUPPERWARE, STOCK, BANKRUPTCY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE END OF TUPPERWARE?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STOCK PLUNGES AFTER COMPANY SAYS IT COULD GO UNDER\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And we're going to turn now to what could be the end of an American kitchen classic. \uc2 Tupperware\uc2  now saying it could soon go out of business with stock prices plummeting nearly 50 percent yesterday. The brand has been a staple in American homes for more than 75 years and was once known as an innovator of problem-solving kitchen gadgets. The products were famously sold through home parties, a trend that swept the nation in the '50s and '60s, but the analysts say the company has struggled to connect with younger consumers. It was also around in the '70s because I remember my mama having some \uc2 Tupperware\uc2  parties. I love \uc2 Tupperware\uc2 . I think I should buy some just to help out.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right, remember how you had to burp it?\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It kept, it keeps the food fresh, Robin. That's all I care about.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Coming up on our "GMA Morning Menu," Oscar winner Hilary Swank welcoming twins at the age of 48. Dr. Ashton is here with what women should know about having babies later in life.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Also this morning, get ready to treat yourself. Tory Johnson is here with some sparkles, spring sparkle "Deals & Steals."\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And Kathryn Hahn is here. She's going to tell us about her new series, "Tiny Beautiful Things." And Lara, you have a special guest, as well.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, I hope you're hungry, George. I'm here with Kristin Cavallari, and she's going to show us what's for dinner tonight from her brand-new cookbook out today, and we are going to dish. Did you get that? Coming up on "Good Morning America," everyone.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 I know I've said this before, I'll say it again. Every time I hear this song, I think of this man right here. First time I walked in your dressing room, you were playing that.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Yeah, makes me happy.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 "Lovely Day," yeah.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230515ej4b0003b\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 "THE MARVELS" FIRST LOOK\b0\par\par\uc2 464 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 LUOMA, MOORE, HASTE, STURGEON, BESHEAR, GREENBERG, SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 LEAK, KIRBY, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON, GUN REFORM, JONES, COOPER, SHULMAN, FARMER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXPELLED TENNESSEE LAWMAKER REINSTATED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ONE OF TWO DEMOCRATS OUSTED FROM STATE LEGISLATURE VOTED BACK IN\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION PILL BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DRUGMAKERS CALL FOR REVERSAL OF FEDERAL JUDGE'S RULING\par \par \uc2 CHARGES, TAYLOR, SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 CLIMATE CHANGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GROWING CONCERNS OVER RISING SEA LEVELS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STUDY FINDS MAJOR SURGE SINCE 2010 IN SOUTHERN U.S.\par \par \uc2 BASEBALL\par \par \uc2