, WHITENING, CANDLES\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 Welcome back to "GMA," live from Times Square.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230515ej4b0003g\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 NEW NUMBERS SHOW IMPACT OF ABORTION BANS TENS OF THOUSANDS UNABLE TO GET LEGAL ACCESS\b0\par\par\uc2 834 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 LUOMA, MOORE, HASTE, STURGEON, BESHEAR, GREENBERG, SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 LEAK, KIRBY, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON, GUN REFORM, JONES, COOPER, SHULMAN, FARMER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXPELLED TENNESSEE LAWMAKER REINSTATED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ONE OF TWO DEMOCRATS OUSTED FROM STATE LEGISLATURE VOTED BACK IN\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION PILL BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DRUGMAKERS CALL FOR REVERSAL OF FEDERAL JUDGE'S RULING\par \par \uc2 CHARGES, TAYLOR, SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 CLIMATE CHANGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GROWING CONCERNS OVER RISING SEA LEVELS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STUDY FINDS MAJOR SURGE SINCE 2010 IN SOUTHERN U.S.\par \par \uc2 BASEBALL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: METS "ROLL" TO VICTORY!\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REMARKABLE PAIR OF FAIR BALLS HELP NEW YORK TOP SAN DIEGO\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 PARDON, ABBOTT, PERRY, GARZA, BROGDON, FOSTER\par \par \uc2 DAYBELL, TRIAL, BLAKE, WOODCOCK, ARCHIBALD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "DOOMSDAY MOM" LORI VALLOW DAYBELL ON TRIAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IDAHO MOTHER ACCUSED OF KILLING HER SON & DAUGHTER\par \par \uc2 "JUICE JACKING", SECURITY, HACKING, PAYTON\par \par \uc2 REYNOLDS, WREXHAM AFC, FOSTER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AHEAD ON GMA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HILARY SWANK WELCOMES TWINS AT 48\par \par \uc2 LOUISVILLE, SHOOTING, BANK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY LOUISVILLE BANK RAMPAGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AT LEAST FIVE KILLED, EIGHT WOUNDED\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, PILL, ROE V WADE, ACCESS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW NUMBERS SHOW IMPACT OF ABORTION BANS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TENS OF THOUSANDS UNABLE TO GET LEGAL ACCESS\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to the state of access to abortion in America. Nearly 10 months after the Supreme Court's decision overturning Roe v Wade, new numbers give us a picture of just how many people have been impacted as a new battle over the abortion pill plays out in the courts. Rachel is back with more on that. Good morning again, Rachel.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey Robin, good morning to you again. We are expecting a ruling on the abortion pill any day now. No matter what side of the debate you are on, everyone agrees it could dramatically change the landscape of abortion access for the second time in less than a year, and it comes as we are only starting to learn the impact of the Supreme Court's decision to overturn Roe v Wade.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Kylie and Seth Beaton were thrilled to be expecting their second child, but the Texas couple's joy was short-lived when Kylie's doctor discovered her baby had a rare and severe condition impacting the development of the brain.\par \par \uc2 KYLIE BEATON (TEXAS RESIDENT)\par \par \uc2 The baby could survive maybe an hour, a day, but the longevity or the likelihood of the max is anywhere for a couple weeks.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) With Texas' strict abortion ban, Kylie is faced with carrying her nonviable pregnancy to term.\par \par \uc2 SETH BEATON (TEXAS RESIDENT)\par \par \uc2 I'm just terrified for my wife. I mean, she's the strongest person I know, and she's just helpless right now.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Texas is one of 14 states that have banned nearly all access to abortion after the supreme court overturned Roe v Wade nearly a year ago. New estimates from research project We Count, obtained exclusively by FiveThirtyEight, show around 66,000 people have been unable to receive a legal abortion in their home states, an estimated 35,000 of them traveling out of state for an abortion, while the remaining 31,000 were likely left without access to legal abortion at all, either continuing their pregnancies or getting an abortion another way.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) We traveled to a clinic in Florida where an abortion provider told us she's seen a surge in out-of-state patients.\par \par \uc2 DR. SUJATHA PRABHAKARAN (FLORIDA ABORTION CARE)\par \par \uc2 Every time I'm in the health center, there is a patient, at least one, if not multiple, from Alabama, Georgia, Louisiana, Tennessee, Arkansas, all over the Southeast, who traveled hundreds of miles to get their health care.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Abortion is still legal in Florida up to 15 weeks, but state lawmakers are moving forward with a bill to ban abortion after six weeks, before most people even know they're pregnant.\par \par \uc2 STATE SENATOR ERIN GRALL (REP) (FLORIDA)\par \par \uc2 Florida is the destination for many great things, but we should never be considered a destination state for the termination of an unborn child.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, states are pushing for their own restrictions, but all eyes, of course, are on this legal fight over access to the abortion pill. A conservative judge in Texas ruled it should have never been approved by the \uc2 FDA\uc2  in the first place, but the Biden administration is giving up for a fight, and more than 400 drug and biotech companies are backing that up. They put out a joint letter blasting the decision, saying it ignores decades of scientific evidence and legal precedent. The bottom line here, a ban would have a huge impact. Abortion pills are used in more than half of abortions in the US, Michael.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You said it, a huge impact. Thank you so much for that.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230515ej4b0003a\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 INTRODUCTION TO THE 8:00 HALF HOUR\b0\par\par\uc2 520 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 LUOMA, MOORE, HASTE, STURGEON, BESHEAR, GREENBERG, SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 LEAK, KIRBY, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON, GUN REFORM, JONES, COOPER, SHULMAN, FARMER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXPELLED TENNESSEE LAWMAKER REINSTATED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ONE OF TWO DEMOCRATS OUSTED FROM STATE LEGISLATURE VOTED BACK IN\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION PILL BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DRUGMAKERS CALL FOR REVERSAL OF FEDERAL JUDGE'S RULING\par \par \uc2 CHARGES, TAYLOR, SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 CLIMATE CHANGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GROWING CONCERNS OVER RISING SEA LEVELS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STUDY FINDS MAJOR SURGE SINCE 2010 IN SOUTHERN U.S.\par \par \uc2 BASEBALL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: METS "ROLL" TO VICTORY!\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REMARKABLE PAIR OF FAIR BALLS HELP NEW YORK TOP SAN DIEGO\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 PARDON, ABBOTT, PERRY, GARZA, BROGDON, FOSTER\par \par \uc2 DAYBELL, TRIAL, BLAKE, WOODCOCK, ARCHIBALD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "DOOMSDAY MOM" LORI VALLOW DAYBELL ON TRIAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IDAHO MOTHER ACCUSED OF KILLING HER SON & DAUGHTER\par \par \uc2 "JUICE JACKING", SECURITY, HACKING, PAYTON\par \par \uc2 REYNOLDS, WREXHAM AFC, FOSTER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AHEAD ON GMA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HILARY SWANK WELCOMES TWINS AT 48\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Good morning, America. It's 8:00 am.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY LOUISVILLE BANK RAMPAGE\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 New details this morning and the deadly Louisville bank rampage, an employee opening fire in a crowded conference room. Officers on the scene in three minutes, stopping the shooter. Five people killed, eight others wounded, including two police officers.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Abortion pill showdown. Hundreds of drug companies warning of the potential repercussions for other medications plus the new numbers breaking down how many people have been impacted.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HILLARY SWANK HAS TWINS!\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Oscar-winner Hilary Swank becoming a mother for the first time at 48, sharing this photo of her newborn twins. With more women later in life giving breath, Dr. Ashton is here with what moms-to-be need to know.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VOGUE'S MAY ISSUE\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 It's time to "Vogue." Ahead of fashion's biggest night, we are exclusively revealing "Vogue's" May cover, how they're honoring this year's Met Gala theme.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SPRING SPARKLE DEALS AND STEALS!\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 We are getting the party started with spring sparkle "Deals & Steals." Tory Johnson is here with some amazing products to treat yourself.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: KATHRYN HAHN\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And Kathryn Hahn is live in Times Square talking about her new show and more, and she is saying...\par \par \uc2 KATHRYN HAHN ("TINY BEAUTIFUL THINGS")\par \par \uc2 Good morning, America.\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 Live in Times Square, this is "GMA."\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Good morning, America. You know who's is having a really good morning? Aliyah Boston, that woman right there, stand-out at South Carolina for Dawn Staley, the number one pick in last night's \uc2 WNBA\uc2  draft. She's going to tell us all about that incredible moment hearing her name called first and what her future will bring as a member of the Indiana Fever. That's coming up.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 We are looking forward to that. Also ahead, a report looking at the change in access to abortion by the numbers, revealing the impact of the ban spreading across the country.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230515ej4b00038\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ABORTION PILL BATTLE DRUGMAKERS CALL FOR REVERSAL OF FEDERAL JUDGE'S RULING\b0\par\par\uc2 413 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 LUOMA, MOORE, HASTE, STURGEON, BESHEAR, GREENBERG, SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 LEAK, KIRBY, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON, GUN REFORM, JONES, COOPER, SHULMAN, FARMER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXPELLED TENNESSEE LAWMAKER REINSTATED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ONE OF TWO DEMOCRATS OUSTED FROM STATE LEGISLATURE VOTED BACK IN\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION PILL BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DRUGMAKERS CALL FOR REVERSAL OF FEDERAL JUDGE'S RULING\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to the abortion pill battle. Executives from hundreds of pharmaceutical and biotech companies calling for a federal judge's ruling to be reversed. Our senior congressional correspondent Rachel Scott is here in the studio with us and has more. Good morning, Rachel.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, Robin, good morning. And this is the first major test of abortion rights since the Supreme Court overturned Roe vs. Wade nearly a year ago, and the Biden demonstration is gearing up for a fight.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) At the center of all of this, conflicting rulings about access to the abortion drug, mifepristone. This is a pill that's used in more than half of abortions in the US. It's been available for more than 20 years, but one conservative judge in Texas ruled to ban the pill, saying that it should've never been approved by the \uc2 FDA\uc2  in the first place. And this morning, the Justice Department is firing back, filing an emergency appeal blasting the decision as an extraordinary and unprecedented decision, insisting that it would severely harm women.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And just as scathing was the reaction of more than 400 drug and biotech companies, whose executives published this letter insisting the decision "ignores decades of scientific evidence and legal precedent and lays the groundwork for banning any medicine."\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DRUG COMPANIES CONDEMN TEXAS ABORTION PILL RULING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CALL FOR FEDERAL JUDGE'S RULING TO BE REVERSED & WARN OF FALLOUT\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) In the meantime, we have several Democratic-led states that are now taking matters into their own hands. They are stockpiling this abortion medication.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOME STATES STOCKPILING MEDICATION IN WAKE OF FEDERAL RULING\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Massachusetts, for instance, buying 15,000 doses, enough to last an entire year. But this is a legal fight that is only just beginning. It is widely expected to go all the way to the Supreme Court, guys.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's far from over. Rachel, thanks.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230515ej4b0002x\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 BATTLE OVER ABORTION PILL BIDEN CALLS JUDGE'S RULING "COMPLETELY OUT OF BOUNDS"\b0\par\par\uc2 398 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, STURGEON, GALLOWAY, VILLAROEL, MCGARVEY\par \par \uc2 FIRE, EVACUATION, SNOW\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INFERNO TRIGGERS EVACUATIONS\par \par \uc2 AUSTIN, UKRAINE, LEAK, RUSSIA, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LEAKED DOCUMENTS FALLOUT\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, BRAGG, JORDAN, LAWSUIT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MANHATTAN DA SUING REP. JORDAN\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, BIDEN, RULINGS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BATTLE OVER ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to the fierce and deeply personal debate over abortion pill. Tonight, a federal appeals court decision expected within days here on whether to block or uphold a Texas judge's ruling that would take effect by the end of the week. It would suspend \uc2 FDA\uc2  approval of a drug used for 20 years in this country. Well, tonight, President Biden now weighing in. So, let's bring in Mary Bruce on what the White House says it is ready to do. But first, here's what the President said today.\par \par \uc2 REPORTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 And on the abortion pill ruling, what are your thoughts?\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2  (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 My thoughts are, it's completely out-of-bounds what the judge did.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, let's bring in Mary Bruce. She's overseas traveling with the President. But, Mary, the White House indicating they are ready to act if this judge's ruling isn't blocked, at least temporarily.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) David, it is very possible that this case could land at the Supreme Court before the end of the week. So, here's where things stand. The White House is hoping that the Fifth Circuit will freeze the Texas ruling. They are asking them to weigh in by noon on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BIDEN CALLS JUDGE'S RULING "COMPLETELY OUT OF BOUNDS"\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And if they don't, the White House is prepared to take this to the Supreme Court and fast because the Texas ruling is set to take effect Friday night at midnight, banning the manufacturing and distribution of this abortion medication nationwide. Now, in the meantime, you're seeing the scramble across the country. Four states now, California, Massachusetts, Washington and, just today, New York also are all now stockpiling abortion medications. David?\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Mary Bruce, who's in Belfast. We'll have more on the President's trip tomorrow night right here. Mary, thank you on the breaking headline.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020230412ej4b00006\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 SHOWDOWN OVER THE ABORTION PILL TEXAS JUDGE RULES \uc2 FDA\uc2 'S APPROVAL OF MIFEPRISTONE NOW INVALID\b0\par\par\uc2 828 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TOP SECRET DOCUMENT LEAK\par \par \uc2 DOCUMENTS, PENTAGON, DOJ, LEAK, COHEN, INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 DOCUMENTS, CLASSIFIED, SECURITY, PENTAGON, INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, JUDGES, MIFEPRISTONE, MCGILL, BECERRA, HAWKINS\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hopefully the authorities will get to the bottom of it very soon, George. Now we have the latest on the abortion pill standoff. Questions over whether the pill will soon be available following contradictory rulings by two federal judges. Our senior congressional correspondent Rachel Scott is here now with more. Good morning, Rachel.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SHOWDOWN OVER THE ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS JUDGE RULES \uc2 FDA\uc2 'S APPROVAL OF MIFEPRISTONE NOW INVALID\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Robin, good morning. More than half of abortions in the country are done by pill. This is something that was approved by the \uc2 FDA\uc2  more than 20 years ago. But now we have one court saying it should be allowed, you have another court saying it should be not, and future access is hanging in limbo.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, conflicting federal rulings sparking new uncertainty and confusion over access to the most widely used abortion medication. Abortion rights advocates taking to the streets after a conservative federal judge in Texas ruled to suspend \uc2 FDA\uc2  approval of Mifepristone, a medication that has been available for more than 20 years and is used in more than half of abortions in the US.\par \par \uc2 ALEXIS MCGILL (PRESIDENT PLANNED PARENTHOOD)\par \par \uc2 How is it that one person, one judge, with no medical degree, no science degree, can make a decision about a drug that has been used, that has been safe, and proven effective?\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But within hours, a federal judge in Washington State ruled to keep the pill available. The Justice Department now appealing the case as the Biden administration promises a fight.\par \par \uc2 XAVIER BECERRA\uc2  (SECRETARY OF HEALTH AND HUMAN SERVICES)\par \par \uc2 This is not America. What you saw by that one judge in that one court in that one state, that's not America.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It now heads to the conservative fifth circuit court of appeals, set to decide this week if Mifepristone should stay available or be put on pause, as the case makes its way through the courts. Anti-abortion rights advocates hope it'll be taken off the market for good.\par \par \uc2 KRISTAN HAWKINS (PRESIDENT STUDENTS FOR LIFE ACTION)\par \par \uc2 It was certainly a victory, it was one that we've been praying for for some time.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SHOWDOWN OVER THE ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LEGAL FIGHT EXPECTED TO GO ALL THE WAY TO T SUPREME COURT\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) For now, Mifepristone is still available, but experts say this is a legal showdown expected to go all the way to the Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And of course it's been nearly a year since the Supreme Court overturned Roe V. Wade. President Biden warning the Texas ruling is the next big step toward a national ban on abortion. But so far we quite frankly have heard little from Republicans on this. Democrats of course use abortion rights to help mobilize their voters in the midterm election. Robin.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SHOWDOWN OVER THE ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT IF YOU LIVE IN A STATE WHERE ABORTION IS LEGAL?\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We do remember that, Rachel. You talked about how widely used this abortion medication is. Now if you live in a state where abortion is legal, does the Texas abortion pill ruling have an impact?\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, Robin, so let's break this down. 40% of abortion clinics only offer abortion pills, and it's used, again, in more than half of abortions in the country. So the implications here are significant and would dramatically change the landscape if this was put on hold by a federal judge. It would affect everyone nationwide, even in the 36 states where the pill is currently legally available, Robin.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So in those states where abortion is legal, what are officials doing to prepare, Rachel?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SHOWDOWN OVER THE ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW OFFICIALS ARE PREPARING IN STATES WHERE ABORTION IS LEGAL\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Look, it's very possible that Democratic governors and abortion clinics spend this next week trying to buy the abortion drug in bulk, so if the \uc2 FDA\uc2  approval is suspended, they would already have that stock in hand. We've seen this happen in Washington State where the Democratic governor there just purchased a three-year supply.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But if the higher courts do let this ruling stand, we will see that supply go away, and then of course, there won't be a chance to buy anymore. Robin.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Rachel, good to have you in the studio here with us. Rebecca.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230515ej4a00004\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 GOOD MORNING AMERICA\b0\par\par\uc2 513 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TOP SECRET DOCUMENT LEAK\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Good morning, America. The Biden administration now containing the fallout from a highly classified documents leaked. The scramble to find out who's responsible. The Justice Department has launched a criminal investigation after highly sensitive materials were posted on the internet, including detailed information on the fight for Ukraine, Iran's nuclear program, China, and North Korea. The top-secret documents prompting allies to respond. And this morning, the blame game, as the Pentagon races to get to the bottom of the breach.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS; GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION PILL SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Abortion pill showdown. Future access now hanging in the balance after conflicting federal rulings. The legal battle ahead. Abortion rights advocates taking to streets, and how it could affect everyone nationwide, even states where abortion is legal.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WILL LAWMAKERS BE REINSTATED?\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Also this morning, fighting to get their jobs back. The emergency meetings now set for the Tennessee lawmakers who were removed from the state legislature for protesting, and calling for gun reform on the House floor. Could they be reinstated as pressure grows?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FACING JUSTICE\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Facing justice. The Idaho mother, Lori Vallow Daybell, accused of killing her two children and her husband's previous wife, in what prosecutors allege was part of a doomsday plot, set to go on trial this morning. Dan Abrams is here breaking down the case.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEARCH FOR ANSWERS\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 The hunt for answers. Nearly 2,000 people searching for a missing Minnesota mother of two who vanished more than a week ago. What her family is saying this morning, and who saw her last.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPER ALLERGY SEASON?\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Super allergy season? Dr. Ashton breaks down the possibly longer, tougher time, and is what you're eating making your symptoms worse?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "SHARK" ROGER HERJAVEC LIVE\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 "Shark" Robert Herjavec, the business mogul, here live answering your questions on jobs, the housing market, paying down debt, and starting a business.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WOODS WITHDRAWS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MASTERS COMEBACK KID\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And will it be the last time we see Tiger at Augusta? As comeback kid Jon Rahm collects his first jacket, surging to victory at the Masters. Did the champion predict his own fortune 10 years ago?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 Live in Times Square, this is "Good morning America."\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 This is "Good Morning America." We hope everyone had a lovely weekend. Will Reeve will have everything Masters coming up.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Robin, Will Reeve always ready to grip it and rip it. We have also have a lot of news to get to, including the latest on the abortion pill showdown, and two Tennessee lawmakers waiting to see if they will be reinstated.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230515ej4a00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 INTRODUCTION TO THE 08:00 HALF-HOUR\b0\par\par\uc2 613 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TOP SECRET DOCUMENT LEAK\par \par \uc2 DOCUMENTS, PENTAGON, DOJ, LEAK, COHEN, INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 DOCUMENTS, CLASSIFIED, SECURITY, PENTAGON, INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, JUDGES, MIFEPRISTONE, MCGILL, BECERRA, HAWKINS\par \par \uc2 TENNESSEE, EXPULSION, JONES, PEARSON, KUMAR, REINSTATE\par \par \uc2 CHINA, TAIWAN, TENSIONS, WARPLANES, STRAIT\par \par \uc2 VIOLENCE, MIDDLE EAST, ROCKETS, RETALIATION\par \par \uc2 MASTERS, RAHM, LIV, PGA, SMITH, WOODS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR SPRING THAW\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM "THE SUPER MARIO BROS MOVIE"\par \par \uc2 VALLOW, DAYBELL, MURDERS, GRAY, WOODCOCK\par \par \uc2 KINGSBURY, MISSING, SEARCH, DAY CARE, WILLIAMS\par \par \uc2 HERJAVEC\uc2 , "SHARK TANK", JOBS, BUSINESSES, SAVINGS\par \par \uc2 NHL, \uc2 BRUINS\uc2 , RECORD, WINS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Good morning, America. It's 8:00 AM.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TOP SECRET DOCUMENT LEAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR BREACH\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 The Justice Department has launched a criminal investigation after highly sensitive materials were posted in the internet, including detailed information about the fight in Ukraine, Iran's nuclear program, China and North Korea. The Biden administration rushing to contain the fallout and the scramble to find out who is responsible.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NATIONWIDE IMPACT?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION PILL SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Abortion pill battle. Future access hanging in the balance after conflicting federal rulings. The legal showdown ahead and the effect it could have nationwide, even in states where abortion is legal.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TAYLOR SWIFT AND JOE ALWYN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: A NEW "ERA"\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 A new "era." Taylor Swift and Joe Alwyn calling it quits as she travels the globe on tour.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EASING INTO YOUR WORK WEEK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BARE MINIMUM MONDAYS\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Are you missing summer Fridays? Well, say hello to "bare minimum Mondays." How boundaries could help you ease into the work week. Rebecca will tell us if this trend is a good idea for your career.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE "SHARK" DIVES IN!\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 ROBERT HERJAVEC\uc2  LIVE!\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 It's time for a financial fix. Shark \uc2 Robert Herjavec\uc2  is here live answering your money questions.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HUGE "STAR WARS" ANNOUNCEMENTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "REY" OF SUNSHINE RETURNS!\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Inside "Star Wars" celebration 2023. Going behind the scenes of a galaxy far, far away, fans flipping out over the big announcements. A "Rey" of sunshine set to return. Plus, Jude Law and Rosario Dawson joined the ride of a lifetime.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LIVE ON GMA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RAMON RODRIGUEZ\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And we've got Ramon Rodriguez on the case.\par \par \uc2 RAMON RODRIGUEZ ("WILL TRENT")\par \par \uc2 I bet I can solve this tonight.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 The "Will Trent" star is live in Times Square. And he's saying...\par \par \uc2 RAMON RODRIGUEZ ("WILL TRENT")\par \par \uc2 Good morning, America.\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 Live in times square, this is "GMA."\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Good morning, America. It's good to have you with us on this busy Monday morning. Thank you so much, Rebecca, for being here. Michael will be back from his much-deserved spring break tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Absolutely, it's great to be here.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 But we want folks to meet the Clark family. They're from Michigan. They welcomed their first baby daughter a few weeks ago, making her the first baby girl in more than, are you ready for this, more than 130 years on her dad's side of the family.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Wow.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 We're going to meet mom and dad in a little bit and baby Audrey, who has broken the streak. That's coming up.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 But first, Dr. Jen Ashton is here with why this may be one of the worst and longest allergy seasons in years, and the surprising things that could make your symptoms worse.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230515ej4a0000f\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 SHOWDOWN OVER THE ABORTION PILL TEXAS JUDGE RULES FDA'S APPROVAL OF MIFEPRISTONE NOW INVALID\b0\par\par\uc2 417 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TOP SECRET DOCUMENT LEAK\par \par \uc2 DOCUMENTS, PENTAGON, DOJ, LEAK, COHEN, INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 DOCUMENTS, CLASSIFIED, SECURITY, PENTAGON, INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, JUDGES, MIFEPRISTONE, MCGILL, BECERRA, HAWKINS\par \par \uc2 TENNESSEE, EXPULSION, JONES, PEARSON, KUMAR, REINSTATE\par \par \uc2 CHINA, TAIWAN, TENSIONS, WARPLANES, STRAIT\par \par \uc2 VIOLENCE, MIDDLE EAST, ROCKETS, RETALIATION\par \par \uc2 MASTERS, RAHM, LIV, PGA, SMITH, WOODS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR SPRING THAW\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM "THE SUPER MARIO BROS MOVIE"\par \par \uc2 VALLOW, DAYBELL, MURDERS, GRAY, WOODCOCK\par \par \uc2 KINGSBURY, MISSING, SEARCH, DAY CARE, WILLIAMS\par \par \uc2 HERJAVEC, "SHARK TANK", JOBS, BUSINESSES, SAVINGS\par \par \uc2 NHL, \uc2 BRUINS\uc2 , RECORD, WINS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 LEAK, SECURITY, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS, KIRBY\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, RULINGS\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, George, we turn now to the latest on the abortion pill standoff.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SHOWDOWN OVER THE ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS JUDGE RULES FDA'S APPROVAL OF MIFEPRISTONE NOW INVALID\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Questions over whether the pill will soon be available following contradictory rulings by two federal judges. Our senior congressional correspondent Rachel Scott is back with more. Good morning again, Rachel.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, Robin, good morning to you again. Well, there's new uncertainty and confusion over access to the most widely used abortion medication. It comes after a federal judge in Texas rule to suspend FDA approval of mifepristone.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This is a pill that has been available for more than 20 years and is used in more than half of abortions in the US. Within hours of that ruling, another federal judge in Washington state weighed in to keep the pill available.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TWO FEDERAL JUDGES ISSUE CONTRADICTORY RULINGS\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) So, now, you have one court saying it should be allowed, you have another court saying it should not. The big question, where does it all go from here? Well, all eyes are on the Fifth Circuit Court of Appeals, which is set to decide this week if the pill should stay available or be put on hold this case makes its way through the court.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But this is a legal showdown that's expected to go all the way to the Supreme Court, Robin.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LEGAL FIGHT EXPECTED TO GO ALL THE WAY TO SUPREME COURT\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We will see where it goes from here. Rebecca? I'm sorry, Rachel. Thank you. Rebecca?\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Robin, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230515ej4a0000h\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ABORTION PILL LEGAL BATTLE DOJ APPEALS RULING THAT WOULD BLOCK ACCESS TO DRUG\b0\par\par\uc2 691 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 BANK, SHOOTING, HUMPHREY, BESHEAR, STURGEON\par \par \uc2 PEARSON, JONES, SHULMAN, HARDY, FARMER, JOHNSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXPELLED LAWMAKER REINSTATED\par \par \uc2 LEAK, SECURITY, KIRBY, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "TOP SECRET" LEAKS SEARCH\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, MACE, BAPTIST, HEALEY, INSLEE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION PILL LEGAL BATTLE\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to the deeply personal issue of abortion. And tonight, the Justice Department is now appealing that federal judge's ruling in Texas, suspending \uc2 FDA\uc2  approval of an abortion pill used across much of this nation for more than 20 years. Here's Rachel Scott.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOJ APPEALS RULING THAT WOULD BLOCK ACCESS TO DRUG\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, the Justice Department filing an emergency appeal, trying to block a federal judge's ruling that would revoke the \uc2 FDA\uc2 's approval of the abortion drug mifepristone and taken off the market as soon as Friday. The DOJ writing, "If allowed to take affect, the court's order would thwart \uc2 FDA\uc2 's scientific judgment and severely harm women."\par \par \uc2 HEALTH CARE PROVIDER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 And then this is the medicine for tomorrow. So, you'll do the first dose.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The abortion pill was approved by the \uc2 FDA\uc2  more than 20 years ago and is used in more than half of all abortions in the US. But the Texas judge appointed by former president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , arguing the \uc2 FDA\uc2 's approval was based on plainly unsound reasoning. Tonight, executives from more than 400 pharmaceutical and biotech companies blasted the ruling, writing, "It ignores decades of scientific evidence and legal precedent. If courts can overturn drug approval without regard for science or evidence, any medicine is at risk for the same outcome as mifepristone."\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHITE HOUSE: PREPARED FOR LONG FIGHT IN COURTS\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Some Democrats and even some Republicans now urging the White House to defy the judge's order entirely.\par \par \uc2 REPRESENTATIVE NANCY MACE (REP) (SOUTH CAROLINA)\par \par \uc2 This is an \uc2 FDA\uc2 -approved drug. I support the usage of \uc2 FDA\uc2 -approved drugs, even if we might disagree. It's not up to us to decide as legislators or even, you know, as the court system that whether or not this is the right drug to use or not, number one. So, I agree with ignoring it at this point.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Hours after the Texas ruling came down, a judge in Washington state issuing a contradictory ruling, blocking any change, the status quo rights as it related to the availability of mifepristone." But that ruling only applying to the 36 states where it's currently legal. The Texas ruling would apply to every state. Anti-abortion rights advocates preparing for a long legal battle cute\par \par \uc2 ERIK BAPTIST (ALLIANCE DEFENDING FREEDOM)\par \par \uc2 Obviously, this is not the last stage and the last word on this issue and we're ready to go the next stage.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Now, some Democratic governors building up a stockpile of the drug in case it's taken off the market.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR MAURA HEALEY (DEM) (MASSACHUSETTS)\par \par \uc2 At my request, the \uc2 University of Massachusetts Amherst\uc2  agreed to purchase approximately 15,000 doses of mifepristone. That's enough, that's sufficient to ensure coverage for well over a year.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Washington state already purchasing a three-year supply.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR JAY INSLEE (DEM) (WASHINGTON STATE)\par \par \uc2 Washington state will not allow a judge in Texas to deny the right of Washington women to this safe drug.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Obviously, a lot on the line. Rachel Scott with me here in New York tonight. And is this headed to the Supreme Court?\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) David, it is widely expected to go all the way to the Supreme Court. The bench of conservative supermajority. You have the six conservative justices outnumbering the three liberals. And this would be the first major test of abortion rights since the Supreme Court overturned Roe vs. Wade nearly a year ago, David.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Rachel Scott, always great to have you here with me. Thank you, Rachel.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020230411ej4a00005\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WORLD NEWS TONIGHT WITH DAVID MUIR\b0\par\par\uc2 534 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Tonight, breaking news as we come on the air, the horrific mass shooting at a bank in Louisville. Four dead, nine wounded. Two officers shot, one in the head.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY MASS SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Police say a bank employee armed with a rifle opening fire in the conference room. At least four people killed, several more wounded, including those two police officers, one in critical condition, undergoing surgery. Authorities on the scene within three minutes immediately in a shoot-out with the suspect. Some employees locking themselves in the vault. Governor Andy Beshear clearly shaken today, revealing this is his bank. Two of his close friends among those killed. And just in tonight, a law enforcement source telling ABC News that the suspect left a note to his parents and friends, what he indicated in that note. Trevor Ault in Louisville.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXPELLED LAWMAKER REINSTATED\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Also, just in tonight, that political showdown in Tennessee, drawing national scrutiny. Just days after two Democratic lawmakers were expelled by the Republican-led state assembly, what just happened there. Alex Perez in Nashville tonight.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LEAKED DOCUMENTS INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 We also have new reporting tonight into the damaging leak of top-secret US intelligence. Tonight, what the White House is now acknowledging. They don't know who took the highly classified documents and if there's more to come. And what they reveal, including what US intelligence knows about Russia, its military in this war with Ukraine. And what it knows about Ukraine as well. Terry Moran at the White House.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION PILL LEGAL BATTLE\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 To the issue of abortion tonight. Major developments this evening in the legal battle over nationwide access to the abortion pill. The Justice Department now appealing a federal judge's ruling in Texas, suspending \uc2 FDA\uc2  approval of that drug after being used for more than 20 years in this country across much of the nation. Tonight, the states now stockpiling this drug. Is this headed to the Supreme Court? Rachel Scott reporting.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHINA: "READY TO FIGHT"\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 China warning Taiwan tonight it is, quote, "ready to fight." A record number of Chinese fighter jets flying near the island. And what our correspondent witnessed in Taiwan at a makeshift shooting range. Citizens preparing to defend themselves against China.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MOTHER CHARGED WITH NEGLIGENCE\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Here in the US, the 6-year-old who police say shot his teacher, tonight, his mother is now charged.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 FBI\uc2  WARNING ABOUT CHARGING STATIONS\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Your smartphone, you iPhone. The \uc2 FBI\uc2  warning tonight about where you charge your phone.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Also, tonight, news on those eye drops. The number of cases worsening and what we've now learned. And the record heat coming for millions of Americans, the summer-like temperatures by the end of the week. We'll time it out here.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WORLD NEWS TONIGHT WITH DAVID MUIR\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 From ABC News world headquarters in New York, this is "World News Tonight with David Muir."\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020230411ej4a00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 CALLING IT QUITS? REPORTS: TAYLOR SWIFT & JOE ALWYN BREAK UP AFTER SIX YEARS\b0\par\par\uc2 566 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DUELING RULINGS FROM FEDERAL COURTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION PILL BATTLE\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, PROTESTS, LANGEN, BAPTIST, SCHUMER\par \par \uc2 LEAK, SECURITY, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JUSTICE DEPT INVESTIGATING PENTAGON CLASSIFIED DOCS LEAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UKRAINIAN OFFICIAL CALLS IT RUSSIA'S ATTEMPT TO SOW DOUBT AMONG ITS ALLIES\par \par \uc2 VIOLENCE, ISRAEL, PALESTINE, SYRIA, HECHT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDDLE EAST VIOLENCE AS HOLY DAYS CONVERGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TENSIONS RISE AS ISRAELI MILITARY SAYS SYRIA FIRED ROCKETS\par \par \uc2 POPE FRANCIS, EASTER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THOUSANDS JOIN POPE FRANCIS FOR EASTER MASS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PONTIFF SKIPPED GOOD FRIDAY SERVICE AFTER HEALTH CONCERNS\par \par \uc2 PEARSON, SCHULMAN, QUALLS, JONES, SEXTON, PROTEST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GROWING OUTRAGE OVER EXPULSION OF BLACK LAWMAKERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CALLS FOR THEM TO BE REINSTATED AFTER BEING KICKED OUT OVER PROTEST\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, INDICTMENT\par \par \uc2 TRIAL, WALKER, SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GRAND JURY TO HEAR EVIDENCE IN DEADLY POLICE SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JAYLAND WALKER SHOTS MORE THAN 40 TIMES BY AKRON, OHIO OFFICERS\par \par \uc2 PROFITS, INFLATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FOOD INDUSTRY PROFITS SOAR AS CONSUMERS PAY 