RICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DUELING RULINGS FROM FEDERAL COURTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION PILL BATTLE\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, PROTESTS, LANGEN, BAPTIST, SCHUMER\par \par \uc2 LEAK, SECURITY, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JUSTICE DEPT INVESTIGATING PENTAGON CLASSIFIED DOCS LEAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UKRAINIAN OFFICIAL CALLS IT RUSSIA'S ATTEMPT TO SOW DOUBT AMONG ITS ALLIES\par \par \uc2 VIOLENCE, ISRAEL, PALESTINE, SYRIA, HECHT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDDLE EAST VIOLENCE AS HOLY DAYS CONVERGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TENSIONS RISE AS ISRAELI MILITARY SAYS SYRIA FIRED ROCKETS\par \par \uc2 POPE FRANCIS, EASTER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THOUSANDS JOIN POPE FRANCIS FOR EASTER MASS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PONTIFF SKIPPED GOOD FRIDAY SERVICE AFTER HEALTH CONCERNS\par \par \uc2 PEARSON, SCHULMAN, QUALLS, JONES, SEXTON, PROTEST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GROWING OUTRAGE OVER EXPULSION OF BLACK LAWMAKERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CALLS FOR THEM TO BE REINSTATED AFTER BEING KICKED OUT OVER PROTEST\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, INDICTMENT\par \par \uc2 TRIAL, WALKER, SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GRAND JURY TO HEAR EVIDENCE IN DEADLY POLICE SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JAYLAND WALKER SHOTS MORE THAN 40 TIMES BY AKRON, OHIO OFFICERS\par \par \uc2 PROFITS, INFLATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FOOD INDUSTRY PROFITS SOAR AS CONSUMERS PAY MORE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMERICANS REPORTEDLY SPENDING 7.3 BILLION ON FOOD THIS EASTER SUNDAY\par \par \uc2 WOODS, WITHDRAW, MASTERS\par \par \uc2 LAWSUIT, HAZING, BRENNAN, FRANTZ, GIBSON\par \par \uc2 PRIVACY, TESLA, HASKINS, LAWSUIT, FITZGERALD, STECKLOW\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TESLA PRIVACY CONCERNS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OWNER SEEKS POTENTIAL CLASS ACTION SUIT INVOLVING CAMERAS ON CARS\par \par \uc2 SWIFT, ALWYN, BREAKUP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CALLING IT QUITS?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPORTS: TAYLOR SWIFT & JOE ALWYN BREAK UP AFTER SIX YEARS OF DATING\par \par \uc2 "SUPER MARIO BROS. MOVIE", ROBBINS\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We are back now on "GMA." And it's a winning weekend for the "Super Mario Bros. Movie" smashing records and its box office debut in highlighting the success of videogames hitting the big screen. ABC's Jaclyn Lee is here now with more on that. Jaclyn, good morning.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "THE SUPER MARIO BROS. MOVIE" SCORES AT BOX OFFICE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VIDEO GAME-INSPIRED MOVIES & TV SHOWS DRAWING BIG AUDIENCES\par \par \uc2 JACLYN LEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Whit, a big good morning to you. And the movie is drawing in viewers who grew up playing the game. You know, it has mass appeal for the whole family and we may see more videogames turning into movies.\par \par \uc2 JACLYN LEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, "The Super Mario Bros. Movie" is leveling up the charts.\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM MOVIE, "THE SUPER MARIO BROS. MOVIE"\par \par \uc2 CARTOON VOICEOVER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Look at us. We're adorable.\par \par \uc2 JACLYN LEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Smashing expectations and heading for a record with $195 million US opening, the most ever for a videogame adaption on the big screen.\par \par \uc2 CARTOON VOICEOVER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Come on, Mario, our big adventure begins now.\par \par \uc2 SHAWN ROBBINS (CHIEF ANALYST BOXOFFICE PRO)\par \par \uc2 We see people from multiple generations going out to see these movies.\par \par \uc2 JACLYN LEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The iconic franchise is now passing "Frozen II" as the biggest global opening for an animated film.\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM MOVIE, "FROZEN II"\par \par \uc2 CARTOON VOICEOVER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 My heart.\par \par \uc2 CARTOON VOICEOVER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Oh, my goodness.\par \par \uc2 JACLYN LEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In 2019, the film bringing in $358 million its first weekend. The pick now another videogame to movie success story. Movies like "Sonic the Hedgehog," one and two, "Uncharted," "Angry Birds" and "Dungeons and Dragons."\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM MOVIE\par \par \uc2 CHRIS PINE (ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 If the existing plan fails, I'll make a new plan.\par \par \uc2 SOPHIA LILLIS (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 So, you make plans that fail.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS PINE (ACTOR)\par \par \uc2 No.\par \par \uc2 MICHELLE RODRIGUEZ (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 He also plans to lose.\par \par \uc2 JACLYN LEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) \u8230\'20\'26have attracted some of Hollywood's biggest stars and follows a growing trend over the last two decades.\par \par \uc2 SHAWN ROBBINS (CHIEF ANALYST BOXOFFICE PRO)\par \par \uc2 People are looking for entertainment from movies, but also for videogames. We're seeing that people wanted to experience both of these things in different formats. I think this opens the door for videogame adaptations.\par \par \uc2 JACLYN LEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And it's not just the movies. Streaming has jumped in the action too. Earlier this year, \uc2 HBO\uc2  debuting "The Last of Us." The show becoming the most watch show ever in Latin America and Europe, averaging 30 million viewers across its first six episodes here in the US. As theaters look to rebound to pre-pandemic levels, "Mario's" $368 million opening is sure to give them a boost.\par \par \uc2 SHAWN ROBBINS (CHIEF ANALYST BOXOFFICE PRO)\par \par \uc2 It's generating really strong word-of-mouth. And that really all adds up, especially over a holiday weekend like Easter, to this cultural moment. People want to share this experience together in a movie theater.\par \par \uc2 JACLYN LEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And the highest grossing animated movies of all time include "Toy Story 3," "Frozen" and "Finding Nemo." So, "Mario Bros." has a long way to go. Guys.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Wow. And we're just hearing about Gio Benitez and his trip down memory lane.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) In the '90s, I was crashing those tunnels there. I was like. Yep.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, yes. Thank you so much, Jaclyn. Coming up, our "Play of the Day."\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230509ej490000h\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 GRAND JURY TO HEAR EVIDENCE IN DEADLY POLICE SHOOTING JAYLAND WALKER SHOT MORE THAN 40 TIMES BY AKRON OFFICERS\b0\par\par\uc2 489 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DUELING RULINGS FROM FEDERAL COURTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION PILL BATTLE\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, PROTESTS, LANGEN, BAPTIST, SCHUMER\par \par \uc2 LEAK, SECURITY, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JUSTICE DEPT INVESTIGATING PENTAGON CLASSIFIED DOCS LEAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UKRAINIAN OFFICIAL CALLS IT RUSSIA'S ATTEMPT TO SOW DOUBT AMONG ITS ALLIES\par \par \uc2 VIOLENCE, ISRAEL, PALESTINE, SYRIA, HECHT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDDLE EAST VIOLENCE AS HOLY DAYS CONVERGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TENSIONS RISE AS ISRAELI MILITARY SAYS SYRIA FIRED ROCKETS\par \par \uc2 POPE FRANCIS, EASTER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THOUSANDS JOIN POPE FRANCIS FOR EASTER MASS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PONTIFF SKIPPED GOOD FRIDAY SERVICE AFTER HEALTH CONCERNS\par \par \uc2 PEARSON, SCHULMAN, QUALLS, JONES, SEXTON, PROTEST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GROWING OUTRAGE OVER EXPULSION OF BLACK LAWMAKERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CALLS FOR THEM TO BE REINSTATED AFTER BEING KICKED OUT OVER PROTEST\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, INDICTMENT\par \par \uc2 TRIAL, WALKER, SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GRAND JURY TO HEAR EVIDENCE IN DEADLY POLICE SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JAYLAND WALKER SHOTS MORE THAN 40 TIMES BY AKRON, OHIO OFFICERS\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Janai, turning now to Ohio, where special grand jury this week will be hearing evidence in the deadly police shooting of Jayland Walker. He was shot more than 40 times by eight police officers in Akron following a car and foot chase last year. ABC's Alex Presha joining us now in Columbus, Ohio with the very latest. Alex, good morning.\par \par \uc2 ALEX PRESHA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Whit. Yes, tomorrow all eyes on Ohio are going to be on this summit county special grand jury, as the state's AG office begins making its case against eight officers involved in the fatal shooting of 25-year-old Jayland Walker last June.\par \par \uc2 ALEX PRESHA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Officers initially tried to pull Walker over in the early hours of June 27 for minor violations. And when he refused to stop, a chase started. During that pursuit, police say Walker fired a shot from his car. Officers continued chasing. Walker eventually got out and ran away. He was cornered in a parking lot where officers shot him at least 40 times. He was unarmed at the time. And Walker, who had no criminal record, was deemed a deadly threat by police, who say they found a handgun on the driver's seat. We're learning this grand jury will consider police body camera footage and possibly hear testimony from witnesses from that night.\par \par \uc2 ALEX PRESHA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Now, this case prompted protests in Akron. And in anticipation of the grand jury's decisions, Akron is bracing for more. Security beefed up around the courthouse. The city even setting up an updates website and designating a demonstration zone.\par \par \uc2 ALEX PRESHA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, as for those officers involved, they are back on the force, though they were reassigned to administrative duties. Gio?\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Alex, I know you'll keep following this one for us. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230509ej4900008\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WEATHER\b0\par\par\uc2 625 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DUELING RULINGS FROM FEDERAL COURTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION PILL BATTLE\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, PROTESTS, LANGEN, BAPTIST, SCHUMER\par \par \uc2 LEAK, SECURITY, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JUSTICE DEPT INVESTIGATING PENTAGON CLASSIFIED DOCS LEAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UKRAINIAN OFFICIAL CALLS IT RUSSIA'S ATTEMPT TO SOW DOUBT AMONG ITS ALLIES\par \par \uc2 VIOLENCE, ISRAEL, PALESTINE, SYRIA, HECHT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDDLE EAST VIOLENCE AS HOLY DAYS CONVERGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TENSIONS RISE AS ISRAELI MILITARY SAYS SYRIA FIRED ROCKETS\par \par \uc2 POPE FRANCIS, EASTER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THOUSANDS JOIN POPE FRANCIS FOR EASTER MASS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PONTIFF SKIPPED GOOD FRIDAY SERVICE AFTER HEALTH CONCERNS\par \par \uc2 PEARSON, SCHULMAN, QUALLS, JONES, SEXTON, PROTEST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GROWING OUTRAGE OVER EXPULSION OF BLACK LAWMAKERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CALLS FOR THEM TO BE REINSTATED AFTER BEING KICKED OUT OVER PROTEST\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, INDICTMENT\par \par \uc2 TRIAL, WALKER, SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GRAND JURY TO HEAR EVIDENCE IN DEADLY POLICE SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JAYLAND WALKER SHOTS MORE THAN 40 TIMES BY AKRON, OHIO OFFICERS\par \par \uc2 PROFITS, INFLATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FOOD INDUSTRY PROFITS SOAR AS CONSUMERS PAY MORE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMERICANS REPORTEDLY SPENDING 7.3 BILLION ON FOOD THIS EASTER SUNDAY\par \par \uc2 WOODS, WITHDRAW, MASTERS\par \par \uc2 LAWSUIT, HAZING, BRENNAN, FRANTZ, GIBSON\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And Somara Theodore is here with the weather. And you were showing us with some numbers earlier that are looking pretty good.\par \par \uc2 SOMARA THEODORE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, you know, it's really exciting. We've got Easter Sunday, everyone is going to church, brunch. You've got the babies who are going to dress in their cute little Sunday best and, hopefully, some little bunny outfits. This is what we've got.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EASTER CITIES\par \par \uc2 SOMARA THEODORE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's not a bad Sunday at all, might I add. If you head out towards, Oregon, we're looking at temperatures at the low 50s. Egg Harbor, New Jersey, 55. Baskett, Kentucky, you see what we did here, 67. Peep Lake, we're looking at temperatures in the mid to upper 40s.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: APRIL CHILL\u8230\'20\'26 FOR NOW\par \par \uc2 SOMARA THEODORE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, while it is going to be a mild afternoon, it's a cold start. We have freeze alerts through the northeast. Roanoke, 40 degrees, into the 30s in Reading, Pennsylvania.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUMMER, IS THAT YOU?\par \par \uc2 SOMARA THEODORE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But we are warming. What an exciting forecast. We've got to be outside in DC on Thursday, in the 80s, New York, 82 on Thursday. That's a look at the weather across the country, let's see what's going on a little closer to home.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NATIONAL MAP\par \par \uc2 SOMARA THEODORE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, we're back now. And so, it's going to be a great Easter Sunday as far as temperatures go. But I can't wait till Friday. Much of the country's are going to be warming up and we deserve it.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And I have to...\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Whit, show us?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) \u8230\'20\'26bust out the tank top.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) No.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right? Sun's up, (inaudible).\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I was going to say, show us your warm weather dance. Oh, gosh.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) No. But we'll leave it right there. Thank you very much, Somara. And apologies for that image.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COMING UP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRIVACY CONCERNS?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Coming up here on "GMA," the \uc2 Tesla\uc2  owner seeking a potential class action suit against the company. Why he's accusing it of violating customer privacy.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPER MARIO BROTHERS\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And super success for "Super Mario Bros." How videogames turned movies are scoring big with audiences. Stick around. You're watching "GMA."\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230509ej490000e\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 TESLA PRIVACY CONCERNS OWNER SEEKS POTENTIAL CLASS ACTION SUIT INVOLVING CAMERAS ON CARS\b0\par\par\uc2 739 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DUELING RULINGS FROM FEDERAL COURTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION PILL BATTLE\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, PROTESTS, LANGEN, BAPTIST, SCHUMER\par \par \uc2 LEAK, SECURITY, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JUSTICE DEPT INVESTIGATING PENTAGON CLASSIFIED DOCS LEAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UKRAINIAN OFFICIAL CALLS IT RUSSIA'S ATTEMPT TO SOW DOUBT AMONG ITS ALLIES\par \par \uc2 VIOLENCE, ISRAEL, PALESTINE, SYRIA, HECHT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDDLE EAST VIOLENCE AS HOLY DAYS CONVERGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TENSIONS RISE AS ISRAELI MILITARY SAYS SYRIA FIRED ROCKETS\par \par \uc2 POPE FRANCIS, EASTER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THOUSANDS JOIN POPE FRANCIS FOR EASTER MASS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PONTIFF SKIPPED GOOD FRIDAY SERVICE AFTER HEALTH CONCERNS\par \par \uc2 PEARSON, SCHULMAN, QUALLS, JONES, SEXTON, PROTEST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GROWING OUTRAGE OVER EXPULSION OF BLACK LAWMAKERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CALLS FOR THEM TO BE REINSTATED AFTER BEING KICKED OUT OVER PROTEST\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, INDICTMENT\par \par \uc2 TRIAL, WALKER, SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GRAND JURY TO HEAR EVIDENCE IN DEADLY POLICE SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JAYLAND WALKER SHOTS MORE THAN 40 TIMES BY AKRON, OHIO OFFICERS\par \par \uc2 PROFITS, INFLATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FOOD INDUSTRY PROFITS SOAR AS CONSUMERS PAY MORE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMERICANS REPORTEDLY SPENDING 7.3 BILLION ON FOOD THIS EASTER SUNDAY\par \par \uc2 WOODS, WITHDRAW, MASTERS\par \par \uc2 LAWSUIT, HAZING, BRENNAN, FRANTZ, GIBSON\par \par \uc2 PRIVACY, TESLA, HASKINS, LAWSUIT, FITZGERALD, STECKLOW\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TESLA PRIVACY CONCERNS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OWNER SEEKS POTENTIAL CLASS ACTION SUIT INVOLVING CAMERAS ON CARS\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Welcome back to "GMA" now and the privacy concerns being raised involving those cameras on \uc2 Tesla\uc2  cars. A car owner filing a potential class action suit after a Reuters report published Thursday said a small group of former employees described sharing sensitive customer videos internally.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, a major automaker is facing a lawsuit in California. A \uc2 Tesla\uc2  owner filing a complaint, accusing the company of allegedly violating California privacy laws among other claims.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POTENTIAL CLASS ACTION LAWSUIT\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The potential class action lawsuit alleges that between 2019 and 2022, by virtue of this defective system, \uc2 Tesla\uc2  employees accessed and circulated recordings of \uc2 Tesla\uc2  customers in private and embarrassing situations without their consent.\par \par \uc2 JACK FITZGERALD (PARTNER FITZGERALD JOSEPH LLP)\par \par \uc2 It's not okay for \uc2 Tesla\uc2  to be using that information in ways that it's promised not to use.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The lawsuit filed Friday comes after a Reuters report published Thursday in which a small group of former \uc2 Tesla\uc2  employees, who are nameless, said they internally shared private photos and videos captured by \uc2 Tesla\uc2 's car cameras without customer's consent.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER TESLA EMPLOYEES\par \par \uc2 STEVE STECKLOW (PULITZER PRIZE-WINNING INVESTIGATIVE REPORTER REUTERS)\par \par \uc2 To relieve boredom, a lot of these data labelers would share these videos with each other.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REUTERS REPORT\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Reuters said in its report that it wasn't able to obtain any of the shared material and the former employee said they hadn't saved the alleged private information. Examples of the shared materials mentioned in the lawsuit were also referenced without evidence. And the lawsuit does not allege the plaintiff's \uc2 Tesla\uc2  camera was access.\par \par \uc2 JACK FITZGERALD (PARTNER FITZGERALD JOSEPH LLP)\par \par \uc2 He didn't consent to, you know, images of his family being available to \uc2 Tesla\uc2  employees to circulate around the office or comment on. Nobody consented to that.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) \uc2 Tesla\uc2  did not immediately respond to ABC's request for comment. But earlier this year, \uc2 Tesla\uc2  releasing a detailed look at their privacy practices, which included explaining when the cameras are enabled and how information is stored.\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM TESLA VIDEO\par \par \uc2 VIDEO VOICEOVER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 The cameras will only record if you opt in. And the recordings are saved in your vehicle, not on \uc2 Tesla\uc2  servers.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TESLA CUSTOMER PRIVACY NOTICE\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) \uc2 Tesla\uc2  also saying, recording preferences can be updated at any time. \uc2 Tesla\uc2 's customer privacy notice states, "Unless we receive the data as a result of a safety event, vehicle collision or airbag deployment, camera recordings remain anonymous and are not linked to you or your vehicle."\par \par \uc2 CAROLINE HASKINS (DATA PRIVACY EXPERT & SENIOR REPORTER "INSIDER")\par \par \uc2 That's one of the trade-offs that people have to consider when they're getting a car that has one of these experimental features, like autopilot or self-driving.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And a judge still has to review the complaint and decide whether it's a proper class action lawsuit. Janai?\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You know, that will be an interesting to watch.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230509ej490000f\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 GOOD MORNING AMERICA\b0\par\par\uc2 476 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DUELING RULINGS FROM FEDERAL COURTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION PILL BATTLE\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Good morning America. Abortion pill battle. Both sides of the issue fired up following dueling rulings from federal courts. A Texas judge suspending the drug's approval, one in Washington protecting access. The critical decision expected this week and how it's all likely to end up in the Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ESCALATING VIOLENCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AIR STRIKES\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Airstrikes. The escalating violence between Israel and Syria. The rising tensions as hundreds of thousands of people converge on Jerusalem for the holy days of three faiths.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POPE FRANCIS DELIVERS MASS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EASTER MESSAGE\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Easter message. \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  delivers mass in St. Peter's Square. His words to worshipers in the world as he fights off health issues.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TOP SECRET INFORMATION LEAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS BREACH\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Classified documents breach. The clearer picture we are getting about top-secret information winding up on social media and the urgent such for answers.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TENNESSEE LAWMAKERS OUSTED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GROWING OUTRAGE\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Growing outrage following two black state lawmakers ousted from the Tennessee legislature.\par \par \uc2 SUPPORTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 We the people hired Justin J. Pearson, and we didn't fire him.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 The push starting tomorrow to get them back in office.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW THIS MORNING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HAZING LAWSUIT\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Hazing lawsuit. A former student pledge says he nearly died from being forced to consume alcohol and drugs in amounts that would kill most people. His family now speaking out.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SQUEEZED AT THE GROCERY STORE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PROFITS AND PRICES\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Profits and prices. Consumer squeezed at the grocery store while major food companies rake in record profits. Plus, the double whammy we could be seeing just ahead.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING OVERNIGHT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TAYLOR SWIFT SPLITS WITH JOE ALWYN\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Breaking overnight. The Taylor Swift split, reportedly breaking up with Joe Alwyn in the middle of her sold-out "Eras" tour. What we're learning this morning.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RECORD-BREAKING WEEKEND\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPER SHOWING!\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And super showing for the "Super Mar Brothers" movie, ready to score a record-breaking weekend. What's behind its success?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUNDAY, APRIL 9\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 Live from ABC News in New York, this is good morning America.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And good morning, America. And happy Easter if you are celebrating today. We do have a lot to cover here. And just a short time ago, \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  holding Easter mass for tens of thousands of people in St. Peter's Square and delivered his annual message. We'll have more on that just ahead.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And we can't wait for that.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230509ej4900001\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 GROWING OUTRAGE OVER EXPULSION OF BLACK LAWMAKERS CALLS FOR THEM TO BE REINSTATED AFTER BEING KICKED OUT OVER PROTEST\b0\par\par\uc2 637 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DUELING RULINGS FROM FEDERAL COURTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION PILL BATTLE\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, PROTESTS, LANGEN, BAPTIST, SCHUMER\par \par \uc2 LEAK, SECURITY, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JUSTICE DEPT INVESTIGATING PENTAGON CLASSIFIED DOCS LEAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UKRAINIAN OFFICIAL CALLS IT RUSSIA'S ATTEMPT TO SOW DOUBT AMONG ITS ALLIES\par \par \uc2 VIOLENCE, ISRAEL, PALESTINE, SYRIA, HECHT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDDLE EAST VIOLENCE AS HOLY DAYS CONVERGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TENSIONS RISE AS ISRAELI MILITARY SAYS SYRIA FIRED ROCKETS\par \par \uc2 POPE FRANCIS, EASTER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THOUSANDS JOIN POPE FRANCIS FOR EASTER MASS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PONTIFF SKIPPED GOOD FRIDAY SERVICE AFTER HEALTH CONCERNS\par \par \uc2 PEARSON, SCHULMAN, QUALLS, JONES, SEXTON, PROTEST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GROWING OUTRAGE OVER EXPULSION OF BLACK LAWMAKERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CALLS FOR THEM TO BE REINSTATED AFTER BEING KICKED OUT OVER PROTEST\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Back home now, as some voters in Tennessee react with outrage to the Republican led expulsion of two black lawmakers from the state House of Representatives. ABC's Faith Abubey is live in Nashville this morning as the push to get them back in office starts tomorrow for at least one of them. Faith, good morning.\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning to you, Janai. Justin Pearson and Justin Jones may no longer be state lawmakers here in Tennessee, but Jones tells me he's still representing his constituents in exile.\par \par \uc2 SUPPORTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 We the people hired Justin J. Pearson, and we didn't fire him.\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Growing community outrage over the expulsion of two Democrats, former State Representatives Justin Pearson and Justin Jones from the Tennessee state legislature.\par \par \uc2 PHYLLIS QUALLS (FORMER CONSULTANT JUSTIN JONES)\par \par \uc2 We have won without representation. Truly, taxation without representation.\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tens of thousands of voters now without an elected representative in the Tennessee statehouse.\par \par \uc2 CAMERON SEXTON (SPEAKER OF THE TENNESSEE HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES)\par \par \uc2 Expelled from the House of Representatives.\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The two lawmakers expelled after ignoring warnings from the state House Republican leadership about protesting in the chamber in the wake of the Covenant School shooting in Nashville.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 No action. No peace. No action. No peace.\par \par \uc2 CAMERON SEXTON (SPEAKER OF THE TENNESSEE HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES)\par \par \uc2 We have decorum. We have process. We have procedures. Imagine if that happened on the congressional floor hearing the State of the Union Address and people took over in front of him, pulled out a bullhorn?\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Representative Gloria Johnson, who joined Pearson and Jones, survived her expulsion by one vote.\par \par \uc2 JUSTIN JONES (FORMER MEMBER TENNESSEE HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES)\par \par \uc2 This has only empowered and given deeper conviction for the need to act.\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) C.J. (Inaudible) moved to the district 2 years ago from Guam and cast her first ballot as a registered voter for Jones.\par \par \uc2 SUPPORTER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 I'm angry.\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The community campaign to reinstate Jones and Pearson gaining momentum.\par \par \uc2 JIM SCHULMAN (VICE MAYOR NASHVILLE)\par \par \uc2 We're getting hundreds of emails and lots of phone calls, and people want to send them right back up.\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The Nashville Metro Council will consider suspending its rules on Monday in order to expedite the process to send Jones back to the House.\par \par \uc2 SUPPORTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 I would like for him to be reinstated. No one could take his place.\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And Pearson's district is considering making the same move to get him back in his seat. Now, regardless of either of these special appointments go through, both of these men do have an opportunity to run in special elections in their districts. The governor will announce those dates. Janai?\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Faith, thank you for that update.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230509ej4900006\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 DUELING RULINGS IN ABORTION PILL BATTLE FUTURE OF DRUG IN LIMBO AFTER OPPOSING RULINGS\b0\par\par\uc2 666 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DUELING RULINGS FROM FEDERAL COURTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION PILL BATTLE\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, PROTESTS, LANGEN, BAPTIST, SCHUMER\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But we start here with the latest on those two contradictory rulings on the abortion pill.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DUELING RULINGS IN ABORTION PILL BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FUTURE OF DRUG IN LIMBO AFTER OPPOSING RULINGS FROM TEXAS & WASHINGTON JUDGES\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) A Trump-appointed federal judge in Texas suspending its approval decades after the \uc2 FDA\uc2  deemed it safe. An Obama-appointed judge in Washington state directing federal officials to keep the drug available in at least 17 states.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And just hours after the Texas ruling, the Biden administration filed an appeal of the decision with it looking likely that it's headed for the Supreme Court. For what that all means right now, let's go to ABC's Elizabeth Schulze who's live at the White House this morning. Elizabeth, good morning to you.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning to you, Janai. This is a high-stakes legal and political battle over abortion rights as the White House argues that the ruling from a Texas judge undermines the \uc2 FDA\uc2 's ability to make decisions based on science, not politics.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, protests around the country now that access to the most widely used abortion medication in America is in the hands of a federal appeals court. The Justice Department appealing a decision out late Friday by conservative federal judge in Texas suspending the \uc2 FDA\uc2 's approval of mifepristone, a pill used in more than half of us abortions. Attorney General \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  arguing the Texas ruling "overturns the \uc2 FDA\uc2 's expert judgment, rendered over two decades ago, that mifepristone the press stone is safe and effective."\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH LANGEN MD (UNIVERSITY OF MICHIGAN DEPARTMENT OF OBSTETRICS)\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FDA\uc2  has continued to, if anything, overly monitor this drug to make sure that it continues to be safe and effective.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) A competing decision Friday from a federal judge in Washington state determined mifepristone should stay available, making it likely the Supreme Court will ultimately weigh in.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION ACCESS UNDER FIRE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STAGE SET FOR SUPREME COURT BATTLE OVER ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But this week, the conservative Fifth Circuit Court of Appeals in New Orleans is expected to weigh in on the Texas case, deciding if the abortion pill should remain available for now as the case winds through the courts. The advocacy group \uc2 Alliance Defending Freedom\uc2  filed the Texas lawsuit.\par \par \uc2 ERIK BAPTIST (SENIOR COUNSEL ALLIANCE DEFENDING FREEDOM)\par \par \uc2 We're happy to obtain that preliminary ruling from the district court, but we know obviously this is not the last stage and the last word on this issue. And we're ready to go to the next stage.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The White House and Democrats are vowing to fight the Texas ruling.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION RULING REACTION\par \par \uc2 SENATOR CHUCK SCHUMER (DEM-NY) (SENATE MAJORITY LEADER)\par \par \uc2 Republicans are once again showing how wildly out of step they are with the law. And they are making clear, once again, they are making clear the real Republican objective, your body, our choice.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS ABORTION PILL RULING\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) If it stands, even Americans and states where abortion is legal wouldn't have access to the medication. And 40% of abortion clinics nationwide only offer abortion pills.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) President Biden and Democrats are loudly speaking out against the Texas ruling this weekend and urging Congress to pass legislation to protect abortion rights. But Republicans have mostly stayed quiet. Abortion was, of course, a galvanizing issue in the midterm elections, helping to turn out Democratic voters. Whit?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And as you noted, so much at stake. Elizabeth Schulze, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230509ej4900002\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 JUSTICE DEPT INVESTIGATING PENTAGON LEAK UKRAINIAN OFFICIAL CALLS IT RUSSIA'S ATTEMPT TO SOW DOUBT AMONG ALLIES\b0\par\par\uc2 403 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DUELING RULINGS FROM FEDERAL COURTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION PILL BATTLE\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, PROTESTS, LANGEN, BAPTIST, SCHUMER\par \par \uc2 LEAK, SECURITY, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JUSTICE DEPT INVESTIGATING PENTAGON CLASSIFIED DOCS LEAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UKRAINIAN OFFICIAL CALLS IT RUSSIA'S ATTEMPT TO SOW DOUBT AMONG ITS ALLIES\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to the new leaks of national security documents. Images of secret papers posted on social media leading to questions about damage to US interests abroad. And just who's responsible? ABC's Patrick Reevell joins us now from London with the very latest. Patrick, good morning.\par \par \uc2 PATRICK REEVELL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Whit. Yes, these leaks have shaken US allies. And they, like American officials, are now scrambling to work out how serious this breach is.\par \par \uc2 PATRICK REEVELL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The Justice Department is investigating how dozens of classified US intelligence documents that contain top-secret information, from the war in Ukraine, to China, to Iran and North Korea, have been leaked and then posted online. Photos of the classified documents were posted to social media, some posted weeks ago in early March. Some seems to have markings identifying them as from the Office of the Joints Chiefs. One documented dated March 2nd appears to come from the CIA's daily intelligence summary provided to senior leaders. And many appear to be photos of printed PowerPoint slides of the military situation in Ukraine as of March.\par \par \uc2 PATRICK REEVELL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) They describe the state of the war, Ukrainian troop numbers, western weapons delivery schedules as well as casualty figures. And some of the documents back up assessments of the war that were already publicly known. One US official told ABC News the documents appear no longer relevant to the battlefield and have limited intelligence value and that some have been altered.\par \par \uc2 PATRICK REEVELL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But those comments don't address the wider scope of the leak. Now, a top advisor to Ukraine's president has warned the leaks are a Russian attempt to sow discord and doubt among Ukraine's allies. But the most urgent focus for US officials now is really finding the source of this leak and understanding if there's more to come. Gio?\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Patrick, thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230509ej4900003\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 THE POWERHOUSE ROUNDTABLE\b0\par\par\uc2 3,691 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: This Week\par \uc2 THWK\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2023 American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THIS WEEK\par \par \uc2 TRUSTY, BARR, TRUMP, INDICTMENT, BRAGG\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE TRUMP INDICTMENT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP PLEADS NOT GUILTY TO 34 COUNTS OF FALSIFYING RECORDS\par \par \uc2 PEARSON, JONES, TN, STATEHOUSE, PROTEST, GUNS\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP FROM THURSDAY\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, POLL, 2024, TENNESSEE, PEARSON, JONES, ABORTION\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 There is no question that the President and I are gonna stand with the women of America and do everything we can to make ensure that women have ability to make decisions about their healthcare, their reproductive healthcare. It is contrary to makes for good public health policy to allow courts and politicians to tell the FDA what it should do.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE POWERHOUSE ROUNDTABLE\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  Friday evening, speaking as the Biden administration announced they would appeal an unprecedented ruling that reversed an FDA approval of the abortion pill. The case is likely to wind up at the Supreme Court. Let's bring in the Roundtable, former New Jersey Governor \uc2 Chris Christie\uc2 , Democratic strategist and CNN political commentator Karen Finney, ABC News political director Rick Klein, and "Washington Post Live" anchor Leanne Caldwell. Thank you all for being here.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP PLEADS NOT GUILTY TO 34 COUNTS OF FALSIFYING RECORDS\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I - want to start, we're, we're gonna get to the - court case, but I want to start with this indictment and the effect on, on our politics. Our new poll this morning, Governor Christie, shows actually significant downgrading - of Trump's favorability rating in view of this case since the indictment was unsealed. Take a look at, take a look at this, the effect on Independents. So, the question, should he have been (inaudible) the arrest in the unsealing of that indictment? Forty percent said of Independents said yes. After, 54 percent. Should he suspend his campaign? About the same before, now more than half saying he should. I mean, what do you, - what's your take on this?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHANGE AMONG INDEPENDENTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABC/IPSOS POLL: MORE AMERICANS SAY TRUMP SHOULD DROP OUT\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's kind of what I said a few weeks ago here, Jon. Like, no matter what he says and his people say, being indicted is not good for a political candidate. Like, that's just, you know, he can get short-term bump among certain parts of our own party. But in the end, it's not good to be indicted. Now, we're not gonna see a trial here probably until early 2024, and so we won't see what the result is. But he has other things, you know, it's kind of like trying to land at Newark Airport on a Friday.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You know, you got a bunch of planes circling and you don't know when exactly they're gonna land, and if they land, when they're gonna have a gate, you know? But it's coming. And being indicted, the public does still look at that and say that's not what should be happening to a national leader.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And - you heard, you heard Barr, he, he seemed to think that there will be further indictments, that, that Jack Smith doesn't do all this and decide not to indict.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SPECIAL COUNSEL BUILDS CASES ON JAN 6TH, CLASSIFIED DOCS\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Look, I, I think that when, when you bring over a war crimes tribunal prosecutor to be the Special Counsel, those are generally not known as low-key men and women.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) They're known as prosecutors typically who have blinders on and see that they have a job to do and they're gonna do it. Now, I don't know what Jack Smith will or won't do, but that was not a compromiser that they brought over here. That was not somebody who they brought over to try to plead the case out.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, and Karen?\par \par \uc2 KAREN FINNEY (DEMOCRATIC STRATEGIST)\par \par \uc2 Yeah, I was just gonna say, I thought a couple things were interesting, and Trump also didn't do himself any favors with that speech, I'll call it that, after the, the indictment, after he'd gone in for the indictment. It reminded so many people of exactly why they did not vote for him in 2020, in terms of the chaos, the attacks on democracy, attacking the Judge and his family. I think it also showed, though, the poll, the growing division in this country. It's like the one third of the country that is for Trump is in their own MAGA bubble.\par \par \uc2 KAREN FINNEY (DEMOCRATIC STRATEGIST)\par \par \uc2 And the rest of the country, a growing number of Independents, a majority of Democrats are living in the actual reality that says they saw through. They didn't just know that being indicted wasn't good, they saw through, whatever people said about the strength of the case or not, the American people got it, that he - I think they understood that here these actions were taken to try to subvert an election, essentially, to withhold evidence that the American people should have had when they went to the polls in 2016.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, it was interesting because there was like, virtually no change among Democrats or Republicans. They think of Trump what they think of Trump. All the change was on Independents. But, but Rick, does that mean we're headed towards a scenario where Trump is actually maybe even stronger in the Republican primary but weaker in a, in a general election?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABC/IPSOS POLL: 53% SAY TRUMP'S ACTIONS 'INTENTIONALLY ILLEGAL'\par \par \uc2 RICK KLEIN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Look, if you're looking to, to piece that argument together, this poll is a big piece of evidence in that direction. Republicans are in his corner, although a large number are still saying they're not sure, which might be that, where they're parking support 'cause they don't want to say they're behind but they don't want to say they're against him. People are tuned into this. And I think that number - among Independents is really telling.\par \par \uc2 RICK KLEIN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And the fact that a clear majority of the country thinks he did something wrong intentionally, that is very bad news if you're going into a general election campaign. And we just heard the former Attorney General say, it might be that this strengthens him politically among Republicans inside the Republican primary at the same time that it makes him significantly weaker with the, with the whole American public, especially 'cause we're just beginning to see even what this case is, much less what the other cases might be.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But, but do Republicans charge into a general election like this, with a candidate who the evidence seems to suggest can't win a general election?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MANY IN GOP RALLY BEHIND TRUMP, INCLUDING SOME 2024 RIVALS\par \par \uc2 LEIGH ANN CALDWELL (WASHINGTON POST LIVE ANCHOR)\par \par \uc2 Well, it depends on what Republican primary voters think. And what Karen mentioned, she said there's always had been a third of the - of the public who has backed Trump. What this poll showed me, which was really interesting, that third has shrunk since his overall approval rating was just 25 percent, which is the lowest we've seen in a very long time for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . And so, perhaps, even that group is shrinking. And what this poll also confirms to me is what Republican and Democratic sources have been telling me all week, and that is that this does, for some reason, strengthen Trump in the primary, but it really weakens him in the general against President Biden.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And that doesn't seem sustainable as a primary candidate. Hey, I'm the guy that...\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Look, it strengthens you in the primary when you have no opponents. Okay? I mean, basically, it's Nikki Haley and \uc2 Vivek Ramaswamy\uc2  right now.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) He's got that guy in Florida that, that looks like...\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And Asa Hutchinson, right? Well, but again, he's not a candidate yet, not really saying much of anything.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah. Right.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And so, look, campaigns, and Karen knows this, campaigns don't happen until they happen.\par \par \uc2 KAREN FINNEY (DEMOCRATIC STRATEGIST)\par \par \uc2 That's right.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, and they are a human dynamic. Right? They are people interacting and they often say and do things that aren't according to script. And that's why people show up and watch.\par \par \uc2 GUEST (THE POWERHOUSE ROUNDTABLE)\par \par \uc2 Right.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And so, what's gonna happen here with Trump is that, his act is going to remain the same. He's got no other act. Karen mentioned the speech the other night, you know, that sounded, to me, like a guy that you'd, you know, that you'd encounter in a bar who you wind up sitting next to and he's griping to you about his bad divorce, I mean, and you're like, well, what are you doing now? And he's like, well, let me tell you what she did next.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP SLAMS DA BRAGG, JUDGE MERCHAN AFTER ARRAIGNMENT\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, you know, it's, that's what it sounded like to me. I don't think most elections, Jon, in my experience, are won on the past. They're won or lost on the future, and that's gonna be his problem when the primary comes, because the smart primary candidate will be talking about the future and ignoring \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , except for when he pops up. And then like wacko ball, you hit him down.\par \par \uc2 KAREN FINNEY (DEMOCRATIC STRATEGIST)\par \par \uc2 But also, we got signs this week that 2024 is again going to be about protecting democracy and freedom. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  attacking democracy and our Democratic institutions, what happened at Wisconsin. People said no, we're gonna stand up for reproductive freedom. We're gonna stand against gerrymandering which is basically subverting the voices of the people. What we saw and we know that was a big driver of the electorate in 2022, we know that some of the Independents, even Moderate Republicans polls showed voted for Democrats.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PROGRESSIVE SURGE IN WISCONSIN, CHICAGO ELECTIONS\par \par \uc2 KAREN FINNEY (DEMOCRATIC STRATEGIST)\par \par \uc2 They cited January 6th as one of the reasons. So, these attacks on democracy cited January 6th as one of recent attacks on democracy are going to continue to motivate. I was particularly thinking about what happened in Tennessee, the, whether it's at local level where these super majorities are overreaching, whether it is the decisions like we had on Friday with mifepristone, taking away bodily autonomy and reproductive freedom from people.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So...\par \par \uc2 KAREN FINNEY (DEMOCRATIC STRATEGIST)\par \par \uc2 It's going to continue to drive the electorate. And Trump doesn't have the answer to that.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WI SUPREME COURT RACE SHOWS POWER OF ABORTION RIGHTS\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And - Rick, Wisconsin was a big wakeup call for Republicans on that. I mean, - you had the, obviously it's technically a partisan race, but the - the Judge, the candidates supported by Democrats, winning by 11 points in Wisconsin. And then, after that, you have this decision on the abortion pill.\par \par \uc2 RICK KLEIN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah. Think about what it means to win by double digits in Wisconsin. I mean, when \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  won that state, he won it by about point-seven percent. When Biden flipped it, though, I think it was point-six percent. So to win by 11 percent is insane.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Eleven points. Yeah.\par \par \uc2 RICK KLEIN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That is, that is an absolute blowout. And it was clear. The abortion ruling for the 19th century was either going to or not going to go into effect, in all likelihood, based on this. And yes, the, I think we are still only...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) In the 19th century?\par \par \uc2 RICK KLEIN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's right. We're still only beginning to understand the, the real potency of, of the overturning of Roe v. Wade from more than a year ago. The idea that we're gonna have another abortion related case before the Supreme Court potentially, after the ruling out of the, out of Texas, it brings it back front and center. And I think Karen is right to tie it together with the battles over democracy. These are the kind of stakes that are shaking up early. Governor Christie's right, we're a long way from an actual campaign. But if you look at the atmosphere, if you look at the issues that are going to be driver voters in a major way, these are a lot of things that Democrats like the playing field on.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, and Republicans will tell, the Dobbs decision hurt them in - the midterms.\par \par \uc2 LEIGH ANN CALDWELL (WASHINGTON POST LIVE ANCHOR)\par \par \uc2 Absolutely.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, how big is this decision on the abortion pill?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ACCESS TO ABORTION PILL IN DOUBT AFTER DUELING COURT RULINGS\par \par \uc2 LEIGH ANN CALDWELL (WASHINGTON POST LIVE ANCHOR)\par \par \uc2 Well, their silence is deafening. We are hearing...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The Republicans?\par \par \uc2 LEIGH ANN CALDWELL (WASHINGTON POST LIVE ANCHOR)\par \par \uc2 The Republican silence is deafening. We've heard a lot from Democrats decrying this, this case, and you have not heard a lot from Republicans. Even Republican sources that I have reached out to in preparation for this show, asking them to talk to me about this case and what the applications are politically, and I've heard nothing. And so, that is a real big sign that Republicans are actually worried about this. It was abortion and directly, in some instances, in abortion and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  who lost Republicans, the Senate in 2022 and gave Republicans a very slim majority in the House when they were expected to blow out...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But we have a Republican sitting over there who usually isn't very silent.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hi, how are you? Good to see ya.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, what's, so, what's, what is your take?\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) No. I'd - say a few things, 'cause there's a lot in there from what everybody said. First off, on, on the, on the decision itself, I've always been of the view, I'm pro-life, but I've always been of the view that these things should be decided by the states. And state-by-state these decisions should be made, so I don't favor federalizing this in any way. Whether it's by a federal court or whether it's by the Congress or whether it's by some presidential executive order, I think this should be a state-by-state determination. And we saw in Wisconsin that people made decisions.\par \par \uc2 GUEST (THE POWERHOUSE ROUNDTABLE)\par \par \uc2 Yep.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We saw that in Kansas...\par \par \uc2 KAREN FINNEY (DEMOCRATIC STRATEGIST)\par \par \uc2 Yeah.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...that folks made decisions, right? So, these are gonna be state-by-state decisions are made and we should respect those decisions that are made by people in those states. And I think that's what Republicans should be saying, that these should be state-by-state decisions. I'd also say about gerrymandering that where you stand depends on where you sit, you know? In New York, the gerrymandering was so bad that you didn't even need a Republican majority on the State Court of Appeals, that six out of seven were Democrats and they overturned the New York map.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And now what do you see? You see Kathy Hochul in the legislature trying to change the rules to give the Supreme Court, they don't like that (inaudible) not the Supreme Court but the Court of Appeals in New York, which is their highest court, they want to give them new members and other authority so they can overturn and bring back their gerrymandering map. Both parties engage in that kind of stuff.\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, in the end, Jon, I'd say this, that I still think that while Dobbs had an impact on 2022, no question, the bigger impact were the \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  endorsements and the awful candidates, whether it was Kari Lake or \uc2 Herschel Walker\uc2  or \uc2 Tim Michels\uc2  in Wisconsin or Mastriano in Pennsylvania. Those were the candidates who lost and they were \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's candidates.\par \par \uc2 KAREN FINNEY (DEMOCRATIC STRATEGIST)\par \par \uc2 But they were also election deniers. And the election denier...\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 KAREN FINNEY (DEMOCRATIC STRATEGIST)\par \par \uc2 ...is the one who lost in Wisconsin, as you know. And I'll tell you what, when you're looking at Tennessee, boy, that is microcosm of what is happening in this country. The, the older fellas in the Tennessee legislature, they did not know what to do with those younger legislators who represent the changing America. We are younger...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Those guys are gonna come back.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JONES, PEARSON OUSTED FOR TN FLOOR PROTEST; JOHNSON SPARED\par \par \uc2 KAREN FINNEY (DEMOCRATIC STRATEGIST)\par \par \uc2 Yes, they are. We are younger.\par \par \uc2 RICK KLEIN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) With a much bigger platform.\par \par \uc2 KAREN FINNEY (DEMOCRATIC STRATEGIST)\par \par \uc2 We are Black, we are Brown, we are female.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 KAREN FINNEY (DEMOCRATIC STRATEGIST)\par \par \uc2 And they had, I mean, and to lecture them about decorum and to be...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 KAREN FINNEY (DEMOCRATIC STRATEGIST)\par \par \uc2 ...so unaware of the racial implications of the way they were being treated and the firestorm that they sent off that is now I think awakening. In Wisconsin, it was younger voters who actually came out in record numbers that, we will have more younger voters than older voters in 2024. And I think if the GOP doesn't get with it on, whether it's guns, climate, reproductive freedom, they're gonna be in big trouble.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BIDEN DOES NOT COMMENT ON CHAOS SURROUNDING TRUMP\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But Jon, look, but in the end, what we've seen over and over again in national elections is, the economy is what determines what goes on. And if there are huge, foreign challenges and crises, which are both here in Ukraine and over the rising with North Korea, with China, with Iran. And so, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  still sits in the low 40s. He still got a third of the people, just a third when you talk about ratings, who say they think he deserves to be reelected, in the, in the latest poll.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But, but you think he still beats \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in a general election?\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I think he's, I think \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is the only Republican he can beat. I don't think he could beat any other Republican who can get nominated. And, and but, the economy will still be the thing that will determine this. And I think we have more bumps coming to us ahead from the banking problem and other things that have gone on.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But Rick, we're almost out of time, but the, but the politics on abortion have changed.\par \par \uc2 RICK KLEIN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I mean, you look at polling, it's changed dramatically in the last 10 years.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WI SUPREME COURT RACE SHOWS POWER OF ABORTION RIGHTS\par \par \uc2 RICK KLEIN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah. And, and right now what, what the Republicans need to recognize is that there's a majority, a very strong majority of the country that wants to see abortion accessible in at least some circumstances, if not most circumstances. And things flipped in terms of the politics around this where it became a motivating issue for Democrats, for Liberals.\par \par \uc2 KAREN FINNEY (DEMOCRATIC STRATEGIST)\par \par \uc2 When I joined the Board of \uc2 NARAL Pro-Choice America\uc2  ten years ago, six in ten Americans supported access to abortion. It's now eight in ten Americans, because the nature of the conversation has changed.\par \par \uc2 GUEST (THE POWERHOUSE ROUNDTABLE)\par \par \uc2 Yeah.\par \par \uc2 KAREN FINNEY (DEMOCRATIC STRATEGIST)\par \par \uc2 This is about bodily autonomy and not having the government tell a woman what medicine she can take, what procedure she should have.\par \par \uc2 LEIGH ANN CALDWELL (WASHINGTON POST LIVE ANCHOR)\par \par \uc2 (Inaudible).\par \par \uc2 CHRIS CHRISTIE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And let's let each state decide it. And, and that's what this, the whole issue behind Dobbs is and that's what Republicans should be saying. Let each state decide it. In New Jersey, I'm pro-life, but we can have abortion up to the ninth month in New Jersey now. I don't favor that. If I want to try to change it, I've got to go and try to change the legislature.\par \par \uc2 LEIGH ANN CALDWELL (WASHINGTON POST LIVE ANCHOR)\par \par \uc2 For Senate, for Senate Democrats, though, it is actually...\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right. All right, we're, we are out of time. Thank you. We'll continue that later, I'm sure.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Coming up, Major League Baseball is back. But with some of the biggest rule changes in the history of the game. Our exclusive interview with MLB Commissioner Rob Manfred about the new era for America's pastime. That's next.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document THWK000020230413ej4900004\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ABORTION PILL BAN SHOWDOWN WH VOWS TO USE "EVERY OPTION" TO PRESERVE ACCESS\b0\par\par\uc2 481 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Sunday\par \uc2 WNSU\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GROWING CALLS TO REINSTATE TN LAWMAKERS\par \par \uc2 NASHVILLE, EXPELLED, RACISM, JONES, PEARSON, KUMAR, SHULMAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GROWING CALLS TO REINSTATE TN LAWMAKERS\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, MIFEPRISTONE, SHOWDOWN, BECERRA, JUDGE, BAPTIST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION PILL BAN SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Faith Abubey in Nashville for us. Thank you, Faith. Now to the new battleground in the abortion debate in this country. The Biden administration is vowing to protect access to a key abortion pill, that's after a federal judge in Texas ruled to suspend the \uc2 FDA\uc2 's longstanding approval of Mifepristone. ABC's Elizabeth Schulze reports from the White House.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION PILL BAN SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WH VOWS TO USE "EVERY OPTION" TO PRESERVE ACCESS\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight the Biden administration vowing to use every option to preserve Americans access to the abortion pill.\par \par \uc2 XAVIER BECERRA\uc2  (DEPT OF HEALTH & HUMAN SERVICES)\par \par \uc2 Every option is on the table.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) After a conservative federal judge in Texas ruled to suspend \uc2 FDA\uc2  approval of Mifepristone, a medication approved 23 years ago and used in more than half of US abortions.\par \par \uc2 XAVIER BECERRA\uc2  (DEPT OF HEALTH & HUMAN SERVICES)\par \par \uc2 This is not America. What you saw by that one judge in that one court in that one state, that's not America.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The Justice Department appealing the case. It now heads to the conservative 5th circuit court of appeals in New Orleans, set to weigh in this week, deciding if Mifepristone should stay available as the case works through the legal system, likely all the way to the Supreme Court. The anti-abortion group that filed the lawsuit tells ABC News it's hopeful.\par \par \uc2 ERIK BAPTIST (SR COUNSEL ALLIANCE DEFENDING FREEDOM)\par \par \uc2 We're happy to have obtained that preliminary ruling from the district court, but we know obviously this is not the last stage and the last word on this issue, and we're ready to go to the next stage.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) If the Texas ruling stands, even Americans in states where abortion is legal, wouldn't have access to the medication. President Biden warning, "It is the next big step toward the national ban on abortion that Republican elected officials have vowed to make law in America." But many top Republicans staying quiet on the case after abortion rights helped fuel Democratic wins in local and midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The Texas judge's ruling allows for the abortion pill to remain available for at least the next five days or until that appeals court weighs in. So it's possible that in the next week governors and clinics in states where abortion is legal, stock up on the medication so they can have it on hand US manufacturing and distribution are eventually halted. Linsey.\par \par \uc2 Document WNSU000020230411ej4900003\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WORLD NEWS SUNDAY\b0\par\par\uc2 460 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Sunday\par \uc2 WNSU\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GROWING CALLS TO REINSTATE TN LAWMAKERS\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Tonight the push to reinstate two expelled Tennessee lawmakers accelerates. We hear from both men and the Republican who led the charge to oust them. Their competing narratives and what they say should happen now. Days after the historic move by Tennessee's Republicans, Justin Pearson and Justin Jones are speaking out. Pearson calling their expulsion one of the greater tactics of voter disenfranchisement and voter oppression he's ever witnessed. But a leading Republican is strongly defending the action. The pivotal moves now playing out. Faith Abubey from Tennessee.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION PILL BAN SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 The battle over the abortion pill after conflicting federal rulings. The debate on an almost certain fast track to the Supreme Court. What it could mean for abortion access, even in states where abortion is legal, as one of the country's most conservative appeals courts gets set to weigh in. Elizabeth Schulze from the White House.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BARR'S WARNING FOR TRUMP\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Days after former President Trump's historic indictment, Trump's Attorney General, Bill Barr, with a warning for his one-time boss. What he thinks about another potential indictment.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POPE'S EASTER MESSAGE FOR PEACE\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  celebrating mass and speaking out on this most holy of days for Christians, calling for peace around the world, singling out the Middle East, the Ukrainian and Russian people. Marcus Moore from Vatican City.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UKRAINIAN CHILDREN RETURN FROM RUSSIA\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 The war in Ukraine. The emotional reunion. Mothers and children back together and back at home, rescued from Russia, as another Russian strike on civilians claims more lives. Tom Soufi Burridge from Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHINA-TAIWAN DUELING DRILLS\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 The dueling military drills as China turns up the heat on Taiwan, simulating a strike on the independent democracy. Britt Clennett is Taipei.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WILL CONVICTED MURDERER BE PARDONED?\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 The controversy building in Texas. Governor Gregg Abbott seeks to pardon a sergeant convicted of killing a protester during a black lives matter rally. We hear from the DA and the victim's widow. Zohreen Shah reports.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TIGER WITHDRAWS FROM MASTERS\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Tiger Woods Masters quest now on hold. Why the five-time champ pulled out ahead of today's competition.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMERICA STRONG\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And "America Strong" tonight. the young musician who hit one out of the park at Yankee Stadium without even picking up a bat. His family's message of inclusivity.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WORLDS NEWS TONIGHT\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 From ABC News world headquarters in New York, this is "World News Tonight."\par \par \uc2 Document WNSU000020230411ej4900001\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT MEETS WITH OUSTED LAWMAKERS BIDEN SPEAKS WITH THREE TN LEGISLATORS WHO FACED EXPULSION VOTE\b0\par\par\uc2 552 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DUELING DECISIONS: ABORTION PILL RULINGS\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, WASHINGTON, ABORTION, FDA, BIRTH CONTROL, MCGILL\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, HARRIS, RULING, ABORTION, WOMEN\par \par \uc2 DWYER, FDA, TEXAS, ABORTION, IMPLICATIONS, RULING\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, HARRIS, TN, EXPULSION, JOHNSON, LOWERY\par \par \uc2 PENTAGON, DOCUMENTS, CLASSIFIED, LEAK, UKRAINE, \uc2 NATO\par \par \uc2 CHINA, TAIWAN, MILITARY, EXERCISES\par \par \uc2 VIOLENCE, PASSOVER, RAMADAN, EASTER, MIDDLE EAST\par \par \uc2 JOBS, SLOWING, HIRING\par \par \uc2 POPE, EASTER, GOOD FRIDAY, BRONCHITIS\par \par \uc2 MASTERS, GOLF, KOEPKA, JACKET\par \par \uc2 KINGSBURY, MISSING, MOTHER, MINNESOTA, WILLIAMS, DEGEORGE\par \par \uc2 REID, CRASH, DRUNK DRIVING, ACCIDENT\par \par \uc2 SCHEME, \uc2 JP MORGAN\uc2 , CHARGED, JAVICE, LIEBER\par \par \uc2 HOME RUNS, CLIMATE CHANGE, SCIENCE, CALLAHAN, OLNEY\par \par \uc2 NEGRON, NATIONAL ANTHEM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, RULINGS, HAWKINS, MCGILL\par \par \uc2 JONES, JOHNSON, PEARSON, GUN REFORM\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're staying with politics, but now to the three Tennessee lawmakers who face an expulsion vote in the state legislature getting strong support from the White House.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VICE PRESIDENT MEETS WITH OUSTED LAWMAKERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BIDEN SPEAKS WITH THREE TN LEGISLATORS WHO FACED EXPULSION VOTE\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The three Democrats speaking with President Biden, as you see there, in a video call and getting a visit from Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ABC's Faith Abubey is live in Tennessee and has more on the reaction to this extraordinary punishment and what could be next for the two ousted from their positions. Good morning again, Faith.\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, good morning to you, Janai. One of the things that has outraged some in this community is the fact that a partisan expulsion vote like this hasn't happened around here. In fact, it hasn't happened. This is the first time in the state's modern history that the ousted lawmakers where from a different party and these ones happen to be black.\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Overnight, Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  meeting with all three Democratic lawmakers who face that expulsion vote. Video from the meeting room shows Justin Pearson, Gloria Johnson, and Justin Jones standing together with their arms locked. President Biden also thanked them for their voices during a video conference, and then invited them to the White House. The lawmakers, they're accused of violating Tennessee State House rules when they use a bullhorn as part of a gun-control protests on the House floor last week.\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Now, it was after the Nashville Covenant School shooting that killed six people, including three children. Gloria Johnson, a white woman, was the only one among the group who survived that Republican-led expulsion vote. And she has suggested, many others have as well, that this is because of racism.\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, with Pearson and Jones gone, more than 100,000 people in their districts are now without representation in the Tennessee State House until county commissioners named their replacement. Now, members of the Nashville Metro Council and the Shelby County Board of Commissioners are considering reappointing the lawmakers back to their seats. And, Gio, we're hearing that there is growing momentum. There is growing support for these lawmakers to be reappointed. Gio?\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And we will see what happens. Faith, thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230510ej480000m\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 GMA BOOK CLUB "DIRTY LAUNDRY" DISHA BOSE\b0\par\par\uc2 1,149 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DUELING DECISIONS: ABORTION PILL RULINGS\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, WASHINGTON, ABORTION, FDA, BIRTH CONTROL, MCGILL\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, HARRIS, RULING, ABORTION, WOMEN\par \par \uc2 DWYER, FDA, TEXAS, ABORTION, IMPLICATIONS, RULING\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, HARRIS, TN, EXPULSION, JOHNSON, LOWERY\par \par \uc2 PENTAGON, DOCUMENTS, CLASSIFIED, LEAK, UKRAINE, \uc2 NATO\par \par \uc2 CHINA, TAIWAN, MILITARY, EXERCISES\par \par \uc2 VIOLENCE, PASSOVER, RAMADAN, EASTER, MIDDLE EAST\par \par \uc2 JOBS, SLOWING, HIRING\par \par \uc2 POPE, EASTER, GOOD FRIDAY, BRONCHITIS\par \par \uc2 MASTERS, GOLF, KOEPKA, JACKET\par \par \uc2 KINGSBURY, MISSING, MOTHER, MINNESOTA, WILLIAMS, DEGEORGE\par \par \uc2 REID, CRASH, DRUNK DRIVING, ACCIDENT\par \par \uc2 SCHEME, \uc2 JP MORGAN\uc2 , CHARGED, JAVICE, LIEBER\par \par \uc2 HOME RUNS, CLIMATE CHANGE, SCIENCE, CALLAHAN, OLNEY\par \par \uc2 NEGRON, NATIONAL ANTHEM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, RULINGS, HAWKINS, MCGILL\par \par \uc2 JONES, JOHNSON, PEARSON, GUN REFORM\par \par \uc2 BEACH, SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SIX INJURED AT SOUTH CAROLINA BEACH PARTY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GUNSHOTS FIRED AS STUDENTS CELEBRATED "SENIOR SKIP DAY"\par \par \uc2 OBESITY, RESEARCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW STUDY OUT ON OBESITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING DOWN GENETIC & LIFESTYLE FACTORS\par \par \uc2 KENNEDY, WINSTEAD, BORDIZZO, DAWSON, FAVREAU, "STAR WARS"\par \par \uc2 "ON GRIEF", SENIOR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BUZZ PICK\par \par \uc2 DEALS, SHOPPING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "DEALS & STEALS" WITH TORY JOHNSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 BOSE, "DIRTY LAUNDRY"\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And turning the page on a must-read. Disha Bose is the author of the April "GMA" book club pick, it's called "Dirty Laundry" and tells us the tale of a shocking murder in a seemingly picture-perfect Irish coastal town, exposing decades long secrets. Disha is here with us. Disha, good morning to you.\par \par \uc2 DISHA BOSE (AUTHOR "DIRTY LAUNDRY")\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Welcome. Congratulations on the book.\par \par \uc2 DISHA BOSE (AUTHOR "DIRTY LAUNDRY")\par \par \uc2 Thank you.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, it is finally out in the wild, what are you most excited for readers to experience?\par \par \uc2 DISHA BOSE (AUTHOR "DIRTY LAUNDRY")\par \par \uc2 I hope they pick up a book that they can't put down. And also, I hope that they find there's a very fine line between what's presented on social media, especially about motherhood and what the reality is about early motherhood.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, preach.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And one of the characters, one of the main characters in this novel is Mishti, she's from India. And you've said that one of most burdensome parts of writing this novel was actually making sure that that story was authentic.\par \par \uc2 DISHA BOSE (AUTHOR "DIRTY LAUNDRY")\par \par \uc2 Yes. We have a lot of shared experiences. We're both Indian mothers to young children, we live in Ireland. But then there are differences like I am married to an Irishman, it's not an arranged marriage for me. But I suppose a lot of writers have kind of faced this burden where we want to keep the characters authentic, give them agency in the book, but also keep the story interesting and going, you know.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, clearly, the story is interesting, it's getting so much buzz. And we want to talk about it, because we like to partner with little free library, so we can give copies of the "GMA Book Club" picks all across the country to readers all over. And this morning, we do have a question from the library steward in Wisconsin. So, here is Sandra.\par \par \uc2 SANDRA (LIBRARY STEWARD WISCONSIN)\par \par \uc2 Good morning, America. Hi, Disha, congratulations on your debut novel. I'd love to know that since you have connections to both India and Ireland, are any of your characters in your book based on persons that have been your acquaintances?\par \par \uc2 DISHA BOSE (AUTHOR "DIRTY LAUNDRY")\par \par \uc2 None of my friends and family are in the book, I just want to put it out there.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You're just saying that just in case, right?\par \par \uc2 DISHA BOSE (AUTHOR "DIRTY LAUNDRY")\par \par \uc2 No, but I have been inspired by people I've met both online and in real life. I'd best describe my characters as an amalgamation of the people I've seen online and of the people I know.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah. Disha, we have a quick game that we want to get into, asking you a rapid-fire question. But I want to ask you real quick, as a mother of two young kids what do you think is the sort of misconception between a lot of what we see online and what's real?\par \par \uc2 DISHA BOSE (AUTHOR "DIRTY LAUNDRY")\par \par \uc2 We don't get any sleep. We don't get time to shower. We can barely feed ourselves. I think those are, yeah. And glossy pictures, they don't happen.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah. I love hearing the truth about that. Okay, so we are calling this game, would you reader, I'm going to give you a choice between two things, you say the first answer that comes to mind. Okay? Hardcover or eReader?\par \par \uc2 DISHA BOSE (AUTHOR "DIRTY LAUNDRY")\par \par \uc2 Hardcover.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) There you go. Bookmark or fold the page?\par \par \uc2 DISHA BOSE (AUTHOR "DIRTY LAUNDRY")\par \par \uc2 Bookmark. Oh, my gosh, bookmark.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Bookstore or library?\par \par \uc2 DISHA BOSE (AUTHOR "DIRTY LAUNDRY")\par \par \uc2 Bookstore.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Bookstore? Finish a book, stay up late or wake up early?\par \par \uc2 DISHA BOSE (AUTHOR "DIRTY LAUNDRY")\par \par \uc2 Stay up late, yeah, totally.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Never know a book's ending or start halfway through?\par \par \uc2 DISHA BOSE (AUTHOR "DIRTY LAUNDRY")\par \par \uc2 Start halfway through.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, really?\par \par \uc2 DISHA BOSE (AUTHOR "DIRTY LAUNDRY")\par \par \uc2 I need to know the ending.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah. Read on the beach or at a cozy cabin?\par \par \uc2 DISHA BOSE (AUTHOR "DIRTY LAUNDRY")\par \par \uc2 Cozy cabin.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Cozy cabin. Okay. Your favorite main character? Who is your favorite main carrier in a book?\par \par \uc2 DISHA BOSE (AUTHOR "DIRTY LAUNDRY")\par \par \uc2 In this book?\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Any book.\par \par \uc2 DISHA BOSE (AUTHOR "DIRTY LAUNDRY")\par \par \uc2 My gosh, let's see.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's a tough one.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's a big one.\par \par \uc2 DISHA BOSE (AUTHOR "DIRTY LAUNDRY")\par \par \uc2 I am totally blank, sorry.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's all right. Well, thank you so much for being here.\par \par \uc2 DISHA BOSE (AUTHOR "DIRTY LAUNDRY")\par \par \uc2 Thank you.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) By the way, all of her answers will lead to this being a best seller. Very smart.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you so much, Disha, "Dirty Laundry" is available now. And Disha is sitting down with Eva to talk all about the book. That conversation airs later this month on "GMA." And as always, keep reading along with us on our \uc2 Instagram\uc2  @GMABookClub.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And coming up, Kate and Charlie Gibson re all here as reading into the booming business of audiobooks. We'll be right back here at "GMA."\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230510ej480000u\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ONE-PAN WONDERS SERVING UP EASY EASTER, PASSOVER & POST-SPRING BREAK BREAKFASTS\b0\par\par\uc2 1,058 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DUELING DECISIONS: ABORTION PILL RULINGS\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, WASHINGTON, ABORTION, FDA, BIRTH CONTROL, MCGILL\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, HARRIS, RULING, ABORTION, WOMEN\par \par \uc2 DWYER, FDA, TEXAS, ABORTION, IMPLICATIONS, RULING\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, HARRIS, TN, EXPULSION, JOHNSON, LOWERY\par \par \uc2 PENTAGON, DOCUMENTS, CLASSIFIED, LEAK, UKRAINE, \uc2 NATO\par \par \uc2 CHINA, TAIWAN, MILITARY, EXERCISES\par \par \uc2 VIOLENCE, PASSOVER, RAMADAN, EASTER, MIDDLE EAST\par \par \uc2 JOBS, SLOWING, HIRING\par \par \uc2 POPE, EASTER, GOOD FRIDAY, BRONCHITIS\par \par \uc2 MASTERS, GOLF, KOEPKA, JACKET\par \par \uc2 KINGSBURY, MISSING, MOTHER, MINNESOTA, WILLIAMS, DEGEORGE\par \par \uc2 REID, CRASH, DRUNK DRIVING, ACCIDENT\par \par \uc2 SCHEME, \uc2 JP MORGAN\uc2 , CHARGED, JAVICE, LIEBER\par \par \uc2 HOME RUNS, CLIMATE CHANGE, SCIENCE, CALLAHAN, OLNEY\par \par \uc2 NEGRON, NATIONAL ANTHEM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, RULINGS, HAWKINS, MCGILL\par \par \uc2 JONES, JOHNSON, PEARSON, GUN REFORM\par \par \uc2 BEACH, SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SIX INJURED AT SOUTH CAROLINA BEACH PARTY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GUNSHOTS FIRED AS STUDENTS CELEBRATED "SENIOR SKIP DAY"\par \par \uc2 OBESITY, RESEARCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW STUDY OUT ON OBESITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING DOWN GENETIC & LIFESTYLE FACTORS\par \par \uc2 KENNEDY, WINSTEAD, BORDIZZO, DAWSON, FAVREAU, "STAR WARS"\par \par \uc2 "ON GRIEF", SENIOR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BUZZ PICK\par \par \uc2 DEALS, SHOPPING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "DEALS & STEALS" WITH TORY JOHNSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 BOSE, "DIRTY LAUNDRY"\par \par \uc2 YOUSAFZAI, "JOYLAND", SADIQ\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MALALA'S NEXT CHAPTER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NOBEL LAUREATE TURNED OSCAR-NOMINEE OPENS UP ABOUT REDEFINING HERSELF\par \par \uc2 AUDIOBOOK, GIBSON, COBEN, WEBER, BARONE, VACKER\par \par \uc2 PROVENZANO, PASTRIES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ONE-PAN WONDERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SERVING UP EASY EASTER, PASSOVER & POST-SPRING BREAK BREAKFASTS\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, and we are eating toaster pastries here because welcome back on "GMA." We're serving up one-pan wonders the whole family's going to love. These are easy Easter, Passover, and post-spring break breakfasts. Chef Maria Provenzano has it all and joins us now. Maria, good morning. Welcome to "GMA."\par \par \uc2 MARIA PROVENZANO (CHEF)\par \par \uc2 Good morning. Thanks for having me.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Absolutely. So, these recipes, they're all on our website right now if you scan that QR code on the screen that we're going to have in just a moment. All baked on sheet pans, so they can cook up quick. We're starting with eggs and pancakes. What's the first step for either of those recipes?\par \par \uc2 MARIA PROVENZANO (CHEF)\par \par \uc2 Yeah. So, the first step in doing any kind of sheet pan recipe is really using some parchment paper. This is going to save you.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LINE SHEET PAN WITH PARCHMENT PAPER\par \par \uc2 MARIA PROVENZANO (CHEF)\par \par \uc2 So, especially for eggs, something that can stick to even the skillet when you're making them. So, I have my parchment paper here. You want to go up on the edges. But here's the trick, spray the baking sheet with some cooking spray, then put the parchment down and do another spray. That's going to hold it down there. Then pour your eggs. And I always mix my eggs with a little bit of milk.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POUR BATTER ON SHEET PAN, ADD TOPPINGS\par \par \uc2 MARIA PROVENZANO (CHEF)\par \par \uc2 And the same process with the pancakes. However, with the pancakes, I always do butter instead of cooking spray because what that does when you put it in the oven, because that's how we are cooking these, right, in the oven. And when you do that, it creates that sort of browned butter taste that you get from the skillet. And you don't want to lose that when you're in the oven. So, I like doing butter on that. And then what's great these is that you can customize them as you like. So, for instance, when you're on, you know, doing it on the stove and customizing them for everybody, everybody's eating before you. I want to eat the same time as everybody else and I find that to be highly unfair. So, what you can do is you can actually section these off put the toppings on. Let's say somebody doesn't like chocolate, that is not anybody in my house.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) No.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Or here.\par \par \uc2 MARIA PROVENZANO (CHEF)\par \par \uc2 And then bake them up and they are great you can eat them all together, it's perfect.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, so fun. Okay, Maria, so your last recipe, it's one the kids are going to love that's why we are eating it already. We have the store-bought versions here, but you're making some homemade toaster pastries which I wish we could try here.\par \par \uc2 MARIA PROVENZANO (CHEF)\par \par \uc2 I know, kids and kids at heart. Right? So, it all starts with some pie dough, you can make your own from scratch. I'm a from-scratch girl, but I'm not going to going to judge you if you get them from the store. But the key is having your parchment paper set and then rolling out the pie dough and cutting it into a large rectangular shape.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CUT TWO RECTANGLES, SPREAD JELLY OVER ONE RECTANGLE\par \par \uc2 MARIA PROVENZANO (CHEF)\par \par \uc2 Then I put in some jelly but you can do any kind of filling really that you like. And then top of this with another sheet of the pie dough, boom.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Boom.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLACE OTHER RECTANGLE ON TOP & SEAL WITH FORK, SPREAD BUTTER ON TOP WITH PASTRY BRUSH\par \par \uc2 MARIA PROVENZANO (CHEF)\par \par \uc2 And then you just use the fork to create those little lines and poke some holes. And then once it comes out, it's going to look beautiful like that.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And then you just top it and you are done. Look at that. That's amazing.\par \par \uc2 MARIA PROVENZANO (CHEF)\par \par \uc2 You can add some festive sprinkles.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Maria, thank you so, so much for this, we're all going to be making those toaster pastries, appreciate it. And get that recipe on our website, and we'll be right back here on "GMA."\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, get more "GMA" in your life everyday with "GMA Life" streaming on ABC News Live this morning at 9:00, 11:00 AM and 1:00 PM Eastern. Find ABC News Life on \uc2 Hulu\uc2 , the ABC News app and on abcnews.com.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thanks for being here. We'll see you tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Bye.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Bye.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230510ej480000y\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 PLAY OF THE DAY\b0\par\par\uc2 371 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DUELING DECISIONS: ABORTION PILL RULINGS\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, WASHINGTON, ABORTION, FDA, BIRTH CONTROL, MCGILL\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, HARRIS, RULING, ABORTION, WOMEN\par \par \uc2 DWYER, FDA, TEXAS, ABORTION, IMPLICATIONS, RULING\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, HARRIS, TN, EXPULSION, JOHNSON, LOWERY\par \par \uc2 PENTAGON, DOCUMENTS, CLASSIFIED, LEAK, UKRAINE, \uc2 NATO\par \par \uc2 CHINA, TAIWAN, MILITARY, EXERCISES\par \par \uc2 VIOLENCE, PASSOVER, RAMADAN, EASTER, MIDDLE EAST\par \par \uc2 JOBS, SLOWING, HIRING\par \par \uc2 POPE, EASTER, GOOD FRIDAY, BRONCHITIS\par \par \uc2 MASTERS, GOLF, KOEPKA, JACKET\par \par \uc2 KINGSBURY, MISSING, MOTHER, MINNESOTA, WILLIAMS, DEGEORGE\par \par \uc2 REID, CRASH, DRUNK DRIVING, ACCIDENT\par \par \uc2 SCHEME, \uc2 JP MORGAN\uc2 , CHARGED, JAVICE, LIEBER\par \par \uc2 HOME RUNS, CLIMATE CHANGE, SCIENCE, CALLAHAN, OLNEY\par \par \uc2 NEGRON, NATIONAL ANTHEM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I am so excited for this "Play of The Day" here on "gma." One of our own just hitting out of the park. ABC News publicity director, Anna Negron taking to the field to sing the National Anthem at the Mets home (inaudible). She nailed it, right?\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Lots of praise from so many colleagues. Our own Diane Sawyer said it best, quote, "just wow." The New Jersey native has also performed the National Anthem at Madison Square Garden, Barkley Center, and Met Life Stadium.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Love that.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That is awesome.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And this Sunday, she's going to do "God Bless America" at Citi Field.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're so lucky to have someone who's so super talented.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Congratulations.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) (inaudible) the public release for her (inaudible)...\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah (inaudible).\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...good PR right there for sure.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COMING UP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DUELING RULINGS\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, coming up here on "gma" in our second hour, more on the dueling rulings on the abortion pill and the likely road to the Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HEART HEALTH AND OBESITY\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And our "gma" Cover Story, the new twist on heart health and obesity and who is more at risk.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEALS AND STEALS\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And "Deals & Steals." Stay with us.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230510ej480000j\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 NEW STUDY OUT ON OBESITY BREAKING DOWN GENETIC & LIFESTYLE FACTORS\b0\par\par\uc2 711 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DUELING DECISIONS: ABORTION PILL RULINGS\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, WASHINGTON, ABORTION, FDA, BIRTH CONTROL, MCGILL\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, HARRIS, RULING, ABORTION, WOMEN\par \par \uc2 DWYER, FDA, TEXAS, ABORTION, IMPLICATIONS, RULING\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, HARRIS, TN, EXPULSION, JOHNSON, LOWERY\par \par \uc2 PENTAGON, DOCUMENTS, CLASSIFIED, LEAK, UKRAINE, \uc2 NATO\par \par \uc2 CHINA, TAIWAN, MILITARY, EXERCISES\par \par \uc2 VIOLENCE, PASSOVER, RAMADAN, EASTER, MIDDLE EAST\par \par \uc2 JOBS, SLOWING, HIRING\par \par \uc2 POPE, EASTER, GOOD FRIDAY, BRONCHITIS\par \par \uc2 MASTERS, GOLF, KOEPKA, JACKET\par \par \uc2 KINGSBURY, MISSING, MOTHER, MINNESOTA, WILLIAMS, DEGEORGE\par \par \uc2 REID, CRASH, DRUNK DRIVING, ACCIDENT\par \par \uc2 SCHEME, \uc2 JP MORGAN\uc2 , CHARGED, JAVICE, LIEBER\par \par \uc2 HOME RUNS, CLIMATE CHANGE, SCIENCE, CALLAHAN, OLNEY\par \par \uc2 NEGRON, NATIONAL ANTHEM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, RULINGS, HAWKINS, MCGILL\par \par \uc2 JONES, JOHNSON, PEARSON, GUN REFORM\par \par \uc2 BEACH, SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SIX INJURED AT SOUTH CAROLINA BEACH PARTY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GUNSHOTS FIRED AS STUDENTS CELEBRATED "SENIOR SKIP DAY"\par \par \uc2 OBESITY, RESEARCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW STUDY OUT ON OBESITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING DOWN GENETIC & LIFESTYLE FACTORS\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) \u8230\'20\'26those who gained weight for lifestyle choices. So, let's bring in ABC News medical contributor Dr. Alok Patel to break it all down. We love having you in person.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) How significant is this study when it comes to obesity and the risk to cardiovascular diseases?\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR ALOK PATEL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You know, Janai, you absolutely nailed it. And this adds to the growing body of evidence that even in individuals who are overweight or obese, your lifestyle may actually matter more than the genetics and the cards that we're dealt with when we are born. It was actually designed in a really elegant way. Swedish researchers looked at about 9,000 pairs of twins to control for the genetics. So, this should be a very important news for everyone out there in the public health world.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, does this change anything for those dealing with weight gain?\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR ALOK PATEL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Whit, I hope it adds empowerment to everyone out there and they realize that, hey, wait, BMI, these are just one number. This is just one metric in our overall health. So, regardless of what your situation is, this study, the growing body of evidence, tells us that there's a lot that we can actually do to reduce our risk regardless of how you look, what the shape of your body is.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And what's important to know about that overall risk of obesity, whether it's due to you know, genetics or even lifestyle?\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR ALOK PATEL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, Gio, researchers estimate that, in all individuals who are obese, lifestyle actually creates a percentage, a high percentage of your risk factors as opposed to genetics. And this is important that we talked about because about 40% of US adults are obese, which can lead to diseases such as heart disease, diabetes, many types of cancers. But, again, it's really important we're not only checking with our doctors. We're making healthy everyday choices on everything all day, but including holiday weekends as well. We're all taking our health into our own hands.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I like what you said there, though, that it should be empowering.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And people can take control and make some of these changes.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR ALOK PATEL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's what it's all about.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR ALOK PATEL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That is the important take away from this study and that's what people should really be focusing on and saying, you know what, I'm in the driver's seat for my own health.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) There you go. All right.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Exactly. Dr. Patel, it's great to see you in person in the studio on a Saturday.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR ALOK PATEL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Likewise.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes. Good to see you my, man. Appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Appreciate you being here.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR ALOK PATEL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We weren't in 4D.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230510ej480000o\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 INTRODUCTION TO THE 8:30 HALF HOUR\b0\par\par\uc2 405 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DUELING DECISIONS: ABORTION PILL RULINGS\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, WASHINGTON, ABORTION, FDA, BIRTH CONTROL, MCGILL\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, HARRIS, RULING, ABORTION, WOMEN\par \par \uc2 DWYER, FDA, TEXAS, ABORTION, IMPLICATIONS, RULING\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, HARRIS, TN, EXPULSION, JOHNSON, LOWERY\par \par \uc2 PENTAGON, DOCUMENTS, CLASSIFIED, LEAK, UKRAINE, \uc2 NATO\par \par \uc2 CHINA, TAIWAN, MILITARY, EXERCISES\par \par \uc2 VIOLENCE, PASSOVER, RAMADAN, EASTER, MIDDLE EAST\par \par \uc2 JOBS, SLOWING, HIRING\par \par \uc2 POPE, EASTER, GOOD FRIDAY, BRONCHITIS\par \par \uc2 MASTERS, GOLF, KOEPKA, JACKET\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Welcome back to "GMA." "Star Wars" fans didn't have to go to a galaxy far, far away to celebrate everything about the franchise. Coming up in our second hour, Lama Hasan takes us inside "Star Wars" Celebration Europe 2023, which is taking place this weekend in London.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Ooh.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 That sounds like fun.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Yeah.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Yeah, good assignment.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Yeah.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIGHT NOW: WSJ REPORTER CHARGED\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Well, now, let's take a look at some of the other big stories that we're following on this Saturday morning. Happening right now, a Russian news agency is reporting that Russian investigators have officially charged "Wall Street Journal" reporter \uc2 Evan Gershkovich\uc2  with espionage. The journalist is accused of pursuing state secrets on behalf of the US. Gershkovich denies the charges and has filed an appeal.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW MEXICO POLICE SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Also right now, an investigation is underway after New Mexico police shot and killed a man in his own home. The officers were reportedly responding to a domestic violence call, but they arrived at the wrong address. And according to police, when officers arrived the homeowner answered the door while holding a gun. Officers then fired one round killing him.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And on this Easter eve, we want to salute a hardworking bunny who goes by the name of Percy or Officer Hops. He holds the title of Wellness Officer at the Yuba City Police Department in California where he is in charge of being an outlet for stress. So to all the hardworking bunnies out there, of course, we salute you on this very, very important weekend.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 I mean, we can't top video like that. Like, that's it. We're done.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 We certainly can't. Stress relief right there.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Exactly.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230510ej480000d\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 THE FORCE IS STRONG THIS WEEKEND "STAR WARS CELEBRATION" BRINGS CREATORS & CASTS TOGETHER\b0\par\par\uc2 1,148 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DUELING DECISIONS: ABORTION PILL RULINGS\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, WASHINGTON, ABORTION, FDA, BIRTH CONTROL, MCGILL\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, HARRIS, RULING, ABORTION, WOMEN\par \par \uc2 DWYER, FDA, TEXAS, ABORTION, IMPLICATIONS, RULING\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, HARRIS, TN, EXPULSION, JOHNSON, LOWERY\par \par \uc2 PENTAGON, DOCUMENTS, CLASSIFIED, LEAK, UKRAINE, \uc2 NATO\par \par \uc2 CHINA, TAIWAN, MILITARY, EXERCISES\par \par \uc2 VIOLENCE, PASSOVER, RAMADAN, EASTER, MIDDLE EAST\par \par \uc2 JOBS, SLOWING, HIRING\par \par \uc2 POPE, EASTER, GOOD FRIDAY, BRONCHITIS\par \par \uc2 MASTERS, GOLF, KOEPKA, JACKET\par \par \uc2 KINGSBURY, MISSING, MOTHER, MINNESOTA, WILLIAMS, DEGEORGE\par \par \uc2 REID, CRASH, DRUNK DRIVING, ACCIDENT\par \par \uc2 SCHEME, \uc2 JP MORGAN\uc2 , CHARGED, JAVICE, LIEBER\par \par \uc2 HOME RUNS, CLIMATE CHANGE, SCIENCE, CALLAHAN, OLNEY\par \par \uc2 NEGRON, NATIONAL ANTHEM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, RULINGS, HAWKINS, MCGILL\par \par \uc2 JONES, JOHNSON, PEARSON, GUN REFORM\par \par \uc2 BEACH, SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SIX INJURED AT SOUTH CAROLINA BEACH PARTY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GUNSHOTS FIRED AS STUDENTS CELEBRATED "SENIOR SKIP DAY"\par \par \uc2 OBESITY, RESEARCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW STUDY OUT ON OBESITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING DOWN GENETIC & LIFESTYLE FACTORS\par \par \uc2 KENNEDY, WINSTEAD, BORDIZZO, DAWSON, FAVREAU, "STAR WARS"\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, we do want to turn now to another story we're following this morning hitting light speed to a galaxy far, far away. The 2023 "Star Wars" celebration underway right now in London.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE FORCE IS STRONG THIS WEEKEND\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "STAR WARS CELEBRATION" BRINGS CREATORS & CASTS TOGETHER IN LONDON\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And ABCs Lama Hasan is catching up with a cast and the creators behind a cast on the creators behind shows like "The Mandalorian." Best assignment in the house this morning. Lama, good morning.\par \par \uc2 LAMA HASAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning to you, Whit. Tell me about it. Well, you can see, I've been hanging out with Max Rebo. I've got some of my Mandalorian mates. You can probably see them over my shoulder because that's how I roll. Okay, not really. We're here for the "Star Wars" celebration, which is the ultimate fan experience. Fans from all over the world are gathering here to talk about what else but "Star Wars." 20,000 of them were here yesterday. They're also here to find out what's new in the galaxy.\par \par \uc2 LAMA HASAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) From a galaxy not that far away, "Star Wars" fans are uniting in force, all under one roof in London for this year's "Star Wars" celebration, kicking off with some big announcements that so many have been waiting for with none other than the return of Daisy Ridley playing the much-loved Jedi, Rey.\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM MOVIE, "STAR WARS: THE RISE OF SKYWALKER"\par \par \uc2 DAISY RIDLEY (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 (Inaudible) Jedi.\par \par \uc2 LAMA HASAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What can we expect...\par \par \uc2 KATHLEEN KENNEDY\uc2  (PRESIDENT LUCASFILM)\par \par \uc2 We did, we did say that she's rebuilding the Jedi order. So, it's the new Jedi order. And it is 15 years out from "Rise of Skywalker."\par \par \uc2 LAMA HASAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And these are movies, right?\par \par \uc2 KATHLEEN KENNEDY\uc2  (PRESIDENT LUCASFILM)\par \par \uc2 Yes. Back on the big screen. "Star Wars" will always be movies. I mean, that's probably the most important platform for us. There's been this opportunity to let the audience know we are exploring new characters and going to different places. And it takes the expectation off a bit when you can do that experimentation in the TV space and then move back into the theater where you have thousands of people sitting and watching things together, which is really the wonderful thing about movies.\par \par \uc2 LAMA HASAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And the "Star Wars" surprises don't stop there. For the first time \uc2 Disney\uc2 + revealing a trailer for one of the year's most highly anticipated series, "Ahsoka."\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM TV SERIES, "AHSOKA"\par \par \uc2 NATASHA LIU BORDIZZO ("STAR WARS: AHSOKA")\par \par \uc2 It's been a while.\par \par \uc2 ROSARIO DAWSON ("STAR WARS: AHSOKA")\par \par \uc2 Things have changed.\par \par \uc2 ROSARIO DAWSON ("STAR WARS: AHSOKA")\par \par \uc2 It's kind of remarkable as intimate as it feels when we are filming it that the scope of it, just the breadth of it just kind of takes my breath away.\par \par \uc2 MARY ELIZABETH WINSTEAD ("STAR WARS: AHSOKA")\par \par \uc2 Yes.\par \par \uc2 LAMA HASAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) How grueling was the training?\par \par \uc2 NATASHA LIU BORDIZZO ("STAR WARS: AHSOKA")\par \par \uc2 You're 20 minutes onset? Yeah, come on, training. Yeah, let me just get all my armor from there.\par \par \uc2 ROSARIO DAWSON ("STAR WARS: AHSOKA")\par \par \uc2 And then you are sweating like, okay, let's make you orange again.\par \par \uc2 MARY ELIZABETH WINSTEAD ("STAR WARS: AHSOKA")\par \par \uc2 I would forget that I was green and I'd be just walking outside just like walking around and then like oh, my God, where's my clothes? Where's my coat?\par \par \uc2 NATASHA LIU BORDIZZO ("STAR WARS: AHSOKA")\par \par \uc2 Yeah.\par \par \uc2 LAMA HASAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Fans are rejoicing with the news that the franchise's universe is expanding across the galaxy with a new mystery thriller series, "The Acolyte."\par \par \uc2 LAMA HASAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Can you tell us a little bit more about your character?\par \par \uc2 AMANDLA STENBERG ("STAR WARS: THE ACOLYTE")\par \par \uc2 No.\par \par \uc2 LAMA HASAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That was quick.\par \par \uc2 AMANDLA STENBERG ("STAR WARS: THE ACOLYTE")\par \par \uc2 She is contending with the lights and the dark within her.\par \par \uc2 LAMA HASAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And with only two episodes left in season three of "The Mandalorian"...\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM TV SERIES, "THE MANDALORIAN"\par \par \uc2 ACTOR (MALE)\par \par \uc2 This is the way.\par \par \uc2 LAMA HASAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It is not the way to share any spoilers.\par \par \uc2 LAMA HASAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) There's someone, was it you who talked about season four?\par \par \uc2 JON FAVREAU (DIRECTOR "STAR WARS: THE MANDALORIAN")\par \par \uc2 Are you talking about season four?\par \par \uc2 DAVE FILONI ("STAR WARS: THE MANDALORIAN")\par \par \uc2 I was not talking about, you know.\par \par \uc2 LAMA HASAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I'm trying.\par \par \uc2 JON FAVREAU (DIRECTOR "STAR WARS: THE MANDALORIAN")\par \par \uc2 I heard people are talking about season four.\par \par \uc2 DAVE FILONI ("STAR WARS: THE MANDALORIAN")\par \par \uc2 We've heard that play.\par \par \uc2 JON FAVREAU (DIRECTOR "STAR WARS: THE MANDALORIAN")\par \par \uc2 I heard...\par \par \uc2 DAVE FILONI ("STAR WARS: THE MANDALORIAN")\par \par \uc2 Mind tricks don't work on us.\par \par \uc2 ACTRESS (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 May the force be with you.\par \par \uc2 LAMA HASAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, boy, did they know how to keep a secret. Okay, so maybe I couldn't find out that much about "The Mandalorian" season four, what I did find out was that the creator, Jon Favreau, has already written it. But you know what, Whit, I still haven't interviewed Grogu, so maybe I should go and speak to Grogu, maybe he can use the force and spill some beans because, Whit, this is the way.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) This is the way, absolutely. I mean, Grogu is not a big talker, I've got to be honest. But maybe anybody could get some stuff out of him, it's you, Lama. Thank you so much. We appreciate it. Gio, over to you.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Nerd alert.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I know. Yep.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230510ej480000p\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WEATHER\b0\par\par\uc2 420 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DUELING DECISIONS: ABORTION PILL RULINGS\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, WASHINGTON, ABORTION, FDA, BIRTH CONTROL, MCGILL\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, HARRIS, RULING, ABORTION, WOMEN\par \par \uc2 DWYER, FDA, TEXAS, ABORTION, IMPLICATIONS, RULING\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, HARRIS, TN, EXPULSION, JOHNSON, LOWERY\par \par \uc2 PENTAGON, DOCUMENTS, CLASSIFIED, LEAK, UKRAINE, \uc2 NATO\par \par \uc2 CHINA, TAIWAN, MILITARY, EXERCISES\par \par \uc2 VIOLENCE, PASSOVER, RAMADAN, EASTER, MIDDLE EAST\par \par \uc2 JOBS, SLOWING, HIRING\par \par \uc2 POPE, EASTER, GOOD FRIDAY, BRONCHITIS\par \par \uc2 MASTERS, GOLF, KOEPKA, JACKET\par \par \uc2 KINGSBURY, MISSING, MOTHER, MINNESOTA, WILLIAMS, DEGEORGE\par \par \uc2 REID, CRASH, DRUNK DRIVING, ACCIDENT\par \par \uc2 SCHEME, \uc2 JP MORGAN\uc2 , CHARGED, JAVICE, LIEBER\par \par \uc2 HOME RUNS, CLIMATE CHANGE, SCIENCE, CALLAHAN, OLNEY\par \par \uc2 NEGRON, NATIONAL ANTHEM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, RULINGS, HAWKINS, MCGILL\par \par \uc2 JONES, JOHNSON, PEARSON, GUN REFORM\par \par \uc2 BEACH, SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SIX INJURED AT SOUTH CAROLINA BEACH PARTY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GUNSHOTS FIRED AS STUDENTS CELEBRATED "SENIOR SKIP DAY"\par \par \uc2 OBESITY, RESEARCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW STUDY OUT ON OBESITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING DOWN GENETIC & LIFESTYLE FACTORS\par \par \uc2 KENNEDY, WINSTEAD, BORDIZZO, DAWSON, FAVREAU, "STAR WARS"\par \par \uc2 "ON GRIEF", SENIOR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BUZZ PICK\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But until then, let's get a check of the weather and Somara Theodore has it and some beautiful blooming flowers. Yes.\par \par \uc2 SOMARA THEODORE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, good morning. The year was 1909, Mayor Ozaki from Tokyo gifted 2,000 cherry trees to First Lady Taft, and Washington, DC, thus the result blooming in full effect absolutely gorgeous. I will say they bloomed two weeks early than they should have for this time of year.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEMPERATURE OUTLOOK\par \par \uc2 SOMARA THEODORE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But I mean, look at what we're dealing with here, 20 degrees above the norm for this time of year in the week to come. Temperatures much above average throughout the southeast in the coming days as well. That's going to lead to a pretty big thaw.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SPRING FLOOD OUTLOOK\par \par \uc2 SOMARA THEODORE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're looking at major flooding close to Davenport, Iowa, there with that Mississippi River beginning to flood with all of that snowfall that we had earlier in the season. Also, out towards the west, we're looking at a moderate flood threat as well from Sacramento down to Fresno, even parts of Los Angeles. Again, we saw that intense snow pack throughout much of the west and parts of the Midwest. And now, with it thawing out, that is going to lead to flooding. We're going to talk more about the temperatures a little later, so stick around. For now, let's see what's going on a little closer to home.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NATIONAL MAP\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230510ej480000r\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 PENTAGON REVIEWING TOP SECRET DOCUMENTS LEAK PHOTOS APPEAR TO DETAIL US AND NATO AID TO UKRAINE\b0\par\par\uc2 337 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DUELING DECISIONS: ABORTION PILL RULINGS\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, WASHINGTON, ABORTION, FDA, BIRTH CONTROL, MCGILL\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, HARRIS, RULING, ABORTION, WOMEN\par \par \uc2 DWYER, FDA, TEXAS, ABORTION, IMPLICATIONS, RULING\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, HARRIS, TN, EXPULSION, JOHNSON, LOWERY\par \par \uc2 PENTAGON, DOCUMENTS, CLASSIFIED, LEAK, UKRAINE, \uc2 NATO\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're going to turn now to that urgent investigation by the Pentagon after classified documents related to Ukraine, Iran, North Korea, and other regions were posted online. ABC's Karen Travers is at the White House. Karen, good morning to you.\par \par \uc2 KAREN TRAVERS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Gio. The Justice Department is investigating how these top-secret documents from the Pentagon were leaked and posted on social media. Pictures of the documents appeared on social media this week, but ABC News has learned that back in early March dozens of classified documents were published online. They included sensitive details about China, North Korea, Iran's nuclear program, and the war in Ukraine. Some of these documents appear to be photos of slides from March 1st showing how the US and nato were helping Ukraine in its fight against Russia. The photos, most of which we cannot show, include details about casualty numbers, training schedules, and weapons deliveries, and a battle map of the key Ukrainian city of Bakhmut.\par \par \uc2 KAREN TRAVERS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, some of these photos are creased as if they were folded. One US official tells ABC News the documents are no longer relevant to the battlefield and they are of limited intelligence value and appear to have been altered from the original documents. But the fact that they were published online so quickly after they were produced on March 1st makes this already very big leak and even more significant security breach and risk. The Pentagon tells us they are reviewing this matter. Whit.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Certainly raising a lot of concerns. All right, Karen, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230510ej4800006\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 MALALA'S NEXT CHAPTER NOBEL LAUREATE OPENS UP ABOUT REDEFINING HERSELF\b0\par\par\uc2 988 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DUELING DECISIONS: ABORTION PILL RULINGS\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, WASHINGTON, ABORTION, FDA, BIRTH CONTROL, MCGILL\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, HARRIS, RULING, ABORTION, WOMEN\par \par \uc2 DWYER, FDA, TEXAS, ABORTION, IMPLICATIONS, RULING\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, HARRIS, TN, EXPULSION, JOHNSON, LOWERY\par \par \uc2 PENTAGON, DOCUMENTS, CLASSIFIED, LEAK, UKRAINE, \uc2 NATO\par \par \uc2 CHINA, TAIWAN, MILITARY, EXERCISES\par \par \uc2 VIOLENCE, PASSOVER, RAMADAN, EASTER, MIDDLE EAST\par \par \uc2 JOBS, SLOWING, HIRING\par \par \uc2 POPE, EASTER, GOOD FRIDAY, BRONCHITIS\par \par \uc2 MASTERS, GOLF, KOEPKA, JACKET\par \par \uc2 KINGSBURY, MISSING, MOTHER, MINNESOTA, WILLIAMS, DEGEORGE\par \par \uc2 REID, CRASH, DRUNK DRIVING, ACCIDENT\par \par \uc2 SCHEME, \uc2 JP MORGAN\uc2 , CHARGED, JAVICE, LIEBER\par \par \uc2 HOME RUNS, CLIMATE CHANGE, SCIENCE, CALLAHAN, OLNEY\par \par \uc2 NEGRON, NATIONAL ANTHEM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, RULINGS, HAWKINS, MCGILL\par \par \uc2 JONES, JOHNSON, PEARSON, GUN REFORM\par \par \uc2 BEACH, SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SIX INJURED AT SOUTH CAROLINA BEACH PARTY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GUNSHOTS FIRED AS STUDENTS CELEBRATED "SENIOR SKIP DAY"\par \par \uc2 OBESITY, RESEARCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW STUDY OUT ON OBESITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING DOWN GENETIC & LIFESTYLE FACTORS\par \par \uc2 KENNEDY, WINSTEAD, BORDIZZO, DAWSON, FAVREAU, "STAR WARS"\par \par \uc2 "ON GRIEF", SENIOR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BUZZ PICK\par \par \uc2 DEALS, SHOPPING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "DEALS & STEALS" WITH TORY JOHNSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 BOSE, "DIRTY LAUNDRY"\par \par \uc2 YOUSAFZAI, "JOYLAND", SADIQ\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MALALA'S NEXT CHAPTER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NOBEL LAUREATE TURNED OSCAR-NOMINEE OPENS UP ABOUT REDEFINING HERSELF\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're back on "GMA" and Malala Yousafzai's next chapter. The youngest ever Nobel Prize laureate is now a movie producer. ABC's Zohreen Shah sat down with her and the director of the film. That is really cool. Zohreen, good morning again.\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It was a lot of fun, Janai. And you know what, some people might be surprised to see Malala in Hollywood. But whether she is fighting for education or backing a film, her core goals are exactly the same. It is all about empowering women and young people. And that is what she did as the executive producer of "Joyland."\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) She's a global icon who dedicated her life to the education of women and children. Now, Pakistani activist Malala Yousafzai is bringing her star power to Hollywood.\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) How are you bringing activism to art?\par \par \uc2 MALALA YOUSAFZAI (ACTIVIST)\par \par \uc2 Storytelling has been at the center my activism. I began my campaign through storytelling.\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The story she's spotlighting plays out in the movie, "Joyland."\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM MOVIE, "JOYLAND"\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) We caught up with the first-time executive producer and first-time feature film director Saim Sadiq at the South Asian Excellence pre-Oscar celebration.\par \par \uc2 SAIM SADIQ (DIRECTOR "JOYLAND")\par \par \uc2 It starts with the youngest on getting a job at this erotic dance theater and falling in love with a trans girl and how that affects both of them, but also his family, including his wife in particular.\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) "Joyland" gives a real look at patriarchy and desire, but touching on issues like infidelity, being transgender and suicide rarely happen in Pakistani film.\par \par \uc2 ACTRESS (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 (Speaking foreign language)\par \par \uc2 MALALA YOUSAFZAI (ACTIVIST)\par \par \uc2 Pakistan is complex. It's such a diverse country. It's really important for us to not see it in black and white and really ensure that we are seeing, you know, the more real side of it.\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The movie started shattering glass ceilings. It was the first film from Pakistan to ever be short-listed for the Oscars and win an award at Cannes. But because of the transgender scenes, the movie was banned in its own home country.\par \par \uc2 SAIM SADIQ (DIRECTOR "JOYLAND")\par \par \uc2 We were randomly notified that because of certain complaints from people who had never seen the film, the census certificates had been revoked.\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But then the movie became the first film in Pakistan to ever get unbanned. After Malala spoke out, it was overturned in most places.\par \par \uc2 MALALA YOUSAFZAI (ACTIVIST)\par \par \uc2 I think everyone deserves a chance to tell their story. No one should be stopped from that. It's not about promoting a specific point of view, it's all about giving a chance to a person to tell a story from their side.\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) As the director points out, the controversy in Pakistan comes at a time when censorship of LGBTQ+ content in the US is growing.\par \par \uc2 SAIM SADIQ (DIRECTOR "JOYLAND")\par \par \uc2 I think it's easier to understand Pakistan if you think of it not as a country that's too different from America, funnily enough. I mean, the drag shows are banned in Tennessee.\par \par \uc2 MALALA YOUSAFZAI (ACTIVIST)\par \par \uc2 I think this is the bar of storytelling that helps us connect with people from around the world wherever we are.\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Connecting people is why it she says she wants to continue backing meaningful stories.\par \par \uc2 MALALA YOUSAFZAI (ACTIVIST)\par \par \uc2 It's really challenging to change perspectives. And for that, you need to really try other means, including making movies and TV shows and documentaries and comedies. And, you know, it does not really need to be serious documentary about a specific topic it can be funny. It can be funny and entertaining and have jokes, but behind all of those conversations is something that connects you with those people that you see on the screen. There is something in common.\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And "Joyland" achieves that goal. You guys, I saw it a couple months ago at a screening, I got there a few minutes late, and there was not a seat left in the theater. There is just so much buzz and excitement about this. "Joyland" is now playing in New York and around the country on the 21st. Janai?\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Looking forward to that. And, Zohreen, the early bird gets the worm.\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, I kind of figured that.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230510ej480000v\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 DASHCAM VIDEO RELEASED OF BRITT REID'S DRUNK DRIVING CRASH FIVE-YEAR-OLD GIRL LEFT SERIOUSLY INJURED AFTER ACCIDENT\b0\par\par\uc2 593 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DUELING DECISIONS: ABORTION PILL RULINGS\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, WASHINGTON, ABORTION, FDA, BIRTH CONTROL, MCGILL\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, HARRIS, RULING, ABORTION, WOMEN\par \par \uc2 DWYER, FDA, TEXAS, ABORTION, IMPLICATIONS, RULING\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, HARRIS, TN, EXPULSION, JOHNSON, LOWERY\par \par \uc2 PENTAGON, DOCUMENTS, CLASSIFIED, LEAK, UKRAINE, \uc2 NATO\par \par \uc2 CHINA, TAIWAN, MILITARY, EXERCISES\par \par \uc2 VIOLENCE, PASSOVER, RAMADAN, EASTER, MIDDLE EAST\par \par \uc2 JOBS, SLOWING, HIRING\par \par \uc2 POPE, EASTER, GOOD FRIDAY, BRONCHITIS\par \par \uc2 MASTERS, GOLF, KOEPKA, JACKET\par \par \uc2 KINGSBURY, MISSING, MOTHER, MINNESOTA, WILLIAMS, DEGEORGE\par \par \uc2 REID, CRASH, DRUNK DRIVING, ACCIDENT\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, to the new look we are getting into a drunk crash involving former Chief's Assistant Football Coach Britt Reid. Video of that night two years ago in which a 5-year-old girl was seriously injured is just being made public. And ABC's Mona Kosar Abdi watched it. She's here now with more. Mona, good morning.\par \par \uc2 MONA KOSAR ABDI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Gio, good morning. The accident happened just three days before the 2021 Super Bowl, right before Britt Reid, his father Kansas City head coach Andy Reid, and the team were supposed to take on the \uc2 Tampa Bay Buccaneers\uc2 . But, Britt wouldn't attend that game after causing a crash that left a 5-year-old girl in a coma.\par \par \uc2 MONA KOSAR ABDI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, new details in the horrific 2021 crash involving Britt Reid, son of super bowl winning coach Andy Reid, after he hit two parked cars and left a 5-year-old child seriously injured. With his case file now public, Kansas City Police releasing never-before-seen dashcam video of the moments after the crash, for which the former \uc2 Kansas City Chiefs\uc2  Assistant Coach is serving a three year sentence after pleading guilty to driving while intoxicated.\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP: DASHCAM FOOTAGE\par \par \uc2 OFFICER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 I can't have you on the phone.\par \par \uc2 BRITT REID (FORMER ASSISTANT COACH \uc2 KANSAS CITY CHIEFS\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 My dad is sitting right there.\par \par \uc2 OFFICER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Okay, I understand, but I can't have you on the phone right now, okay?\par \par \uc2 MONA KOSAR ABDI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In the footage obtained by our affiliate KNBC, Reid can be heard telling an officer he had taken a prescription medication used to treat ADHD hours before the crash.\par \par \uc2 BRITT REID (FORMER ASSISTANT COACH \uc2 KANSAS CITY CHIEFS\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 My front is starting to swell up.\par \par \uc2 MONA KOSAR ABDI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Reid complaining of injuries. Officers eventually sending him to the hospital. Reid heard in the video asking about the injured. Five-year-old Ariel trapped under the backseat of her mom's car. She suffered a traumatic brain injury from the crash. Her mom, Felicia, who sat down with "gma" in September, said her daughter has had to relearn many of her favorite things.\par \par \uc2 FELICIA MILLER (VICTIM'S MOTHER)\par \par \uc2 At the time she woke up, she didn't know nothing. She didn't know who I was, so as I'm trying to touch my baby, like, "Hey, baby," she was, you know, moving away and her eyes...\par \par \uc2 REPORTER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) She didn't recognize you?\par \par \uc2 FELICIA MILLER (VICTIM'S MOTHER)\par \par \uc2 No, she didn't recognize the.\par \par \uc2 MONA KOSAR ABDI (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And at least one of the cars that Reid hit was pulled over because it had ran out of gas. He is currently serving a three-year sentence for that DWI crash. Guys.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Such an awful story. All right, thank you so much, Mona. We appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230510ej480000f\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 INTRODUCTION TO THE 09:30 HALF-HOUR\b0\par\par\uc2 193 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DUELING DECISIONS: ABORTION PILL RULINGS\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, WASHINGTON, ABORTION, FDA, BIRTH CONTROL, MCGILL\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, HARRIS, RULING, ABORTION, WOMEN\par \par \uc2 DWYER, FDA, TEXAS, ABORTION, IMPLICATIONS, RULING\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, HARRIS, TN, EXPULSION, JOHNSON, LOWERY\par \par \uc2 PENTAGON, DOCUMENTS, CLASSIFIED, LEAK, UKRAINE, \uc2 NATO\par \par \uc2 CHINA, TAIWAN, MILITARY, EXERCISES\par \par \uc2 VIOLENCE, PASSOVER, RAMADAN, EASTER, MIDDLE EAST\par \par \uc2 JOBS, SLOWING, HIRING\par \par \uc2 POPE, EASTER, GOOD FRIDAY, BRONCHITIS\par \par \uc2 MASTERS, GOLF, KOEPKA, JACKET\par \par \uc2 KINGSBURY, MISSING, MOTHER, MINNESOTA, WILLIAMS, DEGEORGE\par \par \uc2 REID, CRASH, DRUNK DRIVING, ACCIDENT\par \par \uc2 SCHEME, \uc2 JP MORGAN\uc2 , CHARGED, JAVICE, LIEBER\par \par \uc2 HOME RUNS, CLIMATE CHANGE, SCIENCE, CALLAHAN, OLNEY\par \par \uc2 NEGRON, NATIONAL ANTHEM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, RULINGS, HAWKINS, MCGILL\par \par \uc2 JONES, JOHNSON, PEARSON, GUN REFORM\par \par \uc2 BEACH, SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SIX INJURED AT SOUTH CAROLINA BEACH PARTY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GUNSHOTS FIRED AS STUDENTS CELEBRATED "SENIOR SKIP DAY"\par \par \uc2 OBESITY, RESEARCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW STUDY OUT ON OBESITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING DOWN GENETIC & LIFESTYLE FACTORS\par \par \uc2 KENNEDY, WINSTEAD, BORDIZZO, DAWSON, FAVREAU, "STAR WARS"\par \par \uc2 "ON GRIEF", SENIOR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BUZZ PICK\par \par \uc2 DEALS, SHOPPING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "DEALS & STEALS" WITH TORY JOHNSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Oh, what is this music? I like it. Welcome back to "GMA" this Saturday morning.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230510ej480000t\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 RISING TECH STAR CHARGED 31-YEAR-OLD START-UP FOUNDER ACCUSED OF $175M SCHEME\b0\par\par\uc2 490 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DUELING DECISIONS: ABORTION PILL RULINGS\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, WASHINGTON, ABORTION, FDA, BIRTH CONTROL, MCGILL\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, HARRIS, RULING, ABORTION, WOMEN\par \par \uc2 DWYER, FDA, TEXAS, ABORTION, IMPLICATIONS, RULING\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, HARRIS, TN, EXPULSION, JOHNSON, LOWERY\par \par \uc2 PENTAGON, DOCUMENTS, CLASSIFIED, LEAK, UKRAINE, \uc2 NATO\par \par \uc2 CHINA, TAIWAN, MILITARY, EXERCISES\par \par \uc2 VIOLENCE, PASSOVER, RAMADAN, EASTER, MIDDLE EAST\par \par \uc2 JOBS, SLOWING, HIRING\par \par \uc2 POPE, EASTER, GOOD FRIDAY, BRONCHITIS\par \par \uc2 MASTERS, GOLF, KOEPKA, JACKET\par \par \uc2 KINGSBURY, MISSING, MOTHER, MINNESOTA, WILLIAMS, DEGEORGE\par \par \uc2 REID, CRASH, DRUNK DRIVING, ACCIDENT\par \par \uc2 SCHEME, \uc2 JP MORGAN\uc2 , CHARGED, JAVICE, LIEBER\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Welcome back to "gma" and the story of a young tech entrepreneur facing criminal charges now. The 31-year-old is accused of fraud for allegedly trying to lure \uc2 JP Morgan Chase\uc2  so it would acquire her college financial planning startup for $175 million. ABC's Chief Business Correspondent Rebecca Jarvis has the details.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) A prominent CEO in the tech world facing charges. Former Forbes 30 under 30 Frank Founder Charlie Javice accused of defrauding \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2  of over $175 million. Javice is charged with multiple counts of fraud and one count of conspiracy. The Justice Department accusing Javice of falsely and dramatically inflating the number of customers of her company to fraudulently induce \uc2 JP Morgan Chase\uc2  to acquire Frank for $175 million.\par \par \uc2 BRAD GARRETT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) These are very serious charges. When you look at wire fraud and mail fraud, they can carry up to 30 years for each count. When you add securities fraud, that's another 20 years per count.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In 2017, Javice founded Frank, a company that promised prospective students a simpler way to sign up for financial aid. The idea soon catapulting Javice into the spotlight and on camera.\par \par \uc2 CHARLIE JAVICE (FOUNDER OF FRANK)\par \par \uc2 Getting financial aid might seem really, really complicated, but at Frank we've really simplified it for you.\par \par \uc2 RON LIEBER (NEW YORK TIMES)\par \par \uc2 The original promise of Frank was that it was going to help a whole bunch of lower income people in particular make it easier to file their federal financial aid forms.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But authorities say Javice faked data and repeatedly misrepresented numbers, touting that the company had 4.25 million users who signed up for an account. But the real number, according to prosecutors, less than 300,000. When \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2  attempted to verify that information before buying the company, Javice allegedly provided fabricated data. A spokesman for Javice says she denies the allegations. Javice's lawyer, \uc2 Alex Spiro\uc2  declined to comment. Rebecca Jarvis, ABC News, New York.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And our thanks to Rebecca for that report.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COMING UP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BASEBALL STUDY\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Coming up here on "Good Morning America," the baseball study on why homerun hitters may be be having a field day.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230510ej480000h\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 DEALS & STEALS ON THE GO\b0\par\par\uc2 1,436 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DUELING DECISIONS: ABORTION PILL RULINGS\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, WASHINGTON, ABORTION, FDA, BIRTH CONTROL, MCGILL\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, HARRIS, RULING, ABORTION, WOMEN\par \par \uc2 DWYER, FDA, TEXAS, ABORTION, IMPLICATIONS, RULING\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, HARRIS, TN, EXPULSION, JOHNSON, LOWERY\par \par \uc2 PENTAGON, DOCUMENTS, CLASSIFIED, LEAK, UKRAINE, \uc2 NATO\par \par \uc2 CHINA, TAIWAN, MILITARY, EXERCISES\par \par \uc2 VIOLENCE, PASSOVER, RAMADAN, EASTER, MIDDLE EAST\par \par \uc2 JOBS, SLOWING, HIRING\par \par \uc2 POPE, EASTER, GOOD FRIDAY, BRONCHITIS\par \par \uc2 MASTERS, GOLF, KOEPKA, JACKET\par \par \uc2 KINGSBURY, MISSING, MOTHER, MINNESOTA, WILLIAMS, DEGEORGE\par \par \uc2 REID, C