r \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, and I actually yeah, I used this on a zero-gravity flight.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right. So, most of us won't necessarily go on a zero-gravity flight.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But there are other reasons that we are feeling nauseous, this is the band. And so, typically, it's like, you know, people have this for motion sickness. But sometimes, quite frankly, it's like chemotherapy, there's other reasons that people can feel nauseous. And so, by wearing this relief band, it's a drug-free way to have these pulses sent that help to tell the stomach that everything is okay. It makes this connection between the brain and the stomach and relieves nausea immediately. Very quick relief and (inaudible).\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And listen, it worked during that flight. It did, I felt those little, it felt like little pricks.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Absolutely. There's a lot of people use this who swear by it. We've got four different types to choose from. All of them today or 50% off and free shipping, which we love.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: $5-%140 + FREE SHIPPING FOR GMA, 50% OFF\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Awesome. Okay, shoes, shoes, shoes.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALIGN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: $100-$110 ORIGINAL\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Next up, yes, Align by Nursemaid. So, these are shoes that are developed by health care professionals but are really for everybody. And they've got an innovative footbed that contours to the foot.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And great soles.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Really good soles. What's great, too, I'll mention the soles is that they're designed specifically are for wet or d