 Of course, she is. Okay, keep charged up on the go. So, this is...\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, I need this.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AQUA VAULT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: $60 ORIGINAL\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right, so that's, it's called the Charge Card from Aqua Vault and it fits literally into a credit card slot in your wallet.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) This is so cool.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And it comes with all the cords. So, whether you use an Android or an iPhone, it's got those plugs right in there for you. It's going to keep you powered up and it doesn't add bulk which I love, $29.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: $29 FOR GMA, 51%\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, that's awesome, that's really cool. Okay, glasses.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Another brilliant one, Thin Optics. So, look literally how thin those are in that case.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THIN OPTICS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: $32-$60 ORIGINAL\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What's perfect about these is you take your glasses anywhere and everywhere. They're always with you. So, you will never get caught wondering why I didn't bring my readers for that menu in the restaurant.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, this is awesome for travel, this is really cool.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So smart for travel, but truly anywhere you go you want your Thin Optics with you, 50% off, these start at $16.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: $16-$30 FOR GMA\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We've got both readers and blue blockers in a variety of strengths. Get in on this one.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And then, finally, whether you are coming or going, why not be greeted with a custom mat from Letter Folk?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LETTER FOLK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: $36-$111 ORIGINAL\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What I love is that these are vintage hexagon-style tiles.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's so cool.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, you can make any words or patterns that you want. It comes black-and-white but you also have a lot of optional additional tiles. This is a really fabulous one whether you put it at your front door, used in the kitchen, anywhere you stop and you need a little extra comfort. This one's for you. Everything today half-price, $18 to $55.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: $18-$55 FOR GMA, 50% OFF\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I feel like we need to make this one part of our set.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, right? It could be.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you, Tory. Check out the deals with the QR code and we'll be right back here on "Good Morning America." Stick around.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 STORY SYNOPSES\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230510ej480000s\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 TEXAS JUDGE SUSPENDS \uc2 FDA\uc2  APPROVAL OF ABORTION PILL RULING PUTS ACCESS TO ABORTION AND OTHER BIRTH CONTROLS AT RISK\b0\par\par\uc2 612 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DUELING DECISIONS: ABORTION PILL RULINGS\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, WASHINGTON, ABORTION, \uc2 FDA\uc2 , BIRTH CONTROL, MCGILL\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, HARRIS, RULING, ABORTION, WOMEN\par \par \uc2 DWYER, \uc2 FDA\uc2 , TEXAS, ABORTION, IMPLICATIONS, RULING\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, HARRIS, TN, EXPULSION, JOHNSON, LOWERY\par \par \uc2 PENTAGON, DOCUMENTS, CLASSIFIED, LEAK, UKRAINE, \uc2 NATO\par \par \uc2 CHINA, TAIWAN, MILITARY, EXERCISES\par \par \uc2 VIOLENCE, PASSOVER, RAMADAN, EASTER, MIDDLE EAST\par \par \uc2 JOBS, SLOWING, HIRING\par \par \uc2 POPE, EASTER, GOOD FRIDAY, BRONCHITIS\par \par \uc2 MASTERS, GOLF, KOEPKA, JACKET\par \par \uc2 KINGSBURY, MISSING, MOTHER, MINNESOTA, WILLIAMS, DEGEORGE\par \par \uc2 REID, CRASH, DRUNK DRIVING, ACCIDENT\par \par \uc2 SCHEME, \uc2 JP MORGAN\uc2 , CHARGED, JAVICE, LIEBER\par \par \uc2 HOME RUNS, CLIMATE CHANGE, SCIENCE, CALLAHAN, OLNEY\par \par \uc2 NEGRON, NATIONAL ANTHEM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, RULINGS, HAWKINS, MCGILL\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We do have a busy morning here, so we're going to begin with that unprecedented ruling by a Texas judge.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS JUDGE SUSPENDS \uc2 FDA\uc2  APPROVAL OF ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RULING PUTS ACCESS TO ABORTION AND OTHER BIRTH CONTROLS AT RISK\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The decision could further restrict abortion access. The Trump appointee issuing a decision to suspend the \uc2 FDA\uc2  approval of mifepristone, overruling decades of scientific approval.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This as another judge in Washington quickly issued a conflicting ruling ordering the \uc2 FDA\uc2  to keep the drug available. ABC's Zohreen Shah is back with what this all means. Zohreen, good morning again.\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Gio, when we think of abortion, we often think of a type of surgery. But the CDC says, more than half of all abortions rely on medication. This Texas ruling could dramatically change that.\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, a major ruling from a Texas federal judge halting the \uc2 FDA\uc2 's approval of mifepristone, the first of two drugs given to abort a pregnancy in the first trimester. The judge says in the ruling that the \uc2 FDA\uc2 's more than 20-year approval is a violation of federal law around accelerated approval of certain drugs.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS FEDERAL JUDGE RULING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WA U.S. DISTRICT JUDGE THOMAS O. RICE\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And overnight, a federal judge in Washington state issuing a ruling protecting access to the abortion drug, preventing the \uc2 FDA\uc2  from altering the status quo and rights as it relates to the availability of mifepristone. The dueling opinions creating uncertainty about access to the key abortion drug. The Justice Department has appealed the Texas ruling. And that means all eyes are now on the Fifth Circuit, which happens to be the country's most conservative appeals court.\par \par \uc2 KRISTAN HAWKINS (PRESIDENT STUDENTS FOR LIFE OF AMERICA)\par \par \uc2 What we're advocating against are direct abortions, intentional abortions. Seeing the reversal of Roe was a great triumph, but it's very much phase one in our movement.\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The \uc2 FDA\uc2  has approved mifepristone for the last 23 years.\par \par \uc2 ALEXIS MCGILL (PRESIDENT & CEO PLANNED PARENTHOOD)\par \par \uc2 How is it that one person, one judge, with no medical degree, no science degree, can make a decision about a drug that has been used, that has been safe and proven effective?\par \par \uc2 ACTIVIST (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Women have the right to have abortions. And you can't turn the rights around, it's not okay.\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The future of the abortion drug will then likely rest in the hands of the Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Critics say this decision will likely go beyond abortion. They believe it can motivate conservatives to challenge other \uc2 FDA\uc2 -approved drugs and vaccines. Janai?\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Zohreen, thank you for that update.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230510ej480000l\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 THE AUDIOBOOK BOOM KATE & CHARLIE GIBSON ARE ALL EARS FOR LATEST LITERARY TREND\b0\par\par\uc2 1,147 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DUELING DECISIONS: ABORTION PILL RULINGS\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, WASHINGTON, ABORTION, FDA, BIRTH CONTROL, MCGILL\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, HARRIS, RULING, ABORTION, WOMEN\par \par \uc2 DWYER, FDA, TEXAS, ABORTION, IMPLICATIONS, RULING\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, HARRIS, TN, EXPULSION, JOHNSON, LOWERY\par \par \uc2 PENTAGON, DOCUMENTS, CLASSIFIED, LEAK, UKRAINE, \uc2 NATO\par \par \uc2 CHINA, TAIWAN, MILITARY, EXERCISES\par \par \uc2 VIOLENCE, PASSOVER, RAMADAN, EASTER, MIDDLE EAST\par \par \uc2 JOBS, SLOWING, HIRING\par \par \uc2 POPE, EASTER, GOOD FRIDAY, BRONCHITIS\par \par \uc2 MASTERS, GOLF, KOEPKA, JACKET\par \par \uc2 KINGSBURY, MISSING, MOTHER, MINNESOTA, WILLIAMS, DEGEORGE\par \par \uc2 REID, CRASH, DRUNK DRIVING, ACCIDENT\par \par \uc2 SCHEME, \uc2 JP MORGAN\uc2 , CHARGED, JAVICE, LIEBER\par \par \uc2 HOME RUNS, CLIMATE CHANGE, SCIENCE, CALLAHAN, OLNEY\par \par \uc2 NEGRON, NATIONAL ANTHEM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, RULINGS, HAWKINS, MCGILL\par \par \uc2 JONES, JOHNSON, PEARSON, GUN REFORM\par \par \uc2 BEACH, SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SIX INJURED AT SOUTH CAROLINA BEACH PARTY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GUNSHOTS FIRED AS STUDENTS CELEBRATED "SENIOR SKIP DAY"\par \par \uc2 OBESITY, RESEARCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW STUDY OUT ON OBESITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING DOWN GENETIC & LIFESTYLE FACTORS\par \par \uc2 KENNEDY, WINSTEAD, BORDIZZO, DAWSON, FAVREAU, "STAR WARS"\par \par \uc2 "ON GRIEF", SENIOR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BUZZ PICK\par \par \uc2 DEALS, SHOPPING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "DEALS & STEALS" WITH TORY JOHNSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 BOSE, "DIRTY LAUNDRY"\par \par \uc2 YOUSAFZAI, "JOYLAND", SADIQ\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MALALA'S NEXT CHAPTER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NOBEL LAUREATE TURNED OSCAR-NOMINEE OPENS UP ABOUT REDEFINING HERSELF\par \par \uc2 AUDIOBOOK, GIBSON, COBEN, WEBER, BARONE, VACKER\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to the audiobook "Business Boom." Kate and Charlie Gibson host of the podcast "The Book Case," turning a page on the growing popularity of pressing play, take a look.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE AUDIOBOOK BOOM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: KATE & CHARLIE GIBSON ARE ALL EARS FOR LATEST LITERARY TREND\par \par \uc2 KATE GIBSON (HOST "THE BOOK CASE" PODCAST)\par \par \uc2 These days, reading looks and sounds a lot different than it used to.\par \par \uc2 CHARLIE GIBSON (HOST "THE BOOK CASE" PODCAST)\par \par \uc2 Audiobooks have unlocked the world of storytelling for readers of all skill levels, thousands of books just a few taps away.\par \par \uc2 KATE GIBSON (HOST "THE BOOK CASE" PODCAST)\par \par \uc2 And the industry is booming. Audio is the fastest growing in publishing with a projected value of $35 billion by 2030.\par \par \uc2 CHARLIE GIBSON (HOST "THE BOOK CASE" PODCAST)\par \par \uc2 Best-selling author Harlan Coben says it's the ease of access that makes audiobooks so appealing.\par \par \uc2 HARLAN COBEN (AUTHOR "I WILL FIND YOU")\par \par \uc2 I really think one of the things that have made audio so big now is how great the technology is on it now. You can carry it on your phone, you can listen in the car, you can listen in your bedroom. You can listen while walking. And this is very convenient, and I think that helps.\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM TV SERIES, "WINGS"\par \par \uc2 STEVEN WEBER (ACTOR AND AUDIOBOOK NARRATOR)\par \par \uc2 Ladies and gentlemen, we're about to begin our final descent.\par \par \uc2 KATE GIBSON (HOST "THE BOOK CASE" PODCAST)\par \par \uc2 Actor Steven Weber is the voice behind a handful of Harlan's audiobooks.\par \par \uc2 STEVEN WEBER (ACTOR AND AUDIOBOOK NARRATOR)\par \par \uc2 I didn't do it. I didn't kill my son. I know I didn't. I know.\par \par \uc2 CHARLIE GIBSON (HOST "THE BOOK CASE" PODCAST)\par \par \uc2 A job he landed after he reached out to Harlan to tell him how much he loved his work.\par \par \uc2 CHARLIE GIBSON (HOST "THE BOOK CASE" PODCAST)\par \par \uc2 How did this partnership come about?\par \par \uc2 STEVEN WEBER (ACTOR AND AUDIOBOOK NARRATOR)\par \par \uc2 I have taken the opportunity to fanboy several people who I have admired or whose work I admired because I figured I'd just reach out there and show my appreciation. It just so happened that Harlan responded in a way that I could not have dreamed of.\par \par \uc2 KATE GIBSON (HOST "THE BOOK CASE" PODCAST)\par \par \uc2 In my research, I read that you narrated one of your own books. Is this true? How was it and what was your process?\par \par \uc2 HARLAN COBEN (AUTHOR "I WILL FIND YOU")\par \par \uc2 Yes, I did read the audio for one of my books. I've made sure that every copy has been burned or deleted. I speak too fast. They kept telling me to slow down and different voices, it's really actually a lot of work. And I would rather leave it to Steven Weber and talented people like that to do it.\par \par \uc2 KATE GIBSON (HOST "THE BOOK CASE" PODCAST)\par \par \uc2 Just like Steven, many of the narrators are trained actors.\par \par \uc2 KARISSA VACKER (ACTRESS AND AUDIOBOOK NARRATOR)\par \par \uc2 Is that okay with you? None of this is okay with me, Mike.\par \par \uc2 CHARLIE GIBSON (HOST "THE BOOK CASE" PODCAST)\par \par \uc2 Karissa Vacker is one of them. She's voiced more than 300 novels.\par \par \uc2 KARISSA VACKER (ACTRESS AND AUDIOBOOK NARRATOR)\par \par \uc2 One single unspoken question lingered among us all. Who's next?\par \par \uc2 KARISSA VACKER (ACTRESS AND AUDIOBOOK NARRATOR)\par \par \uc2 Something that I often do is I cast characters. So, like, I might cast them from somebody in my life or a TV or film or something, so I have a really clear visual sense of what that person looks like, which makes it easier for me to give them a different vocal quality.\par \par \uc2 KATE GIBSON (HOST "THE BOOK CASE" PODCAST)\par \par \uc2 Karissa took us behind the scenes at McMillan Audio as she recorded her latest narration, "Night Will Find You" by Julia Heaberlin.\par \par \uc2 KARISSA VACKER (ACTRESS AND AUDIOBOOK NARRATOR)\par \par \uc2 I snatched the photograph and tucking it with the others.\par \par \uc2 CHARLIE GIBSON (HOST "THE BOOK CASE" PODCAST)\par \par \uc2 Sometimes she works with a director.\par \par \uc2 SALVATORE BARONE (STUDIO SOUND MANAGER)\par \par \uc2 One more time there, a little more desperate.\par \par \uc2 CHARLIE GIBSON (HOST "THE BOOK CASE" PODCAST)\par \par \uc2 Who gives her pointers along the way.\par \par \uc2 SALVATORE BARONE (STUDIO SOUND MANAGER)\par \par \uc2 There needs to be somebody that oversee the whole process and just make sure there is consistency throughout the book.\par \par \uc2 KATE GIBSON (HOST "THE BOOK CASE" PODCAST)\par \par \uc2 Karissa says readers will be delighted to find audiobooks help them visualize books in an entirely new way.\par \par \uc2 KARISSA VACKER (ACTRESS AND AUDIOBOOK NARRATOR)\par \par \uc2 A lot of people are surprised when they've never listened to audiobooks how immersive of an experience it is that we do voices for the various characters. That it is a movie for their brain and they don't expect that.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I love that story, the behind the scenes.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Very cool.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You've that sultry voice ready? Ready to go?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I don't think so. Janai is ready for it.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Used that QR code to...\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, that was...\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You should have kept going, that was good.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Exasperated.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Keep it going. Speaking of the QR code, you can find the latest episode of "The Book Case" with Kate and Charlie Gibson. New episodes every Thursday.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And coming up, oh, so easy sheet pan toaster pastries and more one-pan wonders perfect for the holiday weekend. We'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230510ej480000x\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 DESPERATE SEARCH FOR MISSING MINNESOTA MOTHER HUNDREDS JOIN SEARCH AS POLICE CALL DISAPPEARANCE "SUSPICIOUS"\b0\par\par\uc2 587 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DUELING DECISIONS: ABORTION PILL RULINGS\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, WASHINGTON, ABORTION, FDA, BIRTH CONTROL, MCGILL\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, HARRIS, RULING, ABORTION, WOMEN\par \par \uc2 DWYER, FDA, TEXAS, ABORTION, IMPLICATIONS, RULING\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, HARRIS, TN, EXPULSION, JOHNSON, LOWERY\par \par \uc2 PENTAGON, DOCUMENTS, CLASSIFIED, LEAK, UKRAINE, \uc2 NATO\par \par \uc2 CHINA, TAIWAN, MILITARY, EXERCISES\par \par \uc2 VIOLENCE, PASSOVER, RAMADAN, EASTER, MIDDLE EAST\par \par \uc2 JOBS, SLOWING, HIRING\par \par \uc2 POPE, EASTER, GOOD FRIDAY, BRONCHITIS\par \par \uc2 MASTERS, GOLF, KOEPKA, JACKET\par \par \uc2 KINGSBURY, MISSING, MOTHER, MINNESOTA, WILLIAMS, DEGEORGE\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We do start this half hour, though, with a search for a missing mother last seen more than a week ago. Nearly 2,000 volunteers joining in the effort to find Madeline Kingsbury. Police calling her disappearance suspicious. ABC's Jaclyn Lee is here with more. Jaclyn, good morning.\par \par \uc2 JACLYN LEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Janai, good morning. Officials in Minnesota are calling this an endangered missing persons case. The missing mom's family speaking to ABC News, desperate to find her alive. Police receiving hundreds of leads, but still no sign.\par \par \uc2 JACLYN LEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, the desperate search to find a missing Minnesota mom of two who disappeared eight days ago.\par \par \uc2 MEGAN KINGSBURY (MADELINE'S SISTER)\par \par \uc2 Please help us find Madeline. The children need their mother.\par \par \uc2 JACLYN LEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Winona Police officials say 26-year-old Madeline "Mattie" Kingsbury's disappearance is suspicious and they are worried for her safety.\par \par \uc2 CHIEF TOM WILLIAMS (WINONA POLICE DEPARTMENT)\par \par \uc2 Our department and our law enforcement partners are working relentlessly to find Mattie and determine the circumstances surrounding her disappearance.\par \par \uc2 JACLYN LEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Nearly 2,000 volunteers showed up on Friday to help police conduct a massive ground search. Officials pleading with residents to search their properties for signs of the 26-year-old.\par \par \uc2 SHERIFF JOHN DEGEORGE (FILLMORE COUNTY MINNESOTA)\par \par \uc2 Walk your acreage, check your outbuildings, check your vehicles, walk trails, check your cameras for any indications of anything suspicious.\par \par \uc2 JACLYN LEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) According to police, Mattie was last seen at home last Friday at approximately 8:15 in the morning after dropping her two children off with their father at day care. The father told police he left Mattie's house at about 10:00 AM in her dark blue Chrysler minivan. When he returned later that day, he says she was not home. A minivan resembling hers was seen that same morning driving along a nearby county road between 10:30 AM and 1:30 PM. Investigators have searched the minivan and Mattie's home. Inside the house, they found her phone and her wallet.\par \par \uc2 MEGAN KINGSBURY (MADELINE'S SISTER)\par \par \uc2 I just was trying not to panic.\par \par \uc2 JACLYN LEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Mattie's sister, Megan last texted her that morning and everything seemed fine. The family now offering a $50,000 reward for information on her whereabouts.\par \par \uc2 MEGAN KINGSBURY (MADELINE'S SISTER)\par \par \uc2 We love her and we could figure out anything and get through anything together. And we want her back, and we're not, we're not going to stop.\par \par \uc2 JACLYN LEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And police say they don't have any suspects and there is no indication that Mattie left her house on foot or in another car. The police chief declined to say whether the father is participating in the search and would not comment if he is cooperating with authorities. Gio.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Jaclyn, let's hope they find her. Thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230510ej480000e\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 TEXAS JUDGE SUSPENDS FDA APPROVAL OF ABORTION PILL WHAT ARE THE IMPLICATIONS AND NEXT STEPS AFTER THE RULING?\b0\par\par\uc2 296 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DUELING DECISIONS: ABORTION PILL RULINGS\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, WASHINGTON, ABORTION, FDA, BIRTH CONTROL, MCGILL\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, HARRIS, RULING, ABORTION, WOMEN\par \par \uc2 DWYER, FDA, TEXAS, ABORTION, IMPLICATIONS, RULING\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And bringing in our Senior Washington reporter Devin Dwyer, who covers the courts for us. S, Devin, what are the implications of these rulings going forward?\par \par \uc2 DEVIN DWYER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The implications are significant, Whit. They are sweeping. If this stands, as you heard Zohreen report there, it would apply nationwide, even in states where abortion is legal. And that could mean a dramatic reduction into the most commonly used form of abortion in this country, which is medication. In fact, we took a look, 40 percent of abortion clinics in this country only offer abortion pills, so a lot on the line. We should say for at least the next seven days, the fda approval and use of this drug will stand. It's status quo, but this is expected to rocket through the court system, these two competing rulings we've been talking about, one striking down FDA approval of Mifepristone, the other one ordering it to keep the status quo is all but guarantees that the Supreme Court will have to get involved. There is no clear timeline for that yet. It's also not clear how these Justices might vote on this issue. The key question, Whit, which we're going to be watching is will they allow use of Mifepristone to continue as they sort this out? We just don't know right now.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, that is the big question. Devon, thank you. Janai.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230510ej4800004\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT MEETS WITH OUSTED LAWMAKERS SPEAKS WITH THREE TN LEGISLATORS WHO FACED EXPULSION VOTE\b0\par\par\uc2 613 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DUELING DECISIONS: ABORTION PILL RULINGS\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, WASHINGTON, ABORTION, FDA, BIRTH CONTROL, MCGILL\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, HARRIS, RULING, ABORTION, WOMEN\par \par \uc2 DWYER, FDA, TEXAS, ABORTION, IMPLICATIONS, RULING\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, HARRIS, TN, EXPULSION, JOHNSON, LOWERY\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Whit. Now the three Tennessee lawmakers who face an expulsion vote in the state legislature getting strong support from the White House. The three Democrats speaking with President Biden in a video call and getting a visit from Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . ABC's Faith Abubey has more reaction to the extraordinary punishment and what could be next for the two of them ousted from their positions. Faith, good morning.\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning to you, Janai. One of the things that has outraged many in this community is the fact a partisan expulsion like this just doesn't happen around here. In fact, this is the first time in Tennessee's modern-day history and the ousted lawmakers happen to be black.\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Overnight, Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  meeting with all three Democratic lawmakers who face an extremely rare Republican-led expulsion vote this week.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 The truth must never be stifled or silenced when it is on behalf of the people.\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This video after their meeting with the Vice President showing Justin Pearson, Gloria Johnson, and Justin Jones standing together, arms locked. President Biden also video conferencing with the trio and inviting them to the White House. The lawmakers accused of violating Tennessee State House decorum when they joined protests last week calling for stricter gun laws in the wake of the Nashville Covenant School shooting that killed six people, including three children. The House Republican leadership warning them against bringing the protest onto the House floor, but the group doing just that with bullhorns after their microphones were cut off. The move temporarily disrupting House business. Days later, the Republican super majority ousting duly elected Democrats Justin Pearson and Justin Jones.\par \par \uc2 SPEAKER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 I hereby declare Representative Justin J Pearson of the 86th Representative District expelled.\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Gloria Johnson, a white woman, was the only one who survived the expulsion vote.\par \par \uc2 GLORIA JOHNSON (TN REPRESENTATIVE)\par \par \uc2 It might have to do with the color of our skin.\par \par \uc2 SPEAKER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 They played the video. It clearly showed her standing there not doing as much. It had nothing to do with the color of their skin.\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) With Pearson and Jones gone, more than 100,000 people in their district are now without representation in the Tennessee State House until county commissioners name their replacements. Members of Nashville's Metro Council and the Shelby County Board of Commissioners now considering reappointing the lawmakers back to their seats.\par \par \uc2 MICKELL LOWERY (CHAIRMAN SHELBY COUNTY BOARD OF COMMISSIONERS)\par \par \uc2 It doesn't make any sense, so we are looking forward to having a special call meeting to consider appointing Justin Pearson back to the seat that he was duly elected to by the citizens.\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And there is growing momentum and growing support for the reappointment of those lawmakers, but it is not clear, at this point, whether the legislature will try to block that. In the meantime, though, these lawmakers will be able to rerun for their seats in their district in any upcoming elections. Gio.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, as you said, the first time this has happened in Tennessee's modern history. Faith, thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230510ej4800005\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WEATHER\b0\par\par\uc2 352 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DUELING DECISIONS: ABORTION PILL RULINGS\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, WASHINGTON, ABORTION, FDA, BIRTH CONTROL, MCGILL\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, HARRIS, RULING, ABORTION, WOMEN\par \par \uc2 DWYER, FDA, TEXAS, ABORTION, IMPLICATIONS, RULING\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, HARRIS, TN, EXPULSION, JOHNSON, LOWERY\par \par \uc2 PENTAGON, DOCUMENTS, CLASSIFIED, LEAK, UKRAINE, \uc2 NATO\par \par \uc2 CHINA, TAIWAN, MILITARY, EXERCISES\par \par \uc2 VIOLENCE, PASSOVER, RAMADAN, EASTER, MIDDLE EAST\par \par \uc2 JOBS, SLOWING, HIRING\par \par \uc2 POPE, EASTER, GOOD FRIDAY, BRONCHITIS\par \par \uc2 MASTERS, GOLF, KOEPKA, JACKET\par \par \uc2 KINGSBURY, MISSING, MOTHER, MINNESOTA, WILLIAMS, DEGEORGE\par \par \uc2 REID, CRASH, DRUNK DRIVING, ACCIDENT\par \par \uc2 SCHEME, \uc2 JP MORGAN\uc2 , CHARGED, JAVICE, LIEBER\par \par \uc2 HOME RUNS, CLIMATE CHANGE, SCIENCE, CALLAHAN, OLNEY\par \par \uc2 NEGRON, NATIONAL ANTHEM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, RULINGS, HAWKINS, MCGILL\par \par \uc2 JONES, JOHNSON, PEARSON, GUN REFORM\par \par \uc2 BEACH, SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SIX INJURED AT SOUTH CAROLINA BEACH PARTY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GUNSHOTS FIRED AS STUDENTS CELEBRATED "SENIOR SKIP DAY"\par \par \uc2 OBESITY, RESEARCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW STUDY OUT ON OBESITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING DOWN GENETIC & LIFESTYLE FACTORS\par \par \uc2 KENNEDY, WINSTEAD, BORDIZZO, DAWSON, FAVREAU, "STAR WARS"\par \par \uc2 "ON GRIEF", SENIOR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BUZZ PICK\par \par \uc2 DEALS, SHOPPING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "DEALS & STEALS" WITH TORY JOHNSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 BOSE, "DIRTY LAUNDRY"\par \par \uc2 YOUSAFZAI, "JOYLAND", SADIQ\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MALALA'S NEXT CHAPTER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NOBEL LAUREATE TURNED OSCAR-NOMINEE OPENS UP ABOUT REDEFINING HERSELF\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right. Now, we're going to send it back to Somara for another check of the weather. Hey, Somara.\par \par \uc2 SOMARA THEODORE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning. Hey, Janai. Hey, team. And good morning. New London, Connecticut, the sun rising in the eastern sky before it dies in the west. We are looking at temperatures around 50 degrees today, which is great news for the \uc2 UConn\uc2  basketball team victory parade today taking place at Hartford, Connecticut not too far there. So, congratulations to you.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUMMER, IS THAT YOU?\par \par \uc2 SOMARA THEODORE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And congratulations to everyone in the East Coast look at this. Are we outside on Thursday? Philadelphia, 84 degrees. Hartford, 80. Pittsburgh, 83. New York, I know, you're not out there, but we're in 80s on Thursday and Friday as well. That's a look at your forecast. Let's see what's going on in your neighborhood.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NATIONAL MAP\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230510ej480000w\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 TEXAS JUDGE SUSPENDS \uc2 FDA\uc2  APPROVAL OF ABORTION PILL RULING PUTS ACCESS TO ABORTION AND OTHER BIRTH CONTROL AT RISK\b0\par\par\uc2 510 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DUELING DECISIONS: ABORTION PILL RULINGS\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, WASHINGTON, ABORTION, \uc2 FDA\uc2 , BIRTH CONTROL, MCGILL\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And we being with an unprecedented ruling by a Texas judge that could further restrict abortion access.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, the judge deciding, issuing this decision to suspend the fda approval of an abortion pill that's been in use for more than two decades.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But right away, another judge in Washington State issued a separate ruling, ordering the fda to keep the drug available. ABC's Zohreen Shah is in LA to begin our team coverage on what this all could mean. Zohreen, good morning.\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Gio, when we think of abortion, we often think of a type of surgery, but according to the CDC, more than half of all abortions rely on medication, and this ruling in Texas could dramatically change that.\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, a major ruling from a Texas federal judge halting the \uc2 FDA\uc2 's approval of Mifepristone, the first of two drugs given to abort a pregnancy in the first trimester. The judge says in the ruling that the fda's more than 20-year approval is a violation of federal law around accelerated approval for certain drugs. And overnight, a federal judge in Washington State issuing a ruling protecting access to the abortion drug, preventing the \uc2 FDA\uc2  from altering the status quo and rights as it relates to the availability of Mifepristone. The dueling opinions creating uncertainty about access to the key abortion drug. The Justice Department has appealed the Texas ruling, and that means all eyes are now on the Fifth Circuit, which happens to be the country's most conservative appeals court.\par \par \uc2 SPEAKER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 What we're advocating against are direct abortions, intentional abortions. Seeing the reversal of Roe was a great triumph, but it was very much phase one in our movement.\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The fda has approved Mifepristone for the last 23 years.\par \par \uc2 ALEXIS MCGILL (PRESIDENT & CEO PLANNED PARENTHOOD)\par \par \uc2 How is it that one person, one judge with no medical degree, no science degree, can make a decision about a drug that has been used, that has been safe, and proven effective?\par \par \uc2 SPEAKER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Women have the right to have abortions, and you can't turn the rights around. That's not okay.\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The future of the abortion drug will then likely rest in the hands of the Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Critics say this decision will likely go beyond abortion. They believe it could motivate conservatives to challenge other fda approved drugs and vaccines. So, another example is HIV medications, and it could also discourage companies from even investing time and resources into products that could become political targets in court. Whit.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Zohreen, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230510ej4800002\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 GMA BUZZ PICK "ON GRIEF" JENNIFER SENIOR\b0\par\par\uc2 349 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DUELING DECISIONS: ABORTION PILL RULINGS\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, WASHINGTON, ABORTION, FDA, BIRTH CONTROL, MCGILL\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, HARRIS, RULING, ABORTION, WOMEN\par \par \uc2 DWYER, FDA, TEXAS, ABORTION, IMPLICATIONS, RULING\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, HARRIS, TN, EXPULSION, JOHNSON, LOWERY\par \par \uc2 PENTAGON, DOCUMENTS, CLASSIFIED, LEAK, UKRAINE, \uc2 NATO\par \par \uc2 CHINA, TAIWAN, MILITARY, EXERCISES\par \par \uc2 VIOLENCE, PASSOVER, RAMADAN, EASTER, MIDDLE EAST\par \par \uc2 JOBS, SLOWING, HIRING\par \par \uc2 POPE, EASTER, GOOD FRIDAY, BRONCHITIS\par \par \uc2 MASTERS, GOLF, KOEPKA, JACKET\par \par \uc2 KINGSBURY, MISSING, MOTHER, MINNESOTA, WILLIAMS, DEGEORGE\par \par \uc2 REID, CRASH, DRUNK DRIVING, ACCIDENT\par \par \uc2 SCHEME, \uc2 JP MORGAN\uc2 , CHARGED, JAVICE, LIEBER\par \par \uc2 HOME RUNS, CLIMATE CHANGE, SCIENCE, CALLAHAN, OLNEY\par \par \uc2 NEGRON, NATIONAL ANTHEM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, RULINGS, HAWKINS, MCGILL\par \par \uc2 JONES, JOHNSON, PEARSON, GUN REFORM\par \par \uc2 BEACH, SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SIX INJURED AT SOUTH CAROLINA BEACH PARTY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GUNSHOTS FIRED AS STUDENTS CELEBRATED "SENIOR SKIP DAY"\par \par \uc2 OBESITY, RESEARCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW STUDY OUT ON OBESITY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING DOWN GENETIC & LIFESTYLE FACTORS\par \par \uc2 KENNEDY, WINSTEAD, BORDIZZO, DAWSON, FAVREAU, "STAR WARS"\par \par \uc2 "ON GRIEF", SENIOR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BUZZ PICK\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to Saturday's "GMA Buzz Pick." It's the Pulitzer prize-winning story called "On Grief." It's by Jennifer Senior. And it is a powerful read for anyone coping with loss no matter how big or how small. Here's Jennifer with more.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "ON GRIEF" JENNIFER SENIOR\par \par \uc2 JENNIFER SENIOR (AUTHOR "ON GRIEF")\par \par \uc2 Good morning, America. My hope is that anyone who has ever grieved will read this book and feel less alone. The truth is we do not mourn logically. We mourn idiosyncratically in our own strange and beautiful ways. This is a story of one family that lost their oldest child and how very, very differently everyone in that family grieved. It's also a story about a long-lost diary, about the tricks of memory and, most important, about the power of love.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The power of love. "On Grief" is available now. And coming up, more from the "GMA Book Club." We have our April author here live in the studio and keep reading along with us on our \uc2 Instagram\uc2  @gmabookclub.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230510ej480000q\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 SIX INJURED AT SOUTH CAROLINA BEACH PARTY GUNSHOTS FIRED AS STUDENTS CELEBRATED "SENIOR SKIP DAY"\b0\par\par\uc2 352 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DUELING DECISIONS: ABORTION PILL RULINGS\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, WASHINGTON, ABORTION, FDA, BIRTH CONTROL, MCGILL\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, HARRIS, RULING, ABORTION, WOMEN\par \par \uc2 DWYER, FDA, TEXAS, ABORTION, IMPLICATIONS, RULING\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, HARRIS, TN, EXPULSION, JOHNSON, LOWERY\par \par \uc2 PENTAGON, DOCUMENTS, CLASSIFIED, LEAK, UKRAINE, \uc2 NATO\par \par \uc2 CHINA, TAIWAN, MILITARY, EXERCISES\par \par \uc2 VIOLENCE, PASSOVER, RAMADAN, EASTER, MIDDLE EAST\par \par \uc2 JOBS, SLOWING, HIRING\par \par \uc2 POPE, EASTER, GOOD FRIDAY, BRONCHITIS\par \par \uc2 MASTERS, GOLF, KOEPKA, JACKET\par \par \uc2 KINGSBURY, MISSING, MOTHER, MINNESOTA, WILLIAMS, DEGEORGE\par \par \uc2 REID, CRASH, DRUNK DRIVING, ACCIDENT\par \par \uc2 SCHEME, \uc2 JP MORGAN\uc2 , CHARGED, JAVICE, LIEBER\par \par \uc2 HOME RUNS, CLIMATE CHANGE, SCIENCE, CALLAHAN, OLNEY\par \par \uc2 NEGRON, NATIONAL ANTHEM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 ABORTION PILL, RULINGS, HAWKINS, MCGILL\par \par \uc2 JONES, JOHNSON, PEARSON, GUN REFORM\par \par \uc2 BEACH, SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SIX INJURED AT SOUTH CAROLINA BEACH PARTY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GUNSHOTS FIRED AS STUDENTS CELEBRATED "SENIOR SKIP DAY"\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Switching gears here, six people were injured when gunshots were fired at a beach party filled of high schoolers in South Carolina.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The students were participating in what is known as a Senior Skip Day. Police say five of the six people injured were teenagers. They said a couple of altercations took place on the beach during the day. Just so scary.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It really is.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah. Frightening scene there.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA MORNING MENU\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IN 3 MINUTES, NEW OBESITY STUDY\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Coming up on our "GMA Morning Menu," and the new study out on obesity, what researchers are saying about genetic and lifestyle factors.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IN 8 MINUTES, DEALS &STEALS\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Also ahead, "Deals & Steals" we are on the go with gifts and gadgets you don't want to miss. There's Tory.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEXT HALF HOUR, DISHA BOSE LIVE!\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And in our next half hour, the author behind the "GMA Book Club" April pick "Dirty Laundry" is here. There she is. Disha Bose joins live. We'll be right back here on "GMA."\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230510ej480000n\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 VIOLENCE ESCALATING IN MIDDLE EAST DEADLY ATTACKS AS EASTER, RAMADAN, AND PASSOVER COINCIDE\b0\par\par\uc2 455 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DUELING DECISIONS: ABORTION PILL RULINGS\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, WASHINGTON, ABORTION, FDA, BIRTH CONTROL, MCGILL\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, HARRIS, RULING, ABORTION, WOMEN\par \par \uc2 DWYER, FDA, TEXAS, ABORTION, IMPLICATIONS, RULING\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, HARRIS, TN, EXPULSION, JOHNSON, LOWERY\par \par \uc2 PENTAGON, DOCUMENTS, CLASSIFIED, LEAK, UKRAINE, \uc2 NATO\par \par \uc2 CHINA, TAIWAN, MILITARY, EXERCISES\par \par \uc2 VIOLENCE, PASSOVER, RAMADAN, EASTER, MIDDLE EAST\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Staying overseas now to the middle east where violence is escalating over the weekend where Christians, Jews, and Muslims are traveling to Jerusalem to worship during the overlap of Easter, Passover, and Ramadan. ABC's Inez de La Cuetara is in Tel Aviv with the latest deadly attacks there. Ines, good morning to you.\par \par \uc2 INES DE LA CUETARA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Janai. And that attack happening right here behind me, right in the heart of Tel Aviv. You can see the car's tracks in the grass here. People have been gathering here this morning, bringing flowers as Prime Minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  calls up the country's reserve forces to confront the terror threat.\par \par \uc2 INES DE LA CUETARA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, new details in that horrific attack in Tel Aviv. Surveillance video, being reviewed by police, shows the moment a vehicle plowed into pedestrians on the city's iconic promenade killing an Italian tourist and injuring at least five others. The car then flipping over before being surrounded by police. Israeli officials saying they shot and killed the Israeli-Palestinian driver as he reached for a weapon. ABC's Matt Gutman was on the scene.\par \par \uc2 WITNESS (MALE)\par \par \uc2 As I walked down here, I saw three people laying on the floor, two of them being treated by first responders.\par \par \uc2 INES DE LA CUETARA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Earlier on Friday, in a separate incident, officials say a shooter opened fire in the west bank, killing two British-Israeli sisters, their mother critically wounded. This, as Israel sees some of its worst violence in decades. Clashes erupting this week at the (inaudible) mosque in Jerusalem's old city after Israeli police raids on one of Jerusalem's holiest sites. Palestinian militants later responding by firing rockets at Israel at both the Gaza strip and Lebanon. Defense forces firing back, claiming to strike (inaudible) controlled weapons factories and military installations. That back and forth marking the most serious border violence since Israel's 2006 war with \uc2 Lebanon's Hezbollah\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 INES DE LA CUETARA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And this all coming at a sensitive time with Passover, Ramadan, and Easter all coinciding. Both sides saying they are working to de-escalate the situation. Gio.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Ines, thank you so much for that.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230510ej4800008\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WEATHER\b0\par\par\uc2 489 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DUELING DECISIONS: ABORTION PILL RULINGS\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, WASHINGTON, ABORTION, FDA, BIRTH CONTROL, MCGILL\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, HARRIS, RULING, ABORTION, WOMEN\par \par \uc2 DWYER, FDA, TEXAS, ABORTION, IMPLICATIONS, RULING\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, HARRIS, TN, EXPULSION, JOHNSON, LOWERY\par \par \uc2 PENTAGON, DOCUMENTS, CLASSIFIED, LEAK, UKRAINE, \uc2 NATO\par \par \uc2 CHINA, TAIWAN, MILITARY, EXERCISES\par \par \uc2 VIOLENCE, PASSOVER, RAMADAN, EASTER, MIDDLE EAST\par \par \uc2 JOBS, SLOWING, HIRING\par \par \uc2 POPE, EASTER, GOOD FRIDAY, BRONCHITIS\par \par \uc2 MASTERS, GOLF, KOEPKA, JACKET\par \par \uc2 KINGSBURY, MISSING, MOTHER, MINNESOTA, WILLIAMS, DEGEORGE\par \par \uc2 REID, CRASH, DRUNK DRIVING, ACCIDENT\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Let's get a turn and check of the weather right now. Somara Theodore watching that forecast across the country for us.\par \par \uc2 SOMARA THEODORE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, you know, things have been so active lately, especially with severe weather. You've seen how many tornadoes we have seen, but we've got some pretty astonishing video coming out of Fulton County, Illinois. This is a county sheriff here. He actually had a brush with an EF-3 tornado. Look at the sparks flying, car rocking there, window beginning to shatter, 160-mile-per-hour winds in that. This is the car after that. Luckily, he made it through.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ACTIVE START TO 2023: TORNADO REPORTS THIS YEAR\par \par \uc2 SOMARA THEODORE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, if you are wondering, this has really been an active season, it truly has. The average year to date, 259. So far, we have had 496 tornado reports.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE WEATHER THREAT\par \par \uc2 SOMARA THEODORE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, I will say, today is not going to be as active as far as the severe weather threat goes. It is there, relatively minimal, down into the southeast. We could see some damaging winds and flash flooding. Nonetheless, we are in the thick of severe weather season, so it's a great time to begin to prepare. that's a look at the weather across the country, let's see what's going on in your neighborhood.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NATIONAL MAP\par \par \uc2 SOMARA THEODORE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And that is your forecast. It is so great to finally start to have a bit of a quieter weekend. But, of course, we're going to keep our eyes on August, Georgia. They've got the Masters going on...\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yep.\par \par \uc2 SOMARA THEODORE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...heavy rain going to be going through washing them out today.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And incredible to see the numbers of just how busy you guys have been in the weather department this year already.\par \par \uc2 SOMARA THEODORE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Nonstop.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COMING UP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ENTREPRENEUR CHARGED\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, still coming up here on "Good Morning America," an entrepreneur called a rising star in the business world now facing fraud charges.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOMERUN HEAVEN?\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And we are talking baseball and why those home run sluggers may find it easier than ever these days. Stick around. You're watching "GMA."\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230510ej480000g\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WEATHER\b0\par\par\uc2 424 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DUELING DECISIONS: ABORTION PILL RULINGS\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, WASHINGTON, ABORTION, FDA, BIRTH CONTROL, MCGILL\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, HARRIS, RULING, ABORTION, WOMEN\par \par \uc2 DWYER, FDA, TEXAS, ABORTION, IMPLICATIONS, RULING\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, HARRIS, TN, EXPULSION, JOHNSON, LOWERY\par \par \uc2 PENTAGON, DOCUMENTS, CLASSIFIED, LEAK, UKRAINE, \uc2 NATO\par \par \uc2 CHINA, TAIWAN, MILITARY, EXERCISES\par \par \uc2 VIOLENCE, PASSOVER, RAMADAN, EASTER, MIDDLE EAST\par \par \uc2 JOBS, SLOWING, HIRING\par \par \uc2 POPE, EASTER, GOOD FRIDAY, BRONCHITIS\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It is time now for a check of the weather, and Somara Theodore is watching what we are getting. Hey, Somara.\par \par \uc2 SOMARA THEODORE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey. You know, Ray Charles sang it best. He said it's a rainy night in Georgia...\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Mm-hmm, and?\par \par \uc2 SOMARA THEODORE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...and that was the situation for Atlanta, so let's go visit my friends. You know those are my old stomping grounds. Hey, Stone Mountain, Decatur, Marietta, how are you doing? Good morning. This is what you're waking up to. It's pretty dreary out there today. We have a lot of cloud coverage right now, cool, and the rain is going to kick into high gear.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FUTURE RADAR\par \par \uc2 SOMARA THEODORE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You know what is southeast of Atlanta? Augusta, and that's where we have the masters today. This is 2:00 PM. They're going to be in the thick of it, heavy rain coming down in Augusta and into South Carolina. The good news is, they should have time to make up a lot of the time slots there.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RAINFALL FORECAST: THIS WEEKEND\par \par \uc2 SOMARA THEODORE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Tomorrow by noon, sunshine returns. We're drying out. Anywhere from two to five inches of rain is certainly possible. Flash flooding is possible, as well.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOUTHEAST WARMTH: THREE DAY HIGH TEMPERATURES\par \par \uc2 SOMARA THEODORE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And then, it's going to be chilly out there. So, not only is it wet, it's also really cool and dreary. Highs today in the mid-to-upper 40s, but not to worry. We rebound nicely in the 60s. Orlando, what y'all got going on? 90 degrees today. That's a look at the weather across the country, let's see what's going on in your neighborhood.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NATIONAL MAP\par \par \uc2 SOMARA THEODORE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And it is a nice warm day in Orlando. You should head to Disney World. shameless plug.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 There you go, right. That line at Space Mountain getting a little hot today.\par \par \uc2 SOMARA THEODORE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 There you go.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230510ej480000b\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 INTRODUCTION TO THE 09:00 HALF-HOUR\b0\par\par\uc2 629 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DUELING DECISIONS: ABORTION PILL RULINGS\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, WASHINGTON, ABORTION, FDA, BIRTH CONTROL, MCGILL\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, HARRIS, RULING, ABORTION, WOMEN\par \par \uc2 DWYER, FDA, TEXAS, ABORTION, IMPLICATIONS, RULING\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, HARRIS, TN, EXPULSION, JOHNSON, LOWERY\par \par \uc2 PENTAGON, DOCUMENTS, CLASSIFIED, LEAK, UKRAINE, \uc2 NATO\par \par \uc2 CHINA, TAIWAN, MILITARY, EXERCISES\par \par \uc2 VIOLENCE, PASSOVER, RAMADAN, EASTER, MIDDLE EAST\par \par \uc2 JOBS, SLOWING, HIRING\par \par \uc2 POPE, EASTER, GOOD FRIDAY, BRONCHITIS\par \par \uc2 MASTERS, GOLF, KOEPKA, JACKET\par \par \uc2 KINGSBURY, MISSING, MOTHER, MINNESOTA, WILLIAMS, DEGEORGE\par \par \uc2 REID, CRASH, DRUNK DRIVING, ACCIDENT\par \par \uc2 SCHEME, \uc2 JP MORGAN\uc2 , CHARGED, JAVICE, LIEBER\par \par \uc2 HOME RUNS, CLIMATE CHANGE, SCIENCE, CALLAHAN, OLNEY\par \par \uc2 NEGRON, NATIONAL ANTHEM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Good morning, America. It's our second hour.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING OVERNIGHT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FEDERAL JUDGE SUSPENDS ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Breaking overnight, a Texas federal judge suspending approval of the abortion pill. And just minutes later, a contradictory decision coming down from another judge. Now, the matter likely heading to the Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VICE PRESIDENT HARRIS VISITS NASHVILLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT'S NEXT FOR EXPELLED TN LEGISLATORS\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 What's next for the Tennessee state lawmakers expelled for attending gun-control protests? The White House stepping up to show support.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 They chose to show courage.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SIX PEOPLE INJURED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GUNFIRE AT SOUTH CAROLINA BEACH\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Gunfire at a South Carolina beach leaving six people injured, most of them teens on their Senior Skip Day.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BODY MASS INDEX & GENETICS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW OBESITY STUDY\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Also, this morning, the new study out on obesity. Why researchers are saying those with a high BMI due to genetics have a lower risk of stroke and heart attack.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAKE THIS WEEKEND A PAGE TURNER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA BOOK CLUB\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Make this weekend a page turner. From airing out "Dirty Laundry" with the author behind "GMA's" April book club pick to the audiobook from Kate and Charlie Gibson.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "THE BOOK CASE" PODCAST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AUDIO BOOK BOOM\par \par \uc2 KATE GIBSON (HOST "THE BOOK CASE" PODCAST)\par \par \uc2 What was your process?\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 All ears for the latest literary trend.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW TO MAKE SHEET PAN TOASTER PASTRIES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ONE-PAN WONDERS\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Plus, one pan wonders serving up easy Easter and Passover and post-spring break breakfast like the sheet pan toaster pastries. Sure to make the whole family hoppy.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STAR WARS CELEBRATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE FORCE IS STRONG\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And the force is strong. "Star Wars" celebration hits light speed into London. "GMA" catching up with the creators and cast taking audiences to a galaxy far, far away.\par \par \uc2 DAISY RIDLEY (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 (Inaudible) Jedi.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And they're saying...\par \par \uc2 ACTRESSES (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Good morning, America.\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 Its Saturday morning, this is "GMA."\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Yes, it is "GMA." Good morning, America. So great to have you with us on a Saturday. No Jedi mind tricks here, though. Yes, but a Lama Hasan is at the "Star Wars" celebration happening right now in London.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Wow.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 She is getting the inside scoop on everything happening in a galaxy far, far away.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Look at how happy she was.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 She's excited.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Much more on that coming up in our second hour.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Look at the characters behind her.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 We've got some "Star Wars" fans here in the studio. I won't name names.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Oh, yeah.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Whit.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Right here. Much more on that coming up, though.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230510ej480000k\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 GOOD MORNING AMERICA\b0\par\par\uc2 474 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DUELING DECISIONS: ABORTION PILL RULINGS\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Good morning, America. Breaking overnight, abortion pill rulings. A federal judge suspending approval of the abortion pill. Just minutes later, a contradictory decision from another judge. The reaction from both sides with the matter now likely headed to the Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TENNESSEE LAWMAKERS OUSTED: WHITE HOUSE SHOWING SUPPORT\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Showing support. President Biden's message to Tennessee state lawmakers who faced votes to expel them. Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  meeting them personally.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 The truth must never be stifled or silenced when it's on behalf of the people.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 How the two who lost their seats could soon get them back.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JUSTICE DEPARTMENT INVESTIGATION: CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS LEAK\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Classified documents leak. The Justice Department investigation into how sensitive details about the war in Ukraine ended up on social media. The latest on this security breach.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHINA FLEXING ITS MUSCLE AFTER TAIWAN PRESIDENT'S MEETING: MILITARY DRILLS\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Military drills. China flexing its muscles, retaliating after Taiwan's President met with House Speaker McCarthy. The reaction from Taiwan this morning.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ESCALATING VIOLENCE: TENSIONS RISING\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Tensions rising in the Mideast. A driver plows into pedestrians in Tel Aviv, an Italian tourist killed. The escalating violence with Ramadan, Easter, and Passover coinciding this weekend.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INTENSE SEARCH FOR MINNESOTA WOMAN: MISSING MOTHER\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Missing mother. The search for a woman who vanished a week ago. Nearly 2,000 people stepping in to help. The reward this morning.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OFFICERS RESPOND TO WRONG ADDRESS: SHOOTING INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Shooting investigation. Officers responding to the wrong address, killing a man who answered the door holding a gun.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ACCUSED OF DEFRAUDING \uc2 JP MORGAN\uc2 : FACING CHARGES\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Facing charges. A woman once called a rising star in the business world accused of defrauding financial giant \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2  of over $175 million.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW OVERNIGHT: TROUBLE AT THE TEE\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Trouble at the tee. Strong winds toppling trees at Masters Tournament suspending play. What is on tap for today. Tiger Woods battling back and all eyes on a promising talent.\par \par \uc2 SPORTS COMMENTATOR (MALE)\par \par \uc2 And we have an amateur tied for second.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW OVERNIGHT: HOMERUN HEAVEN\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Plus, homerun heaven. The new study on why more sluggers may be hitting it out of the park.\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 Live from ABC News in New York, this is "Good Morning America."\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA, SATURDAY, APRIL 8\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Good morning, America. Happy Saturday morning. Thank you for starting your weekend with us. We, of course, have a lot of news to get to.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230510ej4800001\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 LATEST REPORT SHOWS HIRING IS SLOWING 236,000 JOBS IN MARCH, SMALLEST GROWTH IN MORE THAN TWO YEARS\b0\par\par\uc2 424 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DUELING DECISIONS: ABORTION PILL RULINGS\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, WASHINGTON, ABORTION, FDA, BIRTH CONTROL, MCGILL\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, HARRIS, RULING, ABORTION, WOMEN\par \par \uc2 DWYER, FDA, TEXAS, ABORTION, IMPLICATIONS, RULING\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, HARRIS, TN, EXPULSION, JOHNSON, LOWERY\par \par \uc2 PENTAGON, DOCUMENTS, CLASSIFIED, LEAK, UKRAINE, \uc2 NATO\par \par \uc2 CHINA, TAIWAN, MILITARY, EXERCISES\par \par \uc2 VIOLENCE, PASSOVER, RAMADAN, EASTER, MIDDLE EAST\par \par \uc2 JOBS, SLOWING, HIRING\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And now to the latest on the economy. The new employment report shows jobs growth slowing. Here to break it all down for us and tell us what this means for the economy is ABC's Alexis Christoforous. Alexis, good morning to you.\par \par \uc2 ALEXIS CHRISTOFOROUS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Gio. Look, the once red-hot job market is showing signs of cooling. The economy added 236,000 jobs last month, a solid gain, but less than the 326,000 job added in February, and the smallest job growth in more than two years. The unemployment rate dipping to 3.5 percent as more Americans jumped into the labor market helping to take the pressure off wage increases. The \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 's nine interest rate hikes in the past year combined with tighter bank lending has businesses tightening their belts. Still, Wall Street betting the Fed will raise rates at least one more time this year at its May meeting possibly before pausing. Gio.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And Alexis, we've got just over a week to go before tax day, but now you say the \uc2 IRS\uc2  is actually announcing a major overhaul?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 IRS\uc2  REVEALS MASSIVE NEW OVERHAUL. $80 BILLION PLAN AIMED AT ELIMINATING THE PAPER BACKLOG\par \par \uc2 ALEXIS CHRISTOFOROUS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes. We've been waiting for this information. So, the \uc2 IRS\uc2  releasing a road map for how it intends to spend $80 billion in Congressional funding that could make filing your taxes a whole lot easier. Changes include hiring more staffers to answer customer phone calls and allowing taxpayers to opt into personalized alerts, updating them on their refund status, even pointing out problems with their returns. The agency also promising to address racial disparities in audits, hiring thousands to track down healthy individuals and big corporations that aren't paying what they owe or avoiding taxes entirely. Now these upgrades won't happen overnight, they are expected to roll out over the next decade. Guys.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, helpful information. Thank you so much, Alexis, we appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230510ej4800009\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WHITE HOUSE RESPONDS TO RULINGS ON ABORTION PILL VP HARRIS: PRESIDENT BIDEN WILL "STAND WITH THE WOMEN OF AMERICA"\b0\par\par\uc2 318 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DUELING DECISIONS: ABORTION PILL RULINGS\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, WASHINGTON, ABORTION, FDA, BIRTH CONTROL, MCGILL\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, HARRIS, RULING, ABORTION, WOMEN\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And overnight, the Biden administration promising to fight the decision with the Justice Department filing an appeal to the Texas ruling. ABC's Elizabeth Schulze has the latest reaction from the White House. Elizabeth, good morning.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Whit. The White House is vowing to fight to preserve American's access to the abortion pill. Officials here have been holding internal discussions for weeks, bracing for this decision from the federal judge in Texas. As the Justice Department appeals the ruling, Democrats are attacking the judge as a Trump appointee with a long history of antiabortion activism. In a statement overnight, President Biden said, "This does not just affect women in Texas. If it stands, it would prevent women in every state from accessing the medication," adding "It as the next big step for the national ban on abortion that Republican-elected officials have vowed to make law in America."\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Vice President Harris, who has been spearheading the administration's abortion rights push, warned that this ruling sets a dangerous precedent, undermining the FDA's ability to approve drugs based on science, not politics. But the political reality here is complicated. Without Congressional action, it is not clear what steps the Biden administration can take to preserve abortion access. The President is, again, calling for Congress to take steps to restore Roe V Wade, an effort to do that already failed last year and that was before Republicans took control of the House. Whit.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, let's talk about more of those next steps. Elizabeth, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230510ej4800003\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 NEWS HEADLINES\b0\par\par\uc2 294 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Saturday\par \uc2 WNSA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 RULINGS, ABORTION PILL, LANGREN, HAWKINS, MCGILL\par \par \uc2 RULINGS, ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIVAL RULINGS ON ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 LEAK, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS, MULROY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOJ LAUNCHES CLASSIFIED LEAKS PROBE\par \par \uc2 JONES, PEARSON, JOHNSON, RICHEY, PROTEST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PUSH TO REINSTATE OUSTED LAWMAKERS\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, VIOLENCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ISRAEL: ROCKETS LAUNCHED FROM SYRIA\par \par \uc2 MASTERS, WEATHER, STORM, TRACK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STORMS POSTPONE TOURNAMENT AGAIN\par \par \uc2 CHINA, DRILLS, TAIWAN, ASHEN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHINA RAMPS UP MILITARY DRILLS\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, ARREST, POLICE CHASE, PUPPY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SHOOTING ON POPULAR BEACH\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Next, tonight, panic at a South Carolina beach as gunfire broke out.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Video from the scene shows hundreds running from the area. This happened Friday afternoon in Isle of Palms. Police say the beach was jammed with teenagers enjoying so-called Senior Skip Day. Six people were shot, but officials say the injuries are not believed to be life-threatening. Two teenagers were arrested on weapons charges. But police say it's not clear either of them fired the shots.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PUPPY RESCUED AFTER CHASE\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) New details on a police chase that played out on live TV in Los Angeles on Friday.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) For hours, officers pursued suspects who were first driving a truck and then a second vehicle. Three people were ultimately arrested, one for attempted murder. At some point, police said someone tossed a designer bag out a window and inside was that puppy, amazingly unharmed and now in the care of animal services.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Authorities say the investigation continues. When we come back, an invasion of sorts in south Florida.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WORLD NEWS TONIGHT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COMING UP\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The giant blob storming the beaches.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document WNSA000020230413ej4800009\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 RIVAL RULINGS ON ABORTION PILL NEXT STEPS FOR ACCESS; SUPREME COURT COULD GET CASE\b0\par\par\uc2 288 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Saturday\par \uc2 WNSA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 RULINGS, ABORTION PILL, LANGREN, HAWKINS, MCGILL\par \par \uc2 RULINGS, ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIVAL RULINGS ON ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And the arrival abortion pill rulings sparking concern nationwide on both sides of the debate. So, let's bring in ABC's senior Washington reporter Devin Dwyer who covers the courts for us. So, Devin, what are the immediate next steps in terms of who can access the pill and how likely is it that this will go all the way to the \uc2 US Supreme Court\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 DEVIN DWYER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) For the next six days, that FDA approval will stand because the judge stayed his own ruling. So, it's status quo.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEXT STEPS FOR ACCESS; SUPREME COURT COULD GET CASE\par \par \uc2 DEVIN DWYER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But this week, all eyes will turn to the fifth circuit court of appeals in New Orleans, a very conservative court. That's where the Justice Department will seek an extended stay of the Texas judge's decision, allowing mifepristone to remain in use as this all gets sorted out. Whatever the outcome there, it's certain to be bound for the Supreme Court, though there's no timeline on that just yet. As we've been reporting, Whit, the stakes here are very significant. If this ruling stands, it would have a nationwide impact even in states where abortion is legal.\par \par \uc2 DEVIN DWYER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And that would dramatically reduce access to the most common form of abortion in this co country, Whit.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So much at stake as this moves through the courts. Devin Dwyer, thanks to you tonight.\par \par \uc2 Document WNSA000020230413ej4800003\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 PUSH TO REINSTATE OUSTED LAWMAKERS FMR TN REP. JONES: EXPULSIONS MEANT TO "INTIMIDATE"\b0\par\par\uc2 671 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Saturday\par \uc2 WNSA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 RULINGS, ABORTION PILL, LANGREN, HAWKINS, MCGILL\par \par \uc2 RULINGS, ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIVAL RULINGS ON ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 LEAK, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS, MULROY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOJ LAUNCHES CLASSIFIED LEAKS PROBE\par \par \uc2 JONES, PEARSON, JOHNSON, RICHEY, PROTEST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PUSH TO REINSTATE OUSTED LAWMAKERS\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to the push to reinstate two ousted Tennessee lawmakers.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  giving a fiery speech in support of Justin Pearson and Justin Jones, saying the truth must never be stifled or silenced. Tennessee Republicans voting out the representatives from the legislature after they engaged in protest over gun violence on the House floor.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, both men are trying to get their jobs back. ABC's Faith Abubey in Nashville.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FMR TN REP. JONES: EXPULSIONS MEANT TO "INTIMIDATE"\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, one of the two black Democrats ousted from the Tennessee statehouse in a partisan expulsion vote, Justin Jones, speaking out. Both hoping to take back their seats as soon as next week.\par \par \uc2 JUSTIN JONES (DEM) (FORMER STATE REPRESENTATIVE TENNESSEE)\par \par \uc2 Their action was meant to intimidate, was meant to humiliate. But what it did was put the state of Tennessee on trial for the world to see.\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The Tennessee House Republican supermajority last week accused Jones along with other Democratic colleagues Justin Pearson and Gloria Johnson of violating House rules, ignoring leadership warning not to protest for gun reform on the House floor in the wake of the mass shooting in Nashville's covenant school, where six people including three 9-year-olds were killed. Jones instead taking a megaphone to the chamber well.\par \par \uc2 JUSTIN JONES (DEM) (FORMER STATE REPRESENTATIVE TENNESSEE)\par \par \uc2 Reaction. Reaction.\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Temporarily halting House business.\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Do you feel like you did anything wrong?\par \par \uc2 JUSTIN JONES (DEM) (FORMER STATE REPRESENTATIVE TENNESSEE)\par \par \uc2 I don't, I think that what we did was the only human response to a community grieving. They say we broke decorum, we broke House rules. But what we were obedient to was our oath.\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Both Jones and Pearson, who were black, not merely censured but expelled. Johnson, a white woman, avoiding that fate by a single vote.\par \par \uc2 STATE REPRESENTATIVE GLORIA JOHNSON (DEM) (TENNESSEE)\par \par \uc2 It might have to do with the color of our skin.\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Republican Bryan Richey tells CNN it was not a race issue.\par \par \uc2 STATE REPRESENTATIVE BRYAN RITCHEY (REP) (TENNESSEE)\par \par \uc2 They played the video. It clearly showed her standing there not doing as much, had nothing to do with the color of their skin.\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The White House not missing an opportunity to push back on what they view as Republican extremism. The President talking to the three Democrats Friday. The Vice President meeting with them in Nashville, and then taking the stage at a local chapel.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (DEM) (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 Democracy says you don't silence the people. You do not stifle the people. You don't turn off their microphones when they are speaking.\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Jones, tonight, hopeful about the prospect of going back to finish what he started.\par \par \uc2 JUSTIN JONES (DEM) (FORMER STATE REPRESENTATIVE TENNESSEE)\par \par \uc2 I will probably walk back into the chamber.\par \par \uc2 FAITH ABUBEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The council is considering suspending its rules on Monday in order to expedite the process to send Jones back to the House. It's not clear at this point whether the Republicans will try to take any action to impact the process. Whit?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Faith Abubey, thank you. And tune into "This Week" tomorrow morning.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TOMORROW\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REP. JUSTIN PEARSON, EXPELLED TENNESSEE LAWMAKER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THIS WEEK\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) \uc2 Jonathan Karl\uc2  interviews Tennessee lawmaker Justin Pearson after he was expelled from office for protesting gun violence on the House floor.\par \par \uc2 Document WNSA000020230413ej4800005\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 AMERICA STRONG A SURVIVOR STORY THAT'S COME FULL CIRCLE\b0\par\par\uc2 545 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Saturday\par \uc2 WNSA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 RULINGS, ABORTION PILL, LANGREN, HAWKINS, MCGILL\par \par \uc2 RULINGS, ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIVAL RULINGS ON ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 LEAK, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS, MULROY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOJ LAUNCHES CLASSIFIED LEAKS PROBE\par \par \uc2 JONES, PEARSON, JOHNSON, RICHEY, PROTEST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PUSH TO REINSTATE OUSTED LAWMAKERS\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, VIOLENCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ISRAEL: ROCKETS LAUNCHED FROM SYRIA\par \par \uc2 MASTERS, WEATHER, STORM, TRACK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STORMS POSTPONE TOURNAMENT AGAIN\par \par \uc2 CHINA, DRILLS, TAIWAN, ASHEN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHINA RAMPS UP MILITARY DRILLS\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, ARREST, POLICE CHASE, PUPPY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SHOOTING ON POPULAR BEACH\par \par \uc2 SEAWEED, BEACH, SARGASSUM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE INDEX\par \par \uc2 PETTE, DREYER, CANCER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: #AMERICASTRONG\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Finally, tonight, "America Strong." A young doctor's inspiring journey.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Dr. Courtney Pette has a deep connection to the patients and staff at \uc2 Texas Children's Hospital\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 DR COURTNEY PETTE (TEXAS CHILDREN'S HOSPITAL / CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 I think we're good there.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) She not only works here, it's also where she survived cancer as a child. Her journey began a dozen years ago when she sadly passed out while getting her braces changed at the orthodontist.\par \par \uc2 DR COURTNEY PETTE (TEXAS CHILDREN'S HOSPITAL / CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 My mom was like, something is not right. You shouldn't be passing out when you're laying down at the dentist's.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) A chest x-ray revealing that one of her lungs was filled with fluid.\par \par \uc2 DR COURTNEY PETTE (TEXAS CHILDREN'S HOSPITAL / CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 After running all the tests and getting the biopsy, I was diagnosed with Hodgkin's lymphoma.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Her sister, still emotional, describing when her dad shared the news.\par \par \uc2 SISTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 I knew something was really, really, really wrong and he couldn't even get out the words. But finally, he said, it's cancer.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Courtney was just 15 years old and determined to fight. After four months of chemotherapy and then radiation, her cancer went into remission.\par \par \uc2 DR COURTNEY PETTE (TEXAS CHILDREN'S HOSPITAL / CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 Just for knowing that my family was nervous, I was feeling for them and I didn't want them to be scared and then to be upset because I knew that we'd make it through.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Her time spent at Texas Children's inspired her to go to medical school. Now, she's a resident physician here, working alongside the same doctor who treated her.\par \par \uc2 DR ZOANN DREYER (HEMATOLOGY-ONCOLOGY SPECIALIST TEXAS CHILDREN'S HOSP)\par \par \uc2 I remember her talking to me from the very beginning that she really wanted to be a doctor. And when she was well enough, she kind of morphed that into wanting to be a pediatric oncologist.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, Dr. Pette using that inner strength and courage to motivate her young patients.\par \par \uc2 DR COURTNEY PETTE (TEXAS CHILDREN'S HOSPITAL / CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 I would hope that knowing that my patients know that I also went through cancer and went through the treatment gives them some hope.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And a big thank you to our station \uc2 KTRK\uc2  in Houston for first sharing Dr. Pette's story. I'm Whit Johnson in New York. Have a great night.\par \par \uc2 Document WNSA000020230413ej480000b\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 MAJOR ABORTION PILL COURT BATTLE DUELING RULINGS PUT FUTURE OF DRUG IN LIMBO\b0\par\par\uc2 683 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Saturday\par \uc2 WNSA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 RULINGS, ABORTION PILL, LANGREN, HAWKINS, MCGILL\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good evening. Thanks for joining us on this Saturday. I'm Whit Johnson.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR ABORTION PILL COURT BATTLE\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We begin with the battle lines being drawn over the abortion pill. Two competing judicial rulings handed down almost simultaneously have set up what is widely expected to be a showdown certain at the \uc2 US Supreme Court\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The pill called mifepristone is one of two drugs commonly used in medication abortion. A federal judge in Texas suspending the \uc2 FDA\uc2 's approval, which had been in place for more than 20 years. While a federal judge in Washington state reached the opposite conclusion, ordering that it remains available in states where it's legal. The Biden administration reacting swiftly. Attorney General \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  already appealing the Texas ruling. The \uc2 FDA\uc2  says it's standing behind its determination that the drug is safe.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Both court cases could have national implications. But this widely used abortion pill now remains in legal limbo, raising questions about what this means for access before a higher court weighs in. We have team coverage to. Here's ABC's Zohreen Shah leading us off.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DUELING RULINGS PUT FUTURE OF DRUG IN LIMBO\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, protests from Chicago to Houston.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 This is a huge attack on the rights of women.\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Less than 24 hours after a federal court decision jeopardized access to mifepristone, a key medication used in more than half of US abortions.\par \par \uc2 ALEXIS MCGILL (CEO PLANNED PARENTHOOD ACTION FUND)\par \par \uc2 A reckless decision based on junk science that is going to have devastating consequences for our patients.\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) A Texas judge suspended the \uc2 FDA\uc2 's decades-long approval of the drug on Friday and wrote that the \uc2 FDA\uc2 's, quote, "lack of restrictions resulted in many deaths and many more severe or life-threatening adverse reactions." Adding, whatever the numbers are, they likely would be considerably lower had \uc2 FDA\uc2  is not acquiesced to the pressure to increase access to chemical abortion at the expense of women's safety. Some anti-abortion advocates applauding the judge's ruling.\par \par \uc2 KRISTAN HAWKINS (PRESIDENT STUDENTS FOR LIFE ACTION)\par \par \uc2 Well, it was certainly a victory. It was one that we've been praying for Zahren some time.\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But the \uc2 FDA\uc2  says it will appeal, insisting it stands behind its determination that mifepristone is safe and effective.\par \par \uc2 DR ELIZABETH LANGREN (OBSTETRICS & GYNECOLOGY UNIVERSITY OF MICHIGAN)\par \par \uc2 Mifepristone is an exceptionally effective and safe medication to use for first trimester terminations of frequency. But the \uc2 FDA\uc2  has continued to, if anything, overly monitor this drug to make sure that it continues to be safe and effective.\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And now, there's a conflicting role in Washington state. The judge, an Obama appointee, ruling on Friday to keep the status quo of the drug, writing, quote, "Abortion restrictions vary state by state and plaintiffs alleged harm not shared nationwide." President Biden says his administration will fight the Texas ruling. "If it stands," he says, "it would prevent women in every state from exiting the medication regardless of whether abortion is legal in the state."\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Zohreen Shah joining us now. And, Zohreen, we're hearing from the attorney general. And the DOJ already taking action now.\par \par \uc2 ZOHREEN SHAH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Whit, they have. The Justice Department overnight filed an appeal. The AG says in the statement that the DOJ will continue to defend the \uc2 FDA\uc2 's decision that the abortion pill is safe and effective. Okay, so just how safe and effective? Well, the OB/GYN that we spoke to tells us that the pill is safer than both Viagra and getting your wisdom teeth pulled out. Whit?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Zohreen, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document WNSA000020230413ej4800002\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WORLD NEWS SATURDAY\b0\par\par\uc2 435 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Saturday\par \uc2 WNSA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Tonight, several developing stories as we come on the air. The major court battle over what used to abortion pill.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR ABORTION PILL COURT BATTLE\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Conflicting court rulings in two different states. One federal judge in Texas suspending the \uc2 FDA\uc2  approval for a pillow that's used in more than half of all abortions. Another judge in Washington state keeping its access status quo. The drug has been approved for more than two decades. The \uc2 FDA\uc2  insisting it's safe and effective. An outright ban could impact every stayed even once where abortion is legal. Tonight, the Biden administration weighing in on a case that could go all the way to the \uc2 US Supreme Court\uc2 . We have team coverage tonight.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOJ LAUNCHES CLASSIFIED LEAKS PROBE\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 The Justice Department launching a probe Ito that leak of dozens of classified documents, reportedly exposing US secrets from the war in Ukraine to China to Iran and North Korea. The White House caught off guard. How the Pentagon is responding tonight.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PUSH TO REINSTATE OUSTED LAWMAKERS\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 The new push to reinstate two Tennessee lawmakers expelled after leading a noisy protest at the state capitol. The steps that could put one or both back in office within days. Our Faith Abubey in Nashville.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ISRAEL: ROCKETS LAUNCHED FROM SYRIA\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 The holy land on edge. A new rocket strike on Israel tonight, this time from Syria. Tensions were already rising after two other deadly attacks as Christians, Jews and Muslims gather for sacred celebrations this weekend.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SHOOTING IN POPULAR BEACH\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Panic on a popular beach. Teenagers running for cover as gunfire breaks out on Senior Skip Day. Six people shot. What police are saying after detaining multiple suspects.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLIDAY WEEKEND WEATHER\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Drenching rain in the south forcing another delay at the Masters as a new storm moves into the west. Rob Marciano standing by with your holiday weekend forecast.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHINA RAMPS UP MILITARY DRILLS\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 China ramping up its military drills. Fighter jets streaking towards Taiwan just days after Taiwan's president met with House Speaker McCarthy in California.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMERICA STRONG\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And "America Strong" tonight, a cancer survivor returns to the same hospital where she was treated as a child, this time as a doctor.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WORLD NEWS TONIGHT\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 From ABC News world headquarters in New York, this is "World News Tonight."\par \par \uc2 Document WNSA000020230413ej4800001\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 STORMS POSTPONE TOURNAMENT AGAIN HEAVY RAIN STARTS TO MOVE OUT OF SOUTHEAST\b0\par\par\uc2 330 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Saturday\par \uc2 WNSA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 RULINGS, ABORTION PILL, LANGREN, HAWKINS, MCGILL\par \par \uc2 RULINGS, ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIVAL RULINGS ON ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 LEAK, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS, MULROY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOJ LAUNCHES CLASSIFIED LEAKS PROBE\par \par \uc2 JONES, PEARSON, JOHNSON, RICHEY, PROTEST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PUSH TO REINSTATE OUSTED LAWMAKERS\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, VIOLENCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ISRAEL: ROCKETS LAUNCHED FROM SYRIA\par \par \uc2 MASTERS, WEATHER, STORM, TRACK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STORMS POSTPONE TOURNAMENT AGAIN\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Drenching rain across parts of the southeast here in the US forcing another postponement of the Masters.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Golfers and spectators braved heavy downpours and Augusta. Four officials called an end to play. But heavy rain now moving out of the southeast.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, let's turn to ABC's senior meteorologist Rob Marciano. Rob, what's in store for the rest of the holiday weekend?\par \par \uc2 ROB MARCIANO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, Whit. Yeah, first things first, the Masters will be a drier day tomorrow, certainly in the afternoon. That rain is moving fairly quickly albeit very heavy.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RAINFALL FORECAST\par \par \uc2 ROB MARCIANO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) You see it here on the radar. It's pulling out of Georgia now, but the Carolinas are just getting crushed. And they'll see another one to two inches of rainfall. So, certainly damp sunrise services and (inaudible) in the southeast.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NORTHWEST SOAKER\par \par \uc2 ROB MARCIANO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The other problem spot is going to be the Pacific Northwest. Another storm coming in there tomorrow afternoon. It starts off as mostly rain and snow levels begin to fall as much colder air begins to sink into the west.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LOOKING AHEAD\par \par \uc2 ROB MARCIANO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Look at some of these numbers in Seattle, 49 for a high there and a big warmup with record-breaking temperatures possible midweek in places like Denver. Whit?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, we'll look forward to that. Rob, thanks so much.\par \par \uc2 Document WNSA000020230413ej4800007\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 THE INDEX\b0\par\par\uc2 208 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Saturday\par \uc2 WNSA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 RULINGS, ABORTION PILL, LANGREN, HAWKINS, MCGILL\par \par \uc2 RULINGS, ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIVAL RULINGS ON ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 LEAK, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS, MULROY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOJ LAUNCHES CLASSIFIED LEAKS PROBE\par \par \uc2 JONES, PEARSON, JOHNSON, RICHEY, PROTEST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PUSH TO REINSTATE OUSTED LAWMAKERS\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, VIOLENCE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ISRAEL: ROCKETS LAUNCHED FROM SYRIA\par \par \uc2 MASTERS, WEATHER, STORM, TRACK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STORMS POSTPONE TOURNAMENT AGAIN\par \par \uc2 CHINA, DRILLS, TAIWAN, ASHEN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHINA RAMPS UP MILITARY DRILLS\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, ARREST, POLICE CHASE, PUPPY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SHOOTING ON POPULAR BEACH\par \par \uc2 SEAWEED, BEACH, SARGASSUM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE INDEX\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) To "The Index" now. Florida is getting a preview of what could become the summer of seaweed.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Mounds of brown tangled blobs known as sargassum have been washing up on beaches in south Florida. The occurrence isn't new, but some scientists are concerned about just how much is showing up on beaches this early in the year. The giant boom of seaweed stretches about 5,000 miles wide of the coast. It's big enough to be seen from space.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) When we come back, "America Strong."\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WORLD NEWS TONIGHT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COMING UP\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) A survivor story that's come full circle.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document WNSA000020230413ej480000a\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 DOJ LAUNCHES CLASSIFIED LEAKS PROBE SECRET U.S. MILITARY DOCUMENTS APPEAR ONLINE\b0\par\par\uc2 452 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 April 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Saturday\par \uc2 WNSA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 RULINGS, ABORTION PILL, LANGREN, HAWKINS, MCGILL\par \par \uc2 RULINGS, ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIVAL RULINGS ON ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 LEAK, CLASSIFIED DOCUMENTS, MULROY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOJ LAUNCHES CLASSIFIED LEAKS PROBE\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to the investigation into the leak of dozens of classified documents. The Justice Department launching an urgent probe.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Materials some marked top secret revealed details from the war in Ukraine and offer a snapshot of the battlefield situation in the beginning of March.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ABC's Elizabeth Schulze tonight from Washington.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SECRET U.S. MILITARY DOCUMENTS APPEAR ONLINE\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, the Justice Department is investigating a leak of dozens of classified US military documents that reportedly contained top-secret information from the war in Ukraine to China to Iran and North Korea. Photos of the classified documents, most of which we cannot show, were posted on social media this week as well as dozens of other documents posted online as early as March, raising alarms about the scope and scale of the security breach.\par \par \uc2 MICK MULROY (FMR DEP ASST SECRETARY OF DEFENSE FOR THE MIDDLE EAST)\par \par \uc2 When you take a picture of classified material, there is no excuse for that. So, I think this does indicate that there was at least some level of intent to basically undermine the US national security interests.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) ABC News has learned some of the documents seem to include markings identifying them from the Office of the Joint Chiefs and one document dated March 2nd appears to have come from the CIA's daily intelligence summaries provided to senior leaders. Some military and CIA documents posted seem to be photos of a printed PowerPoint slide. Some photos are creased down the middle as if they were folded. One US official tells ABC News the documents are no longer relevant to the battlefield and they are of limited intelligence value and appear to have been altered from the original documents. The Biden administration now scrambling to find the source of the league.\par \par \uc2 MICK MULROY (FMR DEP ASST SECRETARY OF DEFENSE FOR THE MIDDLE EAST)\par \par \uc2 I do think it does give our allies pause not with working with us, but just what they actually share with us.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, along with the Justice Department, the CIA and Pentagon are also reviewing the posts on social media. One US official tells us that the government is trying to have the documents removed from platforms online. Whit?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Something to watch closely. Thank you so much, Elizabeth Schulze. We appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 Document WNSA000020230413ej4800004\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 FLORENCE PUGH LIVE IN TIMES SQUARE ACTRESS TALKS ABOUT LATEST FILM, "A GOOD PERSON"\b0\par\par\uc2 1,971 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 March 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RECORD BREAKING STORM\par \par \uc2 STORM, RAIN, WINDS, SNOW, HOPPIN, HIGHWAYS\par \par \uc2 STORM, RAIN, SNOW, ALERTS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, DOCUMENTS, HOWELL, INVESTIGATIONS, GRAND JURY\par \par \uc2 FED, INTEREST RATES, BANKING, INFLATION\par \par \uc2 OTIENO, VIDEO, 911, DEATH, OUKO, INDICTED\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, LAUSD, WAGES, STUDENTS, PARENTS\par \par \uc2 LOPEZ, DEAF, SUPREME COURT, MICHIGAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS; STORM MOVES EAST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 SMITH, MURDER, MURDAUGH, SLED, MOORE\par \par \uc2 PALTROW, LAWSUIT, HENDERSON, SKI, CRASH, BUHLER, OWENS\par \par \uc2 DELIVERY, SCAMMERS, SUSPECTS, BURGLARY, HOMEOWNERS\par \par \uc2 SAILBOAT, SUNK, WHALE, RODRIGUEZ, CREW, RESCUE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 INTEREST RATES, HIKE, ECONOMY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALL EYES ON INTEREST RATES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WILL FED HIKE RATES AGAIN AMID BANKING CRISIS?\par \par \uc2 BIRTH CONTROL, RISK, BREAST CANCER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAST CANCER & HORMONAL BIRTH CONTROL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOES BIRTH CONTROL INCREASE RISK OF BREAST CANCER?\par \par \uc2 REED, TRIBUTE, \uc2 KNICKS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REMEMBERING WILLIS REED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 NEW YORK KNICKS\uc2  LEGEND DIES AT 80\par \par \uc2 READING, DAVIS, KIM, "KANGAROO CRAVINGS", SPENCER\par \par \uc2 ANISTON, SANDLER, "MURDER MYSTERY 2"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 DENNIS, WING, ANIMAL RESCUE\par \par \uc2 "A GOOD PERSON", PUGH\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We are back now on "Good Morning America" with Oscar-nominated actress Florence Pugh. You know her from "Little Women," "Black Widow," "Midsommar," and so many more. Now, she's starring in "A Good Person." Thank you so much for being here.\par \par \uc2 FLORENCE PUGH ("A GOOD PERSON")\par \par \uc2 Hi, Lara.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Busy day on "GMA."\par \par \uc2 FLORENCE PUGH ("A GOOD PERSON")\par \par \uc2 Of course, it's busy day. But great to be here. Thank you for having me.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, really, really happy to see you. So, last night, I was online doing my homework.\par \par \uc2 FLORENCE PUGH ("A GOOD PERSON")\par \par \uc2 Yeah\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And over and over again, this is what I read, that this movie fills your heart, that it is so poignant in the most perfect way.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLORENCE PUGH LIVE IN TIMES SQUARE\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's about a young woman finding hope in very unlikely places after enduring a really horrific tragedy.\par \par \uc2 FLORENCE PUGH ("A GOOD PERSON")\par \par \uc2 Yeah. Yeah.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What was it like starting alongside Morgan Freeman and the ever-delightful Molly Shannon?\par \par \uc2 FLORENCE PUGH ("A GOOD PERSON")\par \par \uc2 Oh, my goodness. Well, I've already had the pleasure of working with some of the greats in this industry, but adding Molly and Morgan to that was just absolutely incredible. It's amazing to work with professionals, you just get to watch and learn and soak it all up.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And Molly's character is your mom.\par \par \uc2 FLORENCE PUGH ("A GOOD PERSON")\par \par \uc2 Yeah, great fit. It's mad. It's a bonkers household but, yeah, a family I would like to be a part of.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And Morgan is sort of an unexpected place of solace for you?\par \par \uc2 FLORENCE PUGH ("A GOOD PERSON")\par \par \uc2 Yeah, these two characters come into each other's lives. It's a very unexpected friendship, but it's a friendship that's deeply needed and necessary. And I think we get to watch this, you know, older man suffering through the same things that this younger woman is. And hopefully, they kind of help each other through this tough patch.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, we have a clip.\par \par \uc2 FLORENCE PUGH ("A GOOD PERSON")\par \par \uc2 Yeah.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Let's have everyone take a look.\par \par \uc2 FLORENCE PUGH ("A GOOD PERSON")\par \par \uc2 Oh, great.\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM MOVIE, "A GOOD PERSON"\par \par \uc2 MORGAN FREEMAN ("A GOOD PERSON")\par \par \uc2 Allison, don't go.\par \par \uc2 FLORENCE PUGH ("A GOOD PERSON")\par \par \uc2 This was a mistake.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN FREEMAN ("A GOOD PERSON")\par \par \uc2 No, no, it isn't. Trust me. I know how hard it is to get here. It's damn near impossible, and you did it. Don't run away now because of me.\par \par \uc2 FLORENCE PUGH ("A GOOD PERSON")\par \par \uc2 There are thousands of meetings, I'll find another one.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN FREEMAN ("A GOOD PERSON")\par \par \uc2 Wow, yeah, but this one has the best snacks.\par \par \uc2 FLORENCE PUGH ("A GOOD PERSON")\par \par \uc2 I want to go.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN FREEMAN ("A GOOD PERSON")\par \par \uc2 No, no, you've made it this far and I wouldn't.\par \par \uc2 FLORENCE PUGH ("A GOOD PERSON")\par \par \uc2 I don't want to be here.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN FREEMAN ("A GOOD PERSON")\par \par \uc2 Nobody does in the beginning.\par \par \uc2 FLORENCE PUGH ("A GOOD PERSON")\par \par \uc2 I don't want to be anywhere.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN FREEMAN ("A GOOD PERSON")\par \par \uc2 Then you are definitely in the right spot.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's like soul crushing.\par \par \uc2 FLORENCE PUGH ("A GOOD PERSON")\par \par \uc2 Well, it's, yeah, it's got some important scenes. It's about the opioid crisis and it's the first time that she actually makes it and gets herself to AA. And he happens to be there and he stops her from leaving. So, it's very poignant. And despite it happening very sensitive and dark and sad topic, it's also really, it has moments of levity, it's funny. And Zach has written a fantastic script that kind of matches how we deal with times of sadness.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right. Zach's writing is fantastic.\par \par \uc2 FLORENCE PUGH ("A GOOD PERSON")\par \par \uc2 Yeah.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Produced, directed, wrote it. Let's get into Molly Shannon, she was with us on "Good Morning America" on Monday.\par \par \uc2 FLORENCE PUGH ("A GOOD PERSON")\par \par \uc2 Yeah. I heard.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And shared with us that you guys have a wrestling, a scene in which you wrestled and you guys really got into it.\par \par \uc2 FLORENCE PUGH ("A GOOD PERSON")\par \par \uc2 Yeah, we fight.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Who's stronger? Because I can't decide who my money would be on.\par \par \uc2 FLORENCE PUGH ("A GOOD PERSON")\par \par \uc2 She kept on (inaudible) the other day. We had the premier two nights ago or maybe it was last night, I can't remember and she was like, "You know, you're so stocky and feisty, and I love fighting with you." I genuinely think that we, like, we matched each other perfectly. And so much so, halfway through the fighting, instead of like maybe us just calming down and not fighting as hard, she was like, I think we need to put pads on, so that we can fight more.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, wow. She's all in.\par \par \uc2 FLORENCE PUGH ("A GOOD PERSON")\par \par \uc2 Yeah. So, then we put pads on and we were just jamming each other into mirrors. It was great.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That is so fun. I was also reading that your parents are so very proud of you, even now as you make all of these movies and are becoming a bigger star, they still clip every magazine article and every newspaper.\par \par \uc2 FLORENCE PUGH ("A GOOD PERSON")\par \par \uc2 Yeah. Oh, yeah. And they don't just get one newspaper, it's like seven in case anyone needs one.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's so precious. They must be very proud. That must be a very big box.\par \par \uc2 FLORENCE PUGH ("A GOOD PERSON")\par \par \uc2 Well, yeah. Also, it's like, this is a bizarre life that's unfolding and I think they're just, they're proud of all of their babies. So, whenever there's a clip and they're like.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I know, as a mom, I totally get it. And I now have my mom's box of clippings. So, you will one day really appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 FLORENCE PUGH ("A GOOD PERSON")\par \par \uc2 Oh, really? Yeah, receive it and not have a clue what to do with it.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) No, it's in the closet and every once in while I put it out in front of my daughter hoping she might leaf through it. No luck yet. But, you know, a girl can dream.\par \par \uc2 FLORENCE PUGH ("A GOOD PERSON")\par \par \uc2 No. Aww.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So precious of your parents, though. I want to get back to the movie.\par \par \uc2 FLORENCE PUGH ("A GOOD PERSON")\par \par \uc2 Yep.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) In one scene, your character cuts off all of her hair.\par \par \uc2 FLORENCE PUGH ("A GOOD PERSON")\par \par \uc2 Yes.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And this was the decision behind the scenes that you and Zach may not have seen eye to eye on?\par \par \uc2 FLORENCE PUGH ("A GOOD PERSON")\par \par \uc2 I thought it was a really important thing to do. Like, we meet our character a year after this tragic accident, and I just thought it was important for the audience to see that she is a completely changed and different woman and that she is literally chopping pieces of herself off. And it also, in some way, gets all the vanity out the window.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right.\par \par \uc2 FLORENCE PUGH ("A GOOD PERSON")\par \par \uc2 You don't look at this character in the same way that you probably would do. She is at rock bottom, and she looks wonderfully mad whilst doing so. So, I thought it was really important as a performer and also visually for the audience to just see that it's a changed being.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, I know. I mean...\par \par \uc2 FLORENCE PUGH ("A GOOD PERSON")\par \par \uc2 But Zach wasn't very happy about it because it meant that scheduling, it was a nightmare and he kept coming to me and saying, okay, so the thing, this is a great idea, but it's just going to mean that scheduling is like a nightmare and we won't be able to do it.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right, the producer is coming out.\par \par \uc2 FLORENCE PUGH ("A GOOD PERSON")\par \par \uc2 Yeah. And I would just turn to him and be like, you'll figure it out.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) He was determined.\par \par \uc2 FLORENCE PUGH ("A GOOD PERSON")\par \par \uc2 He would talk to the other producers and talk to the ADs. And they'd be like, Zach, this can't happen, you're going to have to tell her that she, that she cannot.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But in the end, he agreed that it was, it really, it's very symbolic.\par \par \uc2 FLORENCE PUGH ("A GOOD PERSON")\par \par \uc2 I said, figure it out.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah. We know who the boss is. Just before we go, congrats on "Dune 2."\par \par \uc2 FLORENCE PUGH ("A GOOD PERSON")\par \par \uc2 Thank you.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's just wrapped?\par \par \uc2 FLORENCE PUGH ("A GOOD PERSON")\par \par \uc2 Well, I wrapped ages ago. But I think, yeah, they just wrapped before Christmas.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Anything you can share with us because it has such a following?\par \par \uc2 FLORENCE PUGH ("A GOOD PERSON")\par \par \uc2 Absolutely nothing other than the fact that...\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) A girl can try. Come on.\par \par \uc2 FLORENCE PUGH ("A GOOD PERSON")\par \par \uc2 Other than the fact that I, that was as mad for me being on it as it was for people. That movie is just, I'm so proud and excited to be a part of that world so bad.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Love everything you do.\par \par \uc2 FLORENCE PUGH ("A GOOD PERSON")\par \par \uc2 Thank you.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It was so great to see you at the Oscars, you looked beautiful.\par \par \uc2 FLORENCE PUGH ("A GOOD PERSON")\par \par \uc2 Yeah, thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And looking forward to all of the rest. But first, everybody, check out a "A Good Person," and you are.\par \par \uc2 FLORENCE PUGH ("A GOOD PERSON")\par \par \uc2 Yes.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you so much for being with us, Florence.\par \par \uc2 FLORENCE PUGH ("A GOOD PERSON")\par \par \uc2 Thank you. Thank you. It's (inaudible) here.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) "A Good Person" is in theaters this Friday. Don't miss it.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230424ej3m0000p\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 "SHARK" DAYMOND JOHN LIVE IN TIMES SQUARE "SHARK TANK" STAR TALKS ABOUT NEW CHILDREN'S BOOK\b0\par\par\uc2 1,941 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 March 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RECORD BREAKING STORM\par \par \uc2 STORM, RAIN, WINDS, SNOW, HOPPIN, HIGHWAYS\par \par \uc2 STORM, RAIN, SNOW, ALERTS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, DOCUMENTS, HOWELL, INVESTIGATIONS, GRAND JURY\par \par \uc2 FED, INTEREST RATES, BANKING, INFLATION\par \par \uc2 OTIENO, VIDEO, 911, DEATH, OUKO, INDICTED\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, LAUSD, WAGES, STUDENTS, PARENTS\par \par \uc2 LOPEZ, DEAF, SUPREME COURT, MICHIGAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS; STORM MOVES EAST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 SMITH, MURDER, MURDAUGH, SLED, MOORE\par \par \uc2 PALTROW, LAWSUIT, HENDERSON, SKI, CRASH, BUHLER, OWENS\par \par \uc2 DELIVERY, SCAMMERS, SUSPECTS, BURGLARY, HOMEOWNERS\par \par \uc2 SAILBOAT, SUNK, WHALE, RODRIGUEZ, CREW, RESCUE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 INTEREST RATES, HIKE, ECONOMY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALL EYES ON INTEREST RATES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WILL FED HIKE RATES AGAIN AMID BANKING CRISIS?\par \par \uc2 BIRTH CONTROL, RISK, BREAST CANCER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAST CANCER & HORMONAL BIRTH CONTROL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOES BIRTH CONTROL INCREASE RISK OF BREAST CANCER?\par \par \uc2 REED, TRIBUTE, \uc2 KNICKS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REMEMBERING WILLIS REED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 NEW YORK KNICKS\uc2  LEGEND DIES AT 80\par \par \uc2 READING, DAVIS, KIM, "KANGAROO CRAVINGS", SPENCER\par \par \uc2 ANISTON, SANDLER, "MURDER MYSTERY 2"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 DENNIS, WING, ANIMAL RESCUE\par \par \uc2 "A GOOD PERSON", PUGH\par \par \uc2 JOHN, "LITTLE DAYMOND LEARNS TO EARN"\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We are back now with a very special guest this morning. Daymond John, the "Shark Tank" star and financial expert has written a new children's book. He's got the top hat on today. The book called "Little Daymond Learns to Earn," teaching kids all about money.\par \par \uc2 SAM CHAMPION (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Super important. But also, with so much uncertainty in the financial world, we ask you to ask him your money questions. So, we're going to do that. It's so nice to see you. I haven't seen you since the barbershop.\par \par \uc2 DAYMOND JOHN ("SHARK TANK" / AUTHOR "LITTLE DAYMOND LEARNS TO EARN")\par \par \uc2 That's right. I love you, my dear friend.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You said you like the hat, too.\par \par \uc2 SAM CHAMPION (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I'm wearing it.\par \par \uc2 DAYMOND JOHN ("SHARK TANK" / AUTHOR "LITTLE DAYMOND LEARNS TO EARN")\par \par \uc2 I wear these hats because kids don't care about my $10,000 Tom Ford suits. But when I teach them financial intelligence, they ask, am I teaching them magic? I'm going to teach them how to leave your parents' house when you're 20.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You bring the magic, exactly.\par \par \uc2 DAYMOND JOHN ("SHARK TANK" / AUTHOR "LITTLE DAYMOND LEARNS TO EARN")\par \par \uc2 And turn $1 into $3.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, we're going to get into the children's book in just a bit.\par \par \uc2 DAYMOND JOHN ("SHARK TANK" / AUTHOR "LITTLE DAYMOND LEARNS TO EARN")\par \par \uc2 Yep, absolutely.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But we're going to put you to work while you're here.\par \par \uc2 DAYMOND JOHN ("SHARK TANK" / AUTHOR "LITTLE DAYMOND LEARNS TO EARN")\par \par \uc2 That's right.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Because so many people have questions. Given the financial environment, many asking about how to approach banking overall.\par \par \uc2 DAYMOND JOHN ("SHARK TANK" / AUTHOR "LITTLE DAYMOND LEARNS TO EARN")\par \par \uc2 Yes.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And our first question here is from Will out of Greenville, South Carolina. Let's take a look.\par \par \uc2 BUSINESS OWNER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 As a small business owner and dad, would it be wise for me to spread my savings across a few different banks right now?\par \par \uc2 DAYMOND JOHN ("SHARK TANK" / AUTHOR "LITTLE DAYMOND LEARNS TO EARN")\par \par \uc2 It depends how much savings you have because you are federally protected up to $250,000. So, first of all, if you have more than that, yeah, I would consider not spreading or putting it into big banks like Chase, the one you think that are not going to have that type of turmoil. But more importantly, putting your money to work. You're only going to get 6% in the bank. You'll get way more in various other different financial, you know, products.\par \par \uc2 SAM CHAMPION (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah. I like that advice because it's like not just bank it. Does this look okay? Am I rocking it?\par \par \uc2 DAYMOND JOHN ("SHARK TANK" / AUTHOR "LITTLE DAYMOND LEARNS TO EARN")\par \par \uc2 (Inaudible).\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You're a little stiff wearing it but, you know.\par \par \uc2 SAM CHAMPION (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, because it's a little big, so I feel like it'll be on my nose at any second now.\par \par \uc2 DAYMOND JOHN ("SHARK TANK" / AUTHOR "LITTLE DAYMOND LEARNS TO EARN")\par \par \uc2 Oh, no, no, no, no. You don't look like (inaudible).\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Mad Hatter.\par \par \uc2 SAM CHAMPION (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, here's the question. Thank you. She's Chelsea on \uc2 Instagram\uc2 , "I have some extra money to invest in light of the financial crisis," and this goes back to the banking you just talked about, maybe investing some, "what would you suggest I do with my money?"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DAYMOND'S FINANCIAL ADVICE\par \par \uc2 DAYMOND JOHN ("SHARK TANK" / AUTHOR "LITTLE DAYMOND LEARNS TO EARN")\par \par \uc2 Well, always the first investment is in yourself, an education or various other things. Before you get into things that may be hot, you want to do, put all the financial kind of tips on \uc2 Instagram\uc2 , put that, follow 20 sites, don't buy anything. But the same way you scroll through and see travel and things you love, you'll start to get financial intelligence, and then you invest where you feel comfortable.\par \par \uc2 SAM CHAMPION (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We do this with everything else, right?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, exactly.\par \par \uc2 SAM CHAMPION (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I mean, you're right. We do recipes that way, we do vacations that way.\par \par \uc2 DAYMOND JOHN ("SHARK TANK" / AUTHOR "LITTLE DAYMOND LEARNS TO EARN")\par \par \uc2 Travel, working out, whatever it is.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Doing it in a way that actually benefits you in the long run.\par \par \uc2 DAYMOND JOHN ("SHARK TANK" / AUTHOR "LITTLE DAYMOND LEARNS TO EARN")\par \par \uc2 Exactly.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, this question here, this is @HannahBontheGram. I love the handle. She asked, is now a goodtime to make extra payments on my home mortgage?\par \par \uc2 DAYMOND JOHN ("SHARK TANK" / AUTHOR "LITTLE DAYMOND LEARNS TO EARN")\par \par \uc2 It always is a good time. You pay down the principal, though. If you are paying 600, $700 but you want to pay it down $800, you take about $200 and pay down on principal, not on interest. That then reduces the principal. And then, overall, it reduces your payments.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay.\par \par \uc2 SAM CHAMPION (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) How come I'm not smart, as long as I have known you, how come I'm not smarter at this? That's my next question.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You look at the hat.\par \par \uc2 DAYMOND JOHN ("SHARK TANK" / AUTHOR "LITTLE DAYMOND LEARNS TO EARN")\par \par \uc2 Well, by the way, I almost went bankrupt twice when I was broke and once when I had $10 million in the bank. So, this is something that we constantly have to constantly educate ourselves on.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Learn and grow.\par \par \uc2 SAM CHAMPION (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, don't be afraid of it.\par \par \uc2 DAYMOND JOHN ("SHARK TANK" / AUTHOR "LITTLE DAYMOND LEARNS TO EARN")\par \par \uc2 Do not be afraid of it.\par \par \uc2 SAM CHAMPION (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, one more question before I think we talk a little bit about the book. So, so many of our viewers want to know, with interest rates so high and maybe I think a lot of America has credit debt, right? So, what do you, what do you do if you have a lot of credit card debt?\par \par \uc2 DAYMOND JOHN ("SHARK TANK" / AUTHOR "LITTLE DAYMOND LEARNS TO EARN")\par \par \uc2 First of all, you go to your creditors who are around 18% and you ask them, can you renegotiate because you're going to cut the credit card off. They'll move it down to 15% or 14%. Then you try and go get a loan if you can. Now, you have to have discipline to get that into 6%. Combine all the credit cards together and you pay that and you reduce it, but you cannot go back now to putting more into debt.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 DAYMOND JOHN ("SHARK TANK" / AUTHOR "LITTLE DAYMOND LEARNS TO EARN")\par \par \uc2 And that's the entire reason for "Little Daymond Learns to Earn" because you need to understand financial intelligence because we're not taught that in this country because we're taught the way we used to work, in an industrial era. You know, learn a trade or be a good employee. And so, if we don't have financial intelligence starting at five, well, then at 17 years old, we acquired $750,000 worth of student debt that we won't pay off until we're into our 50s.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Exactly. So important. And that brings us to the book right here.\par \par \uc2 DAYMOND JOHN ("SHARK TANK" / AUTHOR "LITTLE DAYMOND LEARNS TO EARN")\par \par \uc2 Yes.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Because "Little Daymond Learns to Earn," I love it. You were telling us that this is your legacy. Not necessarily the book, but the conversation about teaching young people.\par \par \uc2 DAYMOND JOHN ("SHARK TANK" / AUTHOR "LITTLE DAYMOND LEARNS TO EARN")\par \par \uc2 By the way, we did it, the number one book in the country and it just came out yesterday. And it's we did it because this is my legacy, because it's not about a book, America has voted that we need financial intelligence for our children. And I want every celebrity, every bank, everybody else to say, I need to make products for kids five to 15. I'm tired of reading to my little daughter that someday a prince is going to show up and she needs to have a glass slipper or slay a dragon or throw hair out of a tower.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And you say this was inspired by a conversation.\par \par \uc2 DAYMOND JOHN ("SHARK TANK" / AUTHOR "LITTLE DAYMOND LEARNS TO EARN")\par \par \uc2 Exactly, my little girl. By the way, she better not live with seven dwarfs. You know, but at the end of the day, you know what, I want my daughter to be able to say, no, I'm making my own glass slippers. I want the prince to walk in and go, damn, who owns his glass slipper place, I need to meet her.\par \par \uc2 SAM CHAMPION (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Very smart.\par \par \uc2 DAYMOND JOHN ("SHARK TANK" / AUTHOR "LITTLE DAYMOND LEARNS TO EARN")\par \par \uc2 And that's what this is about, teaching kids five to 10 years old and families about financial intelligence in a soluble way where they can read it every month to their child.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I love it. Your daughter is seven, my daughters, eight and 10. So, I will be bringing this home. Daymond, thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 DAYMOND JOHN ("SHARK TANK" / AUTHOR "LITTLE DAYMOND LEARNS TO EARN")\par \par \uc2 Thank you.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Congratulations on everything, my friend.\par \par \uc2 DAYMOND JOHN ("SHARK TANK" / AUTHOR "LITTLE DAYMOND LEARNS TO EARN")\par \par \uc2 Sam, I love you, man.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) "Little Daymond Learns to Earn" available right now. And you can see Daymond on "Shark Tank" Friday at 8:00 PM Eastern right here on ABC. We'll be right back. Oh, out of the hat. All the magic.\par \par \uc2 SAM CHAMPION (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You want to try the hat?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Sure.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) "Good Morning America" is sponsored by...\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I'm working on that drop shot. Everybody, thank you for watching. Have a great day.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230424ej3m0000r\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WEATHER\b0\par\par\uc2 382 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 March 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RECORD BREAKING STORM\par \par \uc2 STORM, RAIN, WINDS, SNOW, HOPPIN, HIGHWAYS\par \par \uc2 STORM, RAIN, SNOW, ALERTS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, DOCUMENTS, HOWELL, INVESTIGATIONS, GRAND JURY\par \par \uc2 FED, INTEREST RATES, BANKING, INFLATION\par \par \uc2 OTIENO, VIDEO, 911, DEATH, OUKO, INDICTED\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, LAUSD, WAGES, STUDENTS, PARENTS\par \par \uc2 LOPEZ, DEAF, SUPREME COURT, MICHIGAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS; STORM MOVES EAST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 SMITH, MURDER, MURDAUGH, SLED, MOORE\par \par \uc2 PALTROW, LAWSUIT, HENDERSON, SKI, CRASH, BUHLER, OWENS\par \par \uc2 DELIVERY, SCAMMERS, SUSPECTS, BURGLARY, HOMEOWNERS\par \par \uc2 SAILBOAT, SUNK, WHALE, RODRIGUEZ, CREW, RESCUE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 INTEREST RATES, HIKE, ECONOMY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALL EYES ON INTEREST RATES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WILL FED HIKE RATES AGAIN AMID BANKING CRISIS?\par \par \uc2 BIRTH CONTROL, RISK, BREAST CANCER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAST CANCER & HORMONAL BIRTH CONTROL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOES BIRTH CONTROL INCREASE RISK OF BREAST CANCER?\par \par \uc2 REED, TRIBUTE, \uc2 KNICKS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REMEMBERING WILLIS REED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 NEW YORK KNICKS\uc2  LEGEND DIES AT 80\par \par \uc2 READING, DAVIS, KIM, "KANGAROO CRAVINGS", SPENCER\par \par \uc2 ANISTON, SANDLER, "MURDER MYSTERY 2"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 DENNIS, WING, ANIMAL RESCUE\par \par \uc2 "A GOOD PERSON", PUGH\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Sam?\par \par \uc2 SAM CHAMPION (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Lara. So, we've been showing you storm after storm on the West Coast. And there's some side effects of this that are great to look at like we've shown the greening in the desert. But also, the super bloom going on right now. Okay, ranunculus, I practiced so hard. But there's a field of them and I have no idea what to tell you if its plural. Are they ranunculuses? All right, also, looking at Arizona as we've got more storms developing in the West Coast and moving across the country.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STORMY PATTERN CONTINUES\par \par \uc2 SAM CHAMPION (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, we've got one coming this weekend high. This one runs in the Pacific Northwest. And then again, on Monday, another one of these powerful kind of atmospheric river lows loads up on California. So, we've got more rain and snow to come for the first of that week. That's the weather around the nation, here's what you can expect this morning.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NATIONAL MAP\par \par \uc2 SAM CHAMPION (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...like this. Coming up, "Shark Tank's Daymond John answers your questions about money. He's here live. I love the hat. I love, love the hat.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230424ej3m0000q\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 CELEBRATING THE NEXT GENERATION OF YOUNG WOMEN 11-YEAR-OLD WANTS TO INSPIRE KIDS TO HELP ANIMALS\b0\par\par\uc2 1,361 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 March 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RECORD BREAKING STORM\par \par \uc2 STORM, RAIN, WINDS, SNOW, HOPPIN, HIGHWAYS\par \par \uc2 STORM, RAIN, SNOW, ALERTS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, DOCUMENTS, HOWELL, INVESTIGATIONS, GRAND JURY\par \par \uc2 FED, INTEREST RATES, BANKING, INFLATION\par \par \uc2 OTIENO, VIDEO, 911, DEATH, OUKO, INDICTED\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, LAUSD, WAGES, STUDENTS, PARENTS\par \par \uc2 LOPEZ, DEAF, SUPREME COURT, MICHIGAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS; STORM MOVES EAST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 SMITH, MURDER, MURDAUGH, SLED, MOORE\par \par \uc2 PALTROW, LAWSUIT, HENDERSON, SKI, CRASH, BUHLER, OWENS\par \par \uc2 DELIVERY, SCAMMERS, SUSPECTS, BURGLARY, HOMEOWNERS\par \par \uc2 SAILBOAT, SUNK, WHALE, RODRIGUEZ, CREW, RESCUE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 INTEREST RATES, HIKE, ECONOMY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALL EYES ON INTEREST RATES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WILL FED HIKE RATES AGAIN AMID BANKING CRISIS?\par \par \uc2 BIRTH CONTROL, RISK, BREAST CANCER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAST CANCER & HORMONAL BIRTH CONTROL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOES BIRTH CONTROL INCREASE RISK OF BREAST CANCER?\par \par \uc2 REED, TRIBUTE, \uc2 KNICKS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REMEMBERING WILLIS REED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 NEW YORK KNICKS\uc2  LEGEND DIES AT 80\par \par \uc2 READING, DAVIS, KIM, "KANGAROO CRAVINGS", SPENCER\par \par \uc2 ANISTON, SANDLER, "MURDER MYSTERY 2"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 DENNIS, WING, ANIMAL RESCUE\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But we are playing that because it is Women's History Month. And we are celebrating the next generation of young women who are sparking change. This morning, we're introducing you to an 11-year-old Delanie Dennis from Tampa, Florida, who raises money for animal rescues and was named Kid of the Year by the \uc2 ASPCA\uc2 . Take a look\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CELEBRATING THE NEXT GENERATION OF YOUNG WOMEN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 11-YEAR-OLD WANTS TO INSPIRE KIDS TO HELP ANIMALS\par \par \uc2 DELANIE DENNIS (FOUNDER DELANIE'S LEMONADE STAND)\par \par \uc2 When life gives you lemons, start a lemonade stand.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And that's what 11-year-old Delanie Dennis has been doing for as long as she can remember.\par \par \uc2 JULIE DENNIS (DELANIE'S MOM)\par \par \uc2 What are you making?\par \par \uc2 DELANIE DENNIS (FOUNDER DELANIE'S LEMONADE STAND)\par \par \uc2 Lemonade.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Her love for lemonade as big as her love for animals.\par \par \uc2 DELANIE DENNIS (FOUNDER DELANIE'S LEMONADE STAND)\par \par \uc2 This is Boots and he is happy to be here. I believe that, somewhere out there, animals have a forever home. If you buy a lemonade, you can help the animals.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) At just seven years old, looking for a way to help animals, Delanie came up with the idea to sell lemonade.\par \par \uc2 ANDY DENNIS (DELANIE'S DAD)\par \par \uc2 So, we talked to her about it and listened to her plan and was like, okay, let's give it a shot.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Rallying around Delanie's dream, they opened Delanie's Lemonade Stand in their Tampa Bay family restaurant, donating each month's proceeds to an animal rescue of their daughter's choice.\par \par \uc2 DELANIE DENNIS (FOUNDER DELANIE'S LEMONADE STAND)\par \par \uc2 Since I started the lemonade stand, we've raised over $61,000 for animal rescues and charities.\par \par \uc2 JULIE DENNIS (DELANIE'S MOM)\par \par \uc2 It's been truly inspiring to see someone at such a young age with such a passion for people and animals to make things happen and make a change. It's heartwarming.\par \par \uc2 DELANIE DENNIS (FOUNDER DELANIE'S LEMONADE STAND)\par \par \uc2 Here's your change.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And it's heartwarming for the community, too.\par \par \uc2 ANDREA WING (CAF\u201\'00\'C9 DELANIE EMPLOYEE)\par \par \uc2 I come in every day and I'm here for Delanie. I'm here for her mission. It gets me emotional because I want to do the best I can. So, it means a lot for me. You're doing a great job.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Her hard work being recognized, earning her the \uc2 ASPCA\uc2  2022 Kid of the Year.\par \par \uc2 DELANIE DENNIS (FOUNDER DELANIE'S LEMONADE STAND)\par \par \uc2 I especially want all the kids out there to know that I think kids at any age can change the world.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And when she's not busy raising funds, she's volunteering at her favorite animal rescue, home to her pet donkey.\par \par \uc2 DELANIE DENNIS (FOUNDER DELANIE'S LEMONADE STAND)\par \par \uc2 This is Pareto. I love giving them ear kisses. I want to inspire my generation to help animals. The future is that hopefully animals' lives will all be changed. Okay, Boots, let's go for a walk.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MEET DELANIE DENNIS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 11-YEAR-OLD WITH A LEMONADE STAND HELPING TO SAVE ANIMALS\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And let's welcome Delanie Dennis to our studio here in Times Square. Welcome to "GMA," Delanie. And we know that you raise money and you volunteer and, but you also help to make sure that the animals get adopted. What's the name of your adoption fair?\par \par \uc2 DELANIE DENNIS (FOUNDER DELANIE'S LEMONADE STAND)\par \par \uc2 The name of my fair is Squeeze the Day.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Squeeze the Day. So, what exactly does Squeeze the Day do? What happens there?\par \par \uc2 DELANIE DENNIS (FOUNDER DELANIE'S LEMONADE STAND)\par \par \uc2 Squeeze the Day is an adoption fair that I host every year where there's a bunch of rescues that come, and they can share the word about their rescue, get donations spelled out, and adopt out animals most of all.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Boy, you are making, you're 11 years old, are you sure? You know, Squeeze the Day, we're going to let you squeeze the day right here on "GMA" because we have some kittens here. We also have a dog here named Hollywood. Come on out, Hollywood. And you are the \uc2 ASPCA\uc2 's Kid of the Year last year, so we're going to let you squeeze the day with these animals, who here all from the \uc2 ASPCA\uc2  in New York City, they are looking at homes, looking for homes, tell us about that.\par \par \uc2 DELANIE DENNIS (FOUNDER DELANIE'S LEMONADE STAND)\par \par \uc2 So, first up, we have Hollywood. He is a 14-year-old terrier mix and he is looking for a home.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Looking for a home. Yes. Lara might be in the market because she loves her animals.\par \par \uc2 DELANIE DENNIS (FOUNDER DELANIE'S LEMONADE STAND)\par \par \uc2 He may be, he may be 14 years old but, you see, he acts like a puppy. And if you wouldn't have heard he's 14, you wouldn't be able to tell.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That is very true. A lot of energy there from Hollywood.\par \par \uc2 DELANIE DENNIS (FOUNDER DELANIE'S LEMONADE STAND)\par \par \uc2 Yeah.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And what about the kittens?\par \par \uc2 DELANIE DENNIS (FOUNDER DELANIE'S LEMONADE STAND)\par \par \uc2 And we have the two kittens. And they are, and they are also sisters from the same litter. They are very fluffy and they are looking for a good home.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Looking for a good home. And I'm glad you came here to help them try to find a good home. And we know you had a record-setting month raising money for animal rescues.\par \par \uc2 DELANIE DENNIS (FOUNDER DELANIE'S LEMONADE STAND)\par \par \uc2 Yes, I did.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You did, which is great. But a veterinarian emergency group, they want to help out. They want to add a little bit to that record-setting month for you, so we've got a little something for you. They want to give you $2,500 to Delanie's Lemonade Stand right there. They want to give you an extra $2,500 to help you out. So, what do you think you're going to do with this money?\par \par \uc2 DELANIE DENNIS (FOUNDER DELANIE'S LEMONADE STAND)\par \par \uc2 Well, help out, help out this month's massive rescue.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You know what, Delanie, you are amazing. Keep on doing the great work you're doing. We appreciate it, the animals appreciate it, and you definitely are the kid of the year for the \uc2 ASPCA\uc2 . You deserve it. Give me that. There we go. Everybody, these animals are up for adoption. So, you can take them home. Lara, I've got you covered. Coming up, Delanie, thank you so much for being here. Coming up, Florence Pugh is here live. There she is.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230424ej3m0000o\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 INTRODUCTION TO THE 08:30 HALF-HOUR\b0\par\par\uc2 213 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 March 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RECORD BREAKING STORM\par \par \uc2 STORM, RAIN, WINDS, SNOW, HOPPIN, HIGHWAYS\par \par \uc2 STORM, RAIN, SNOW, ALERTS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, DOCUMENTS, HOWELL, INVESTIGATIONS, GRAND JURY\par \par \uc2 FED, INTEREST RATES, BANKING, INFLATION\par \par \uc2 OTIENO, VIDEO, 911, DEATH, OUKO, INDICTED\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, LAUSD, WAGES, STUDENTS, PARENTS\par \par \uc2 LOPEZ, DEAF, SUPREME COURT, MICHIGAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS; STORM MOVES EAST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 SMITH, MURDER, MURDAUGH, SLED, MOORE\par \par \uc2 PALTROW, LAWSUIT, HENDERSON, SKI, CRASH, BUHLER, OWENS\par \par \uc2 DELIVERY, SCAMMERS, SUSPECTS, BURGLARY, HOMEOWNERS\par \par \uc2 SAILBOAT, SUNK, WHALE, RODRIGUEZ, CREW, RESCUE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 INTEREST RATES, HIKE, ECONOMY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALL EYES ON INTEREST RATES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WILL FED HIKE RATES AGAIN AMID BANKING CRISIS?\par \par \uc2 BIRTH CONTROL, RISK, BREAST CANCER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAST CANCER & HORMONAL BIRTH CONTROL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOES BIRTH CONTROL INCREASE RISK OF BREAST CANCER?\par \par \uc2 REED, TRIBUTE, \uc2 KNICKS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REMEMBERING WILLIS REED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 NEW YORK KNICKS\uc2  LEGEND DIES AT 80\par \par \uc2 READING, DAVIS, KIM, "KANGAROO CRAVINGS", SPENCER\par \par \uc2 ANISTON, SANDLER, "MURDER MYSTERY 2"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 Welcome back to "GMA" live from Times Square.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 The song got Sam Champion and Lara got, everybody here dancing a little bit. Let me hear you roar, Sam.\par \par \uc2 SAM CHAMPION (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 No, no.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Okay.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Got to draw the line somewhere.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230424ej3m0000n\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 THE GREAT READING CRISIS GROWING NUMBER OF KIDS FALLING BEHIND READING\b0\par\par\uc2 1,064 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 March 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RECORD BREAKING STORM\par \par \uc2 STORM, RAIN, WINDS, SNOW, HOPPIN, HIGHWAYS\par \par \uc2 STORM, RAIN, SNOW, ALERTS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, DOCUMENTS, HOWELL, INVESTIGATIONS, GRAND JURY\par \par \uc2 FED, INTEREST RATES, BANKING, INFLATION\par \par \uc2 OTIENO, VIDEO, 911, DEATH, OUKO, INDICTED\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, LAUSD, WAGES, STUDENTS, PARENTS\par \par \uc2 LOPEZ, DEAF, SUPREME COURT, MICHIGAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS; STORM MOVES EAST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 SMITH, MURDER, MURDAUGH, SLED, MOORE\par \par \uc2 PALTROW, LAWSUIT, HENDERSON, SKI, CRASH, BUHLER, OWENS\par \par \uc2 DELIVERY, SCAMMERS, SUSPECTS, BURGLARY, HOMEOWNERS\par \par \uc2 SAILBOAT, SUNK, WHALE, RODRIGUEZ, CREW, RESCUE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 INTEREST RATES, HIKE, ECONOMY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALL EYES ON INTEREST RATES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WILL FED HIKE RATES AGAIN AMID BANKING CRISIS?\par \par \uc2 BIRTH CONTROL, RISK, BREAST CANCER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAST CANCER & HORMONAL BIRTH CONTROL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOES BIRTH CONTROL INCREASE RISK OF BREAST CANCER?\par \par \uc2 REED, TRIBUTE, \uc2 KNICKS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REMEMBERING WILLIS REED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 NEW YORK KNICKS\uc2  LEGEND DIES AT 80\par \par \uc2 READING, DAVIS, KIM, "KANGAROO CRAVINGS", SPENCER\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) (Inaudible) kind of day.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You don't want to know it, that's all I'm going to say. We are back now with our "GMA Cover Story."\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA COVER STORY\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) March is National Reading Month and there's a growing number of children falling behind in their reading skills.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE GREAT READING CRISIS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GROWING NUMBER OF KIDS FALLING BEHIND READING\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It's a problem that is made worse by the pandemic, but there's a new tool that is helping. Becky Worley is back with that. Good morning again, Becky.\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Michael, good morning again to you. When your child is learning to read, you sort of hold your breath and hope everything works out. But during the pandemic, reading took a hit or millions of kids. And for one mom who is sitting next to her son as he struggled through it, she realized he needed a different way to learn.\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This is a new way to teach reading filled with action, laughter, and fun. But rewind to 2020 when Jacquelyn Davis' son Maden was learning to read, he was not having fun.\par \par \uc2 JACQUELYN DAVIS (CREATOR "KANGAROO CRAVINGS")\par \par \uc2 He would cry. He would hide in a laundry basket, anything to not have to do reading. Ooh, I got three.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MOON ON A MISSION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CREATED NEW GAME TO IMPROVE HER SON'S READING SKILLS\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) So, Jacquelyn, who has a background in education, became a mom on a mission. Armed with art supplies and her creativity, she made a game called Kangaroo Cravings so that 7-year-old Maden could develop his reading skills, focusing on sight words.\par \par \uc2 JACQUELYN DAVIS (CREATOR "KANGAROO CRAVINGS")\par \par \uc2 There are about 300 sight words that children need to learn between kindergarten and second grade. There are words that are really high frequency. And so, children just need to learn them so that they have them in their long-term memory.\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) What was one of the most difficult words you've learned?\par \par \uc2 SON (MALE)\par \par \uc2 There is a lot of words that like they don't follow the rules, it's weird. Like one even, O-N-E, easiest word to spell, right? W-U-N.\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, describe the mechanics of the game.\par \par \uc2 JACQUELYN DAVIS (CREATOR "KANGAROO CRAVINGS")\par \par \uc2 There are actions like spell the word, each letter with your tail like a kangaroo. We know from the science that using the words and moving your body with the letters actually helps you learn them better.\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I get that card and I'd go, me.\par \par \uc2 JACQUELYN DAVIS (CREATOR "KANGAROO CRAVINGS")\par \par \uc2 So, you would go, M-E, with your nose. And then you say the word again for the repetition. M-E.\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Even before the pandemic, the nation's report card says that two out of every three children don't read at grade level, and it's only gotten worse. Just reported the largest drop in children's reading scores in more than 20 years, turning Jacquelyn from mom on a mission to mom-preneur. Kangaroo Cravings was play tested by more than 100 children across 40 classrooms in the US.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW WAY TO TEACH READING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHANGING THE GAME FOR LEARNING SIGHT WORDS\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Like this one at the British International School and some Washington, DC, public schools, which reported encouraging results.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA KIM (FORMER DEPUTY CHANCELLOR DSC PUBLIC SCHOOL SYSTEM)\par \par \uc2 We saw something that kids have fun doing and they were learning and teachers are seeing impacts of that as they tested out the game.\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Candace Spencer is one of the public school teachers who tested the game in her classroom.\par \par \uc2 CANDACE SPENCER (PUBLIC SCHOOL TEACHER)\par \par \uc2 Without the game, sight words are usually just like scale and jelly, use flash cards, you memorize them. It's not nearly as fun as a board game.\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Learning is social sometimes. Do you notice the movement helped?\par \par \uc2 CANDACE SPENCER (PUBLIC SCHOOL TEACHER)\par \par \uc2 100%\par \par \uc2 ALEX MORGAN (CHILD)\par \par \uc2 For her journey to the finish line was a long one.\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Mom of 9-year-old Alex Morgan telling us, she saw the difference.\par \par \uc2 KEVONNE SMALL (MOTHER OF ALEX MORGAN)\par \par \uc2 That was one of the pieces that I really liked about it, understanding how people memorized. He memorized also with action.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA KIM (FORMER DEPUTY CHANCELLOR DSC PUBLIC SCHOOL SYSTEM)\par \par \uc2 I'm really excited that DC public schools will be purchasing the game for every one of our schools.\par \par \uc2 SON (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Playing it made me actually start to kind of want to read and I'm on grade level.\par \par \uc2 BECKY WORLEY (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Amazing, that's a high five. Right here. Good job. Now, Kangaroo Cravings will be out this summer to help with the dreaded summer slide learning loss. And while this is just one game and one new way to learn, it really shows that innovation and differentiated learning can make a huge difference to help kids master this critical skill, Michael.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It really can. Thank you for bringing that to us. We appreciate that, Becky.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230424ej3m0000k\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WEATHER\b0\par\par\uc2 374 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 March 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RECORD BREAKING STORM\par \par \uc2 STORM, RAIN, WINDS, SNOW, HOPPIN, HIGHWAYS\par \par \uc2 STORM, RAIN, SNOW, ALERTS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, DOCUMENTS, HOWELL, INVESTIGATIONS, GRAND JURY\par \par \uc2 FED, INTEREST RATES, BANKING, INFLATION\par \par \uc2 OTIENO, VIDEO, 911, DEATH, OUKO, INDICTED\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, LAUSD, WAGES, STUDENTS, PARENTS\par \par \uc2 LOPEZ, DEAF, SUPREME COURT, MICHIGAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS; STORM MOVES EAST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 SMITH, MURDER, MURDAUGH, SLED, MOORE\par \par \uc2 PALTROW, LAWSUIT, HENDERSON, SKI, CRASH, BUHLER, OWENS\par \par \uc2 DELIVERY, SCAMMERS, SUSPECTS, BURGLARY, HOMEOWNERS\par \par \uc2 SAILBOAT, SUNK, WHALE, RODRIGUEZ, CREW, RESCUE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 INTEREST RATES, HIKE, ECONOMY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALL EYES ON INTEREST RATES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WILL FED HIKE RATES AGAIN AMID BANKING CRISIS?\par \par \uc2 BIRTH CONTROL, RISK, BREAST CANCER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAST CANCER & HORMONAL BIRTH CONTROL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOES BIRTH CONTROL INCREASE RISK OF BREAST CANCER?\par \par \uc2 REED, TRIBUTE, \uc2 KNICKS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REMEMBERING WILLIS REED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 NEW YORK KNICKS\uc2  LEGEND DIES AT 80\par \par \uc2 READING, DAVIS, KIM, "KANGAROO CRAVINGS", SPENCER\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Sam?\par \par \uc2 SAM CHAMPION (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, let's bounce back to the west. I'm going to show you the snowy edge of this storm, from the snow in the Grapevine to a lot of places reporting, as you know already, the record snow season.\par \par \uc2 SAM CHAMPION (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) So, including Steamboat, which says now they're going to extend their season. But I want to show you something hugely important.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STORM ALERTS\par \par \uc2 SAM CHAMPION (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) We'll watch this storm move in. And then the warning includes this right here, these avalanche warnings that are, for the first time I've ever seen it, a five out of a five, which basically means we've been stacking this snow, and we've allowed these little shelves to develop between that snowfall.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SNOW FORECAST\par \par \uc2 SAM CHAMPION (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, it will be very easy to get a huge snow slide out of this. And look at the amount of snow that's coming locally, up to three to four feet back to Steamboat and also to Telluride. Do not backcountry ski. Just don't do it. That's the weather around the nation, here's what you can expect this morning. Here's the best local weather in the business from our ABC station.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NATIONAL MAP\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230424ej3m0000l\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 BREAST CANCER & HORMONAL BIRTH CONTROL DOES BIRTH CONTROL INCREASE RISK OF BREAST CANCER?\b0\par\par\uc2 692 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 March 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RECORD BREAKING STORM\par \par \uc2 STORM, RAIN, WINDS, SNOW, HOPPIN, HIGHWAYS\par \par \uc2 STORM, RAIN, SNOW, ALERTS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, DOCUMENTS, HOWELL, INVESTIGATIONS, GRAND JURY\par \par \uc2 FED, INTEREST RATES, BANKING, INFLATION\par \par \uc2 OTIENO, VIDEO, 911, DEATH, OUKO, INDICTED\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, LAUSD, WAGES, STUDENTS, PARENTS\par \par \uc2 LOPEZ, DEAF, SUPREME COURT, MICHIGAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS; STORM MOVES EAST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 SMITH, MURDER, MURDAUGH, SLED, MOORE\par \par \uc2 PALTROW, LAWSUIT, HENDERSON, SKI, CRASH, BUHLER, OWENS\par \par \uc2 DELIVERY, SCAMMERS, SUSPECTS, BURGLARY, HOMEOWNERS\par \par \uc2 SAILBOAT, SUNK, WHALE, RODRIGUEZ, CREW, RESCUE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 INTEREST RATES, HIKE, ECONOMY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALL EYES ON INTEREST RATES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WILL FED HIKE RATES AGAIN AMID BANKING CRISIS?\par \par \uc2 BIRTH CONTROL, RISK, BREAST CANCER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAST CANCER & HORMONAL BIRTH CONTROL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOES BIRTH CONTROL INCREASE RISK OF BREAST CANCER?\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now a new study that found that most forms of hormonal birth control, regardless of their formulation, seemed to have the same small rise in breast cancer risk. Our chief medical correspondent Dr. Jen Ashton is going to explain this. So, just breakdown the study.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR JENNIFER ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, Robin, you said it perfectly. We've known for a while that estrogen and progesterone, birth control pills, oral contraceptives have a slightly increased risk of breast cancer.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR JENNIFER ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) What we didn't know is the newer forms, progestin only pills, IUDs, injectable implants, what their associated risk if any was in comparison. So, this study found, when you look at all hormonal types of birth control, they really have a similar slight increase in the risk of breast cancer.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HORMONAL BIRTH CONTROL AND BREAST CANCER RISK STUDY\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR JENNIFER ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And that includes even the IUDs that only contain progestin. So, again, kind of an update on the modern forms of birth control.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, you keep using the word slight, but how significance of an increase are we talking about here?\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR JENNIFER ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, Robin, what's so important here is the difference between relative risk and absolute risk. People will hear this headline and hear, excuse me, 20% to 30% increased risk. What does that mean? If you look at these numbers, you have to look at that in terms of for you.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABSOLUTE RISK OF BREAST CANCER WITH HORMONAL CONTRACEPTION\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR JENNIFER ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And so, that risk depending on age group, if you're 16-20, you have a one and 12,500 risk of breast cancer. For older women, 35-39, they have 33 in 12,500 risk of breast cancer. So, it's a slight risk. The headline will be misleading.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You want to take a sip before I actually ask you about this next question?\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR JENNIFER ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you, I'm okay.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, because I want to make sure because I know you want to get this information out here.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR JENNIFER ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, what is your advice for women?\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR JENNIFER ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, listen, I talk to women about this every single day, you have to talk about risk versus benefit. It is clear that hormonal contraception lowers the risk of ovarian and uterine cancer, but it increases the risk of clotting. When you put that head-to-head, it's about individualizing that risk-benefit and the option risk for the woman.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR JENNIFER ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) If you talk to any OBGYN, they will say that we have a line, pregnancy is much higher risk than any associated risk with birth control pills or hormonal contraception. So, you have to have that conversation based on you and your health care provider.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And we're hearing it from an OBGYN.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR JENNIFER ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, okay. Thank you, Jen, as always.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR JENNIFER ASHTON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You bet.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020230424ej3m0000i\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 LIVE IN TIMES SQUARE JENNIFER ANISTON & ADAM SANDLER\b0\par\par\uc2 2,685 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 March 2023\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2023, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RECORD BREAKING STORM\par \par \uc2 STORM, RAIN, WINDS, SNOW, HOPPIN, HIGHWAYS\par \par \uc2 STORM, RAIN, SNOW, ALERTS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, DOCUMENTS, HOWELL, INVESTIGATIONS, GRAND JURY\par \par \uc2 FED, INTEREST RATES, BANKING, INFLATION\par \par \uc2 OTIENO, VIDEO, 911, DEATH, OUKO, INDICTED\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, LAUSD, WAGES, STUDENTS, PARENTS\par \par \uc2 LOPEZ, DEAF, SUPREME COURT, MICHIGAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS; STORM MOVES EAST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 SMITH, MURDER, MURDAUGH, SLED, MOORE\par \par \uc2 PALTROW, LAWSUIT, HENDERSON, SKI, CRASH, BUHLER, OWENS\par \par \uc2 DELIVERY, SCAMMERS, SUSPECTS, BURGLARY, HOMEOWNERS\par \par \uc2 SAILBOAT, SUNK, WHALE, RODRIGUEZ, CREW, RESCUE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM\par \par \uc2 INTEREST RATES, HIKE, ECONOM